le="left:18.1%;top:92.4%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-documents-and-your-account" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Documents and your account</h2><p class="gd-p">The menu has four links: <b class="gd-ui">Trips</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Rewards</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Account</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>: your agreements, receipts, statements and uploads. Press <b class="gd-ui">View</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Download</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>: your contact details (<b class="gd-ui">Save</b>), sign-in, drivers and your Card on File.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Notifications</b>: notices from us. Use <b class="gd-ui">Mark as read</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Mark all as read</b>, and choose which optional emails you get. A number on <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> in the menu is how many notices you have not read.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/account/documents</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/renter-15-documents-desktop-fd428a63.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:91.8%;top:35.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Your legal name is locked once you are verified. To change it, call or message us. To change your email, open Profile, Sign-in and press <b class="gd-ui">Change my email</b>: we send a link to the new address and tell the old one, and the email changes when the link is opened.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-sign-in-with-your-phone-number" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sign in with your phone number</h2><p class="gd-p">No password needed: we text you a 6-digit code from the CarmaCars number.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/sign-in</span>, press <b class="gd-ui">Use my phone number instead</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Enter your mobile number and press <b class="gd-ui">Text me a code</b>. Codes go to Canadian mobile numbers.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Type the 6-digit code from the text (on most phones it fills itself in), or press <b class="gd-ui">Sign in</b>. The code works for 5 minutes; <b class="gd-ui">Send a new code</b> after a minute if it did not arrive.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">To sign in by phone every time, open <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Add and verify my phone number</b>, enter the code we text you, then choose <b class="gd-ui">My phone number (a code by text)</b> under Sign in with. The sign-in page then opens on your phone number.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>New here? On Create account, press Sign up with my phone number instead: your name, your mobile number and the code. An account made by phone has no email yet: you can send requests, accept offers and sign, and the pay page asks for your email before your first payment, for the receipts. A booking request you sent earlier with the same mobile number is added to your account once the code is checked.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-texts-or-email-how-we-reach-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Texts or email: how we reach you</h2><p class="gd-p">Choose Email, Text or Both. Texts are short, come from the CarmaCars number and link to the page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>. Under <b class="gd-ui">Messages</b>, choose <b class="gd-ui">Email</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Both</b>. It is saved at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Texts go to the phone you verified with a code (Sign-in, above). Until you verify one, we email you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Signed agreements, statements and receipts are always emailed when we have your email. On Text you also get a text with a link to view or download them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">No texts from 9 pm to 8 am, except urgent ones such as a late return. Reply STOP to any text to stop texts (we confirm with one text); text START to turn them back on.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>You can also choose in the booking request (How should we reach you?) and when you sign up with your phone number, where Text is chosen for you.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-rewards" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rewards</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Rewards</b> in your account.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every rental earns 1 point per dollar of the rental charge when it closes. 100 points are worth $1 off the rental charge of a later booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">More ways to earn are listed on the page: refer a friend with your link (you both get points at their first rental), follow us, review your rental on carmacars.ca, review us on Google (press <b class="gd-ui">I posted my review</b> and give the name on it), a damage-free rental, your birthday and your first rental.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Get my code</b> turns points into a code of your own, from 500 points. Type it in the promo code box of your request. An unused code can be given back for the points.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Your tier comes from the points you earned in the last 12 months (using points never lowers it): <b class="gd-ui">Gold</b> from 1,000 points gives Instant Book (your request is booked at once), <b class="gd-ui">Platinum</b> from 15,000 gives <b class="gd-ui">Any car, any time</b> (request a car even on dates it shows as taken; we answer within 4 hours), <b class="gd-ui">Black</b> from 60,000 gives one free rental day a year as a code. Each tier keeps the perks below it. The bar shows how many points to the next tier.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Your discounts</b> lists every code you hold (from points, your tier, referrals, our team, the free day): what it gives, when it ends, and whether it is unused, on a request or used, with <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b>. When you send a request, tap the code under <b class="gd-ui">Use a saved discount</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Points end 12 months after your last rental or redemption. We email you a month before.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-your-trip-in-your-calendar-or-wallet" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your trip in your calendar or wallet</h2><p class="gd-p">On a confirmed booking, <b class="gd-ui">Add to calendar</b> adds the pickup and the return. The confirmation email has the same link. <b class="gd-ui">Add to Apple Wallet</b> shows when it is available.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-phone-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">Get an alert on your phone or computer when your offer is ready, before pickup and return, for payments and when we message you, even with CarmaCars closed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>. Under <b class="gd-ui">Phone alerts</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Turn on alerts</b> and allow notifications when your browser asks.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Under <b class="gd-ui">What to alert me about</b>, untick anything you do not want. Your choice applies to all your devices.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Send a test alert</b> to see one. <b class="gd-ui">Turn off on this device</b> stops them there; <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes another device off.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">On iPhone and iPad, add CarmaCars to your Home Screen first: in Safari tap <b class="gd-ui">Share</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Add to Home Screen</b>. Open CarmaCars from your Home Screen, sign in and turn alerts on in Profile (iOS 16.4 or later).</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Alerts come as well as your emails and texts, never instead of them. Alerts that are not urgent wait until 8 am. Sign-in links and codes never come as alerts.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-delete-my-account" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Delete my account</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b> and scroll to <b class="gd-ui">Delete my account</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Delete my account</b>, add a reason if you like, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, delete my account</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">We settle anything still open (a rental, a deposit), delete your account and email you within 30 days. Changed your mind before then? Press <b class="gd-ui">Keep my account</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>We keep rental agreements, receipts and tax records as the law requires. Everything else, including your licence and selfie photos, is deleted.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-odometer-and-fuel-at-pickup-and-return" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Odometer and fuel at pickup and return</h2><p class="gd-p">When you check the car in or out yourself:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Add a photo of the dashboard (the odometer and the fuel gauge). It can come from your camera roll. We read it and ask, for example, &quot;Odometer 45,210 km, fuel 3/4: correct?&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Yes, correct</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">No, I will type it</b> and type the odometer and pick the fuel level.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Take a selfie in front of the car with your camera.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">After the return, <b class="gd-ui">Your return: km and fuel</b> on your booking shows the km driven, the km included and any km over, the fuel compared with pickup, and the charge for each. The photo report shows both dashboard photos.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-earn-reward-points" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Earn reward points</h2><p class="gd-p">Review your rental (add a photo for extra points), review us on Google, follow us from your Rewards page, refer a friend, and every rental after your first earns points too. See them all on <b class="gd-ui">Rewards</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-rewards-and-fuel-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rewards and fuel (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Earn points for a photo with your review and for every rental after your first; every way to earn is on your Rewards page.</li><li>A fuel shortfall at the return is priced from the car&#39;s tank and the local pump price, plus a refuelling fee, and checked by our team before any charge.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'requests-offers-and-bookings', 'chapter', 'people-and-access', 'A booking starts as a request from the website, or as an offer you send yourself to a customer on the phone. You check it, adjust it and send the offer; an offer that is out is changed in place. After that, the booking page holds the money, documents, changes and history.

## Bookings now: what is out, coming back and owed

Open **Bookings**. It opens on **Now**, one screen that refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. Every time is Toronto time.

1. The numbers at the top: cars out now, due back today, overdue, going out in the next 72 hours, payments due in the next 7 days (with the total) and free cars. Tap one to jump to its list.
2. **Out now**: every car on rent, overdue returns first in red. Each shows the car (photo, code, plate), the renter with **Call** and **Text**, when it was picked up, when it is due back with a countdown, the payment plan and the next payment, the deposit held, and the km and fuel at pickup. Filter by Overdue, Due today or Payment due.
3. A confirmed booking whose pickup time has passed with no check-in recorded is listed as out, with **Out (pickup not recorded)**. The car most likely left. Press **Mark picked up**: it records the pickup at the booked time (change it if the car left at another time), the booking goes on rent, and Fleet gets a task to add the photos, km and fuel. The usual checks stay: the deposit taken (or an Admin waives it with the reason), the renter''s signature (or an Admin''s reason), the agreement''s details, every driver verified and the coverage confirmed. If one is missing, the reason is shown.
4. **Coming back**: overdue, today and tomorrow, by the time each is due.
5. **Going out**: confirmed pickups in the next 72 hours, delivery or pickup, with ticks and crosses for the licence, the signed agreement, the payment, the deposit (a clock until the morning of the pickup day, when the hold is placed on the card on file) and the check-in photos (done at the handover).
6. **Money due**: every rental payment due in the next 7 days or overdue, the amount, the plan and which payment it is (for example 3 of 4).
7. **Free now**: cars available and not out, the longest idle first, with the next pickup; then the cars in maintenance or cleaning. Partners'' cars are counted apart.

> Good to know: Placeholder bookings never show on Now.

### Payment plans

A rental is paid in full at pickup, weekly, every 2 weeks, or monthly. A rental longer than one period (30 days) pays each period by itself. To change it, open the booking, then the **Payment plan** card on Overview or Money, and press **Change the plan**. Each payment is its share of the total by its days, due on the day it starts. An insurer-billed rental shows **Insurer billed** and is never in Money due unless the renter owes a part. Admins, customer service and finance change the plan; fleet sees it.

## All bookings

The **All bookings** tab of Bookings has the search (booking number, name, email, phone, plate or car code), the status (All, Out now, Booked, Returned, Cancelled; closed bookings are found with the search, which also finds the insurer). **Out now** shows the bookings on rent and those whose pickup passed without a check-in, together. Each booking is one row: its number and status in plain words, the car with its photo, the renter with **Call** and **Text**, the dates, the money (paid up, to pay, overdue, insurer billed) and Bill to.

## The request queue

Open **Bookings** > **Requests and offers**. The oldest waiting request is at the top.

1. The numbers at the top: waiting for an offer, past the reply target (red), offers out, accepted but not paid, and offers expired. Each one is a filter: press it and the list shows just those, with the matching chip below marked as chosen.
2. One queue, the most urgent first: the longest wait, then offers accepted but not paid, then offers out by when they expire. Each row has the car with its photo, the dates, the price, the renter with **Call** and **Text**, the licence (verified, to review, or not uploaded yet), who is answering it, and one button: **Send offer**, **Follow up** or **Open**. **Decline** sits beside **Send offer**.
3. Waiting shows how long the renter has waited ("12 min", "3 h", "2 days"); red means past the first reply target (5 minutes, set in Program settings). **Promise** counts down the 2 hours the site promises the renter.
4. Filter by Active, New, Changes asked, Offer out, Accepted, not paid or Expired. The list remembers your last choice on that device; **Active** always shows the whole queue and replaces what it remembered. When the same renter asks for the same car for overlapping dates again and the earlier request or offer expired, only the newest is listed: the older ones are linked to it and leave Requests (they keep their history). An expired offer leaves the active queue 48 hours after it expired, or once its pickup time passed; Expired lists the ones from the last 7 days. After 7 days an expired offer leaves Requests and offers and becomes a renter lead, once, in People > Renters > Leads (Expired offers), with the car and the dates the renter wanted and a To do for Sales to win them back. An offer still out when its pickup time passes expires by itself.

![](/guides/img/admin-02-requests-desktop-6521282d.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 820; address: carmacars.ca/admin/requests; pins: 1 38.9 29.9, 2 22.2 43.3")

> Good to know: A request whose pickup time passes without an offer expires by itself, with a note in its history. The renter is not emailed unless "Email the renter when their request expires that way" is on in Program settings.

## Answer a request with an offer

1. The Review and offer tab shows the request as the renter sent it.
2. Adjust the car, the dates, the rate type, the places, the rates (under **Show rate card**) and fees, the deposit and extras. A place changed away from a delivery or a collection takes its fee box and its fee with it.
3. Price on the right updates as you change things.
4. Add a message, choose how long the offer stays open, then press **Send the offer**.

![](/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-353f3707.jpg "desktop; size: 1200 1550; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review; pins: 1 5.0 6.5, 2 7.5 45.8, 3 74.2 42.6, 4 76.7 98.1")

5. Changed fields but not ready to send? Press **Save changes**. The panel "The offer as the renter sees it" shows the result.
6. Can''t do it? Press **Decline** and fill in Reason and any alternative.
7. Need an answer first? Press **Ask the renter** to send a question.

![](/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-4dd4ed06.jpg "desktop; size: 500 80; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review; pins: 6 41.2 52.5, 7 18.0 52.5")

Opening a request takes it for you: everyone else sees "Being answered by" your name and since when, with Send the offer and Decline off, until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work; Program settings). Press **Take over** to answer one someone else holds; it is noted in the history. A second answer is refused with who answered and when. A request from the website opens to Sales after 15 minutes (Program settings); until then Admins, customer service and fleet answer it.

## Send an offer without a request

Press **Send an offer** at the top of Bookings, or **Send an offer without a request** on Requests and offers. For a customer on the phone, by text or at the counter: no request needed.

The screen is seven short steps, each with one line saying what to do, and the price beside it (on a phone the total sits at the bottom of the screen: press **See every line**). What most offers never need is under each step''s **More options**, which stays open while something in it is used.

1. **Who is renting and when**: find the renter by name, phone or email, or press **Not on file? Add a new customer** (full legal name, mobile, email for the offer link, date of birth). A customer already on file with the same email or phone is shown with Use: one person, one record. Then the pickup and the return.
2. **Which car**: search by car code, plate or name; each car says Free or Not free for the dates. More options: the rate card and the type and free-only filters.
3. **Where they pick up and return**: at our location, we deliver or collect (the address and distance), an airport or the owner''s location. The fee each one makes shows under it, Automatic or Set by hand.
4. **How damage is covered**: the renter''s own insurance, a credit card or the Protection Plan. More options: another Protection Plan price.
5. **Extras**: add-ons, when the car has any.
6. **The price**: the rate sheet price is filled in. More options: another price (a total for the trip or a rate a day, with why), Amounts I type (before or after HST), the total the renter pays, kilometres, a promo code, the deposit and a discount (an Admin), and **Fees**: press **Change** to set one by hand, **Reset to automatic** to undo it. Below: how it is paid (card online and a card hold unless you change it under More options).
7. **Send it**: who found this client (sales and customer service), a message, and Text or Email. More options: how long the offer is open, the owner''s view, who found the client (an Admin) and the internal note. Above the button, **Ready to send** or **Missing:** with what is left; press Send and each missing field says what it needs. Press **Send the offer to** the renter, or **Save without sending** to keep it as a request for later. **The offer as the renter sees it** is under the price.

> Good to know: Choices drive the charges. Take off a delivery, a collection, the Protection Plan or an add-on and its fee goes with it, even a fee set by hand: there is nothing to remove in a second place. Choose it again and the fee starts from the automatic amount.

> Good to know: It makes the same request and offer the website makes: the renter approves, signs and pays (or you record the payment), and only then is the car on the calendar. No "request received" email goes to the renter for an offer you send. Staff commissions and statements count it like any other booking.

## Change an offer that is out

The renter has the offer (Offered), or approved it and has not paid (Signing and payment). Open **More actions** on the booking and press **Edit the offer**.

1. Change anything: the car, the dates, the places, the price, fees, the deposit, add-ons, how it is paid. Each changed field is highlighted and the before and after are listed. Amounts I type (Before tax or After tax) and the Total the renter pays (after tax) work as on Send an offer.
2. Write what changed in Message to the renter and choose how long the offer is open.
3. Press **Save and send the update**: the renter gets the new version by email or text (ticked), and the old version no longer counts. Or press **Save without telling the renter** and tell them yourself.
4. A confirmed booking is changed with **Change the booking** (Propose a change, below).

> Tip: No need to withdraw first. **Withdraw the offer** is only for taking it back for good; **Send again, later expiry** gives the renter more time, and **Renter approved by phone** records a yes given on a call.

## Edit a booking that has started

On a confirmed, on-trip or returned booking (an Admin: a closed one too), Overview, **Edit the booking**, **Edit**.

1. Change the pickup or the return (extend or shorten: the rental charge is worked out again at this booking''s rates), the car (on trip: the car it leaves goes to Out of service for Fleet to check), the rental charge for the trip, each fee, the kilometres a day, the deposit (an Admin) and the note.
2. Type why, if you like, and tick **Email the renter what changed**, or leave it off for a silent correction. Press **Save the changes**.
3. What is open now shows at once: **Email a pay link** or **Text a pay link** for exactly that amount, **Charge** the saved card (the renter agreed), or record cash or an e-Transfer on the Money tab.

> Good to know: Each edit is kept with who, when, why, before and after (Edits, under the form) and in the booking''s history. A closed booking''s owner split and the staff commission follow. To have the renter accept and sign first, use Propose a change instead.

## Fees, a forgotten fee and the balance

On the booking''s Money tab, Fees lists each fee. Press **Change or add a fee**.

1. Type a new amount (for the whole trip, before HST) beside any fee, or choose one not on the booking (the young driver fee shows its price for these dates), or add a charge of its own with or without HST.
2. Press **Save the fees**. The balance shows by part (rental, fees) with the pay link, the saved card and Record a payment beside it.
3. The renter sees the balance on their booking with a Pay button, and pays by card on Stripe''s form.

> Good to know: Every change is recorded (Changes to the fees): the amount before and after, who and why. Customer service and sales may change fees while Program settings, Staff may change fees, is on.

## A renter with only a debit or prepaid card

A credit card is required by default: the deposit must be on a credit card so the deductible can be charged. The pay page tells a renter with only a debit or prepaid card to contact us.

1. On the booking''s Money tab, press **Allow debit and prepaid cards for this booking** and type the reason. Who and when are kept, and the change is in the booking''s history.
2. The booking''s pay page, staff pay links and deposit hold then take a debit or prepaid card, and the renter is told the hold lowers the money available on the card until it is released, which can take several business days.
3. **Require a credit card again** turns it off.

The Money tab shows each card used and its type (credit, debit, prepaid). A booking on credit card rental coverage is always paid on the credit card that carries the coverage, and cannot be allowed. Program settings, **Card types accepted**, can open debit and prepaid cards to every booking.

## Correct a renter''s details

On the renter''s page (People, Renters) or on any of their bookings, **Edit renter**.

1. Correct the name, email, phone, date of birth, licence, home address (start typing to find it) or the staff note.
2. A new email also becomes their sign-in at once (no confirmation needed for a typo you correct); tick **Email the renter a link to set a password** to send one there. Unsigned agreements and offers go to the new address.
3. Press **Save the renter**. An email that another renter has is refused with their name; the same phone is a warning.
4. The same person entered twice? Possible duplicates (same email, same phone, or same name and date of birth) shows under the renter. **Merge into this record** moves the other record''s bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages here and fills any detail missing here; the other record stays, blocked, with the merge in both histories.

## The Money tab: Rental charges and Security deposit

The booking''s Money tab opens on a strip with the three numbers that matter: **Rental due**, **Deposit** (one word: Not collected, Held, Charged, Released or Partly kept) and **Total paid**. Below are two panels, side by side on a computer and one above the other on a phone. Collecting one never touches the other, and every receipt says which one it is.

**Rental charges**: each line of the price and the total, Paid, then Balance due.

1. The one main button, Collect (the amount) rental: choose how. **The card on file** charges it now (Finance or an Admin); **A payment link by text** or **A payment link by email** sends the renter Stripe''s secure form; **On this device: hand it to the renter** opens it for the renter to type; **Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)** records money received (an e-Transfer, cheque or transfer needs its reference). For: the rental and fees together by default, or one of them. With the card on file, the rental and fees together are one charge with one receipt that lists both (the rental is paid first, then the fees; an insurer''s part and money already received another way are left out). The renter gets a receipt; **Print** prints one to hand over.
2. **A later charge** (before the return): on the card on file, by a link, on this device, or recorded. Choose the **Reason** from the list (Mileage overage, Fuel, Cleaning, Smoking, Late return, Tolls, Tickets/fines, Damage, Missing items, Other) and add a note; Other needs its note. The renter''s receipt shows the reason.
3. **Save a card** saves the renter''s card without charging it. Card readers, the fees (**Change or add a fee**), failed card payments (**Paid another way**), payments received another way and **Refund** sit in this panel too. The history lists rental payments only.
4. An offer paid another way: once the renter approved and signed and the money is recorded, the booking is confirmed (or press **Confirm the booking**).

**Security deposit**: the amount, how it is taken (a credit card hold, a debit or prepaid card at the standard multiple, a charge, or cash), its status in one word and the next step.

1. Not collected: the one main button, Collect (the amount) deposit. **Hold on the card on file** places the hold now (Finance or an Admin); **A deposit hold link by text** or **A deposit hold link by email**, or **A hold on this device: hand it to the renter**; **Charge the card on file as the deposit** only when no hold can be placed; **Cash or e-Transfer (record it)**. The rental balance is not touched.
2. Before every pickup the deposit hold link is texted to the renter on its own: 24 hours before (at once when the pickup is sooner), for a confirmed booking whose deposit is a card hold with no hold yet. The panel says **Deposit link texted** and when it was opened. No mobile number, or the text not sent: a task **Deposit link not sent**. **Settings**, then Site settings, Deposit link by text: on or off, and the hours.
3. Held, while the car is out: **Release** (an Admin, with the reason), **Keep part (damage/fees)** with the amount and the reason from the list, or **Re-authorize the hold** on the saved card before it lapses (the panel shows when the hold expires). A job re-authorizes it by itself about 24 hours before it expires; if it cannot, Finance and the Admins get the alert **Deposit hold not re-authorized**.
4. **Hold expired**: a card hold lasts about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise. Once it has expired, nothing can be kept from it: the panel says Hold expired, Keep and Release are hidden, and **Charge the card on file instead** opens the later charge with the amount and the reason filled in.
4. After the return: **Settle the deposit** (below).
5. **Waive the deposit** (an Admin, before it is taken), **Change the debit deposit**, and **Allow debit and prepaid cards for this booking** sit in this panel. The history lists deposit payments only.
6. A deposit taken in cash or by e-Transfer is given back the same way after the return: Finance gets a task; press **Returned** with the reference or receipt number.

> Good to know: Statements, reconciliation and the deposit settlement read each payment with its method: a cash deposit is never refunded to a card.

## Settle the deposit

The deposit is never given back by itself. Finance or an Admin settles it after the return: on the booking''s Money tab, under Deposit, press **Settle the deposit**. Issue the Check-out statement first.

1. The form shows the deposit, what is still available, the charges owed from the statement and what is taken from the deposit for them. What the deposit does not cover is charged to the card on file; with no card (or a card declined), the renter gets a pay link by email and text, and Finance has a task until it is paid.
2. Tolls and tickets can take up to 7 days to come in. Inside that window the whole rest of the deposit is filled in as the hold-back, until the window ends. To give it back sooner, tick Release now anyway: a toll that comes in later is charged to the card on file.
3. Something still open keeps the whole deposit: an incident, a claim, new damage at the return not priced, damage found later not billed, a toll or ticket on the car during the rental not matched or not charged, a card dispute, or charges not on a statement yet. The form lists them. Only an Admin can release part of it, with the reason; it is recorded.
4. Damage: **Keep the whole deposit (damage)** turns what is left of the deposit into a damage charge, with what was damaged and the photos; the renter is told. **Bill damage** adds a damage charge up to the $2,500 deductible (more goes through a claim): the deposit pays first, then the card on file.
5. Press **Settle**. The money moves at Stripe at once: the charges are collected and what is not owed is refunded or the hold released. A step Stripe refuses is tried again by itself, and Finance gets a task if it keeps failing.

> Good to know: A card hold lapses after about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise. While the car is out, or returned and not settled, the hold is collected in full a day and a half before it lapses: that keeps the money, and the settlement refunds what is not owed. A hold that lapses anyway is charged to the saved card, and Finance is told at once.

## A booking

Open **Bookings** > **Bookings**, then a booking number. Or type the number in the search box.

1. Tabs: Overview, Money, Changes, History, and Drivers and documents.
2. Overview shows the trip, the renter, what is still missing for the handover, and the price.
3. Open tasks for this booking, with the queue and the due time.
4. Top right: **Email the renter** and **More actions**, the menu with **Edit the offer**, **Stop blocking the calendar**, **Cancel for the renter**, **Cancel by CarmaCars** and the rest.
5. Under the booking number: **Next step**, what happens next and who does it, with one button for that step (for example **Send the offer**, **Sign on this device** or **Check in the car**); then where the booking is on its way, from Request to Closed, with the dates, the days, the total and who pays.

![](/guides/img/admin-04-booking-desktop-b56b668a.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 960; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065; pins: 2 50.0 46.6, 4 85.4 14.5, 5 22.9 26.8")

## Check a car out or in

From the booking, with your phone or a tablet: the same checklist field staff use.

1. A confirmed booking shows **Check in (pickup)** under Check-in, check-out and signing; a booking on rent shows **Check out (return)**. Today lists the check-ins and check-outs due, each with **Check in** or **Check out**.
2. The checklist opens: the ready check, the renter and their licence and card, the odometer (km) and fuel or charge, the keys, the photo set (every side, the wheels, the interior, the odometer and fuel gauge, the plate), damage marks with close-ups, then the renter and you sign.
3. Photos wait on the device without a connection and upload in the background. Each keeps its time, and the place when the device allows location.
4. A field job of the booking is taken over (the history says so); with no job, one is made for you. When done, press **See the photo report**.

> Tip: Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in the same way from their own booking page.

## The photo report, late returns and the return charges

Under Check-in, check-out and signing, press **Photo report**.

1. The report shows the due-back time, the actual check-in and check-out, Late by (or Overdue by while the car is out), the odometer and kilometres over the allowance, the fuel or charge out and in, every photo with its time and place, and the damage.
2. At check-out the late return (after the grace period of the fee defaults), the mileage overage and the fuel or recharging are written to the return charges at once. The fuel is a suggested line: the car''s tank x the fuel missing x the pump price of its grade (Program settings, updated weekly) x 1.25, plus the refuelling fee; an electric car the battery kWh x the charge missing x the price a kWh, plus the fee. A pump receipt entered later replaces it. Fleet and Finance confirm it on the deposit review; it is never charged to a card by itself.
3. Not charging one? Press **Waive** beside it and give the reason: it stays waived if the charges are worked out again.
4. The time was wrong? Press **Correct the check-out time** (or the check-in time) with the reason: lateness and the late charges follow, and the history keeps both times.
5. The renter gets the same report (without these buttons) by email and in their Documents. Late by shows on the booking and in the Bookings list.

### The renter says the car is back

Every overdue email, text and alert (at the return time, at 15 minutes and the final notice) has a one-tap **I''ve returned the car** link, and the renter''s booking page has the button. The renter can add photos, the odometer, the fuel level and the time they returned it. Sending it stops every overdue notice of the booking at once, the booking shows **Returned, waiting for confirmation**, and Fleet gets an urgent To do: "The renter says the car is back".

1. Open the booking. The card **The renter says the car is back** shows what the renter gave, marked renter-provided, with their photos.
2. Check the car: the return place, the tracker, the photos.
3. Press **Confirm** to complete the trip. Correct the odometer, fuel or return time first if they are wrong: the late charges follow the time you confirm. The renter''s photos join the check-out report.
4. Or press **Deny** and say why. The renter gets your reason by email and text, and the overdue notices start again.

Checking the car in the usual way also completes the trip and stops the notices. Admins, Fleet, Sales, Customer service and field staff can Confirm or Deny.

## Signatures on the spot, or by link

The renter or an additional driver signs the rental agreement on your device, or on their own phone.

1. While a signature is missing, the booking shows **Sign now on this device**, **Email the signing link** and **Text the signing link**.
2. No agreement made yet (the renter has not saved their details at home)? **Sign now on this device** still shows: press **Prepare the agreement to sign now** and it is made on the spot.
3. **Sign now on this device**: confirm the name matches their licence and that you saw the original licence (photograph it if none is on file), then press **Hand the device to** and their name.
4. They read both agreements (CarmaCars'' and Blind Spot''s), tick the statements and sign. Then **Back to the staff view** for the next signer.
5. The record is the same as signing online, and says it was signed in person, collected by you, on your device. It is printed on the signed copy''s signature record page.

## Rental agreements: every version, every field

The booking''s Rental agreements card: the current version of CarmaCars'' and Blind Spot''s agreements, every earlier one, and what is still blank.

1. Once the agreement is signed and countersigned, any change to what it prints makes a new version of both documents by itself: the dates, the price lines, the car, a driver added or corrected, the coverage, the deposit or how it was paid, an address.
2. A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage option is signed again: the renter (and each driver it affects) gets their link by email and text, and the card shows "Agreement v3 waiting for signature". A correction (a typo in an address, a plate written differently) is filed without signing; the renter gets the corrected copy by email.
3. Check-in makes the "as picked up" copy (time out, km out, fuel out, the car''s plate and VIN, the check-in report), countersigned by whoever checked the car out; check-out makes the closing copy (time in, km in, driven and charged, fuel in, late hours, damage, the return charges, the final totals). Both go to the renter by email.
4. **Every version** lists each one with what changed and both PDFs. **Resend the signing links**, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your phone or tablet.
5. The card lists what the agreements still print blank (a licence expiry, the insurer''s policy number, the insured vehicle, a VIN). Type the values and press **Save the missing fields**: the agreements follow.
6. Check-in stops while a field a claim needs is blank. An Admin can let it go ahead: type the reason and press **Override**; the reason is in the booking''s history.
7. **Make the agreements again** checks both against the booking at once (they also follow every change by themselves).
8. **Edit the wording** (Admin only) changes CarmaCars'' agreement text for this booking: press **Change** beside a clause, edit its text, say why and press **Save the wording**; **Add** writes Additional terms at the end of Part 2. Only clauses not required by law or the insurer can be removed; the consents are fixed, and Blind Spot''s form (the insurer''s official form) is never changed. Before the renter signs, the agreement is made again; after, the change is a new version they sign, and **Every version** shows each clause before and after.

## Signing that holds up in a dispute

Every signature on the site is made the same way: rental agreements, amendments and new versions (remotely or on your device), and the owner agreements, schedules and forms, a co-owner''s link, the partner, investment and staff agreements.

1. The licence on file is shown. A 6-digit code to their phone or email on file is optional: the signer may press **Verify by code (optional)**, and Program settings, E-signing, **ask for a one-time code** makes it a required first step again (off by default). Without the code, the certificate says the identity was not confirmed by a code.
2. They say they read the documents, initial the key terms (each initials box is saved with **Save initials**; **Clear** takes it back to initial again) (damage and the deductible, the deposit and later charges, fuel, kilometres and late returns, their coverage, cancellation), give three consents (to sign electronically, to receive records electronically, to card charges under the agreement) and draw their signature.
3. Owners, partners, investors and staff do the same for their documents: the code, the reading, the key terms of their documents initialled (for example the Enrollment Agreement''s three confirmations, Form C''s acknowledgments, Schedule C, the staff agreement''s confidentiality), two consents and the drawn signature. Form C''s witness still types their name beside the owner.
4. Each step is recorded with its time, IP address and device, and the place when the device shares it. The signed PDFs end with a certificate of completion; anyone can check a signed file at `carmacars.ca/verify`.
5. Typed names are off. For a signer who cannot draw, an Admin can turn on the accessibility fallback: **Settings** > **Program**, Esign typed fallback.

## Card disputes: the evidence pack

Everything that proves the rental, in one PDF for Stripe.

1. When a card payment is disputed, the evidence pack is built by itself: the signed agreements with their certificates, the check-in and check-out reports with photos, kilometres and fuel, the licence, the payments and charges, every message to the renter, and the card checks from Stripe. It is staged in Stripe as the dispute''s evidence, and To do gets an urgent task.
2. Open the booking: the Rental agreements card shows the pack. Press **Download** to check it, then **Submit to Stripe** before the evidence date.
3. **Build the dispute evidence pack** makes one at any time (an Admin or Finance).

## The licence before an offer is accepted

Front, back and a selfie, from the request on.

1. After sending a request the renter is asked for their licence. A licence already on file from an earlier booking is used again while it is valid after the return.
2. The offer cannot be accepted (by the renter, or by you on their word) and nothing is paid until the licence and its expiry date are on file.
3. Review the images as usual with **Review documents**: the card Renter documents is on Review and offer too.
4. The switch is in **Settings** > **Program**, Booking requests and offers: Booking licence required (on), with the selfie (on).

## The licence reader

Every licence photo is read on upload: the back''s barcode first, else the vision model (within the day''s AI allowance).

1. The renter''s empty licence fields are filled from the read; the renter confirms them. A blurry or cut-off photo is taken again at once.
2. **Review documents** shows what was read and one line per check, Pass or Flag: photos, valid to the return, class accepted, age at pickup, name and date of birth, the Ontario number, front and back, and the main driver''s Ontario licence. Staff still approve.
3. **Settings** > **Program**, Driver''s licence reader: **Approve automatically when every check passes** (off). On: a driver whose front and back both read sharp and every check passes is approved in your name; anything flagged waits for a person.
4. **Primary driver must hold an Ontario licence** (on): a main driver with a licence from elsewhere becomes an additional driver, the booking needs "Primary driver: Ontario licence needed" and pickup is blocked. The renter adds a main driver, who signs on their own link. On the document review, **Admin: undo or let it go**: undo puts the first main driver back; let it go needs a reason.

> Tip: What was read is staff only and is deleted with the licence image. The licence number is never written to the logs.

## Renter documents: licence and proof of coverage

A renter''s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage (OPCF 27 or a credit card''s rental coverage) are checked before the handover. You check them yourself; no task is needed.

1. A booking with documents waiting is a line on To do: "Check ''s documents for booking ", marked Now when the pickup is within two days. Press **Review documents**.
2. The pop-up shows each driver''s images and the coverage: the insurer, policy number and expiry, or the card, its type and whether the name matches.
3. What to check is written once at the top. One wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**: they are asked for a new one.
4. Then press **Approve all**: every image, the proof of coverage and the Protection Plan still waiting are approved in one step. The number in the button is exactly what it approves (an image whose file was removed is not counted), and an image not tied to a driver of the booking is listed under **Other documents**. Anything the system refuses is named with the reason.
5. The same pop-up is on the booking: the card Renter documents (**Review documents**) on Overview and on Drivers and documents.

> Tip: Each opening of a renter''s documents is logged. The links to the images last one minute. Field staff can also check a licence in person at the check-in (photos and four checks): the history says "checked in person". Field staff also review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from My jobs, with the same Approve all or a reason to reject: the history says the reviewer''s role, field. Sales review the licence images (not the coverage) of any booking being arranged or under way from their To do or the booking, with the same Approve all or a reason to reject: the history says the role, sales.

## Payments by day

**Money** > **Payments**, the **By day** tab: every payment and refund of a day or a range, by method, the cash drawer and the refunds waiting. Finance has the same screen.

1. Choose From and To and the methods (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer, bank transfer, pre-authorized debit, other), then press **Show**.
2. Totals by method and for each day; cards read as the card and its last four digits, never a code.
3. The cash drawer: expected (cash in less cash given back) against the count Finance records with **Record the count**; a difference shows over or short.
4. Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere with the policy maths. **Approve** or **Decline** with the reason in the row, then **Issue the refund**.
5. **Export CSV** for the bookkeeper.

## Propose a change to a confirmed booking

The renter gets an email and answers on their booking. The calendar moves only when they accept.

1. Open the booking''s Changes tab. Under Propose a change, set the new pickup, return or car.
2. To price it by hand, type a New rental charge before tax. Leave it empty to use the car''s rates.
3. Write the Reason, for the renter. They read it.
4. Press **Preview the price**, then **Send to the renter**.

![](/guides/img/admin-05-booking-changes-desktop-97008b21.jpg "desktop; size: 1200 520; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065?tab=changes; pins: 1 17.5 33.7, 2 9.2 50.0, 3 38.3 71.2, 4 12.9 91.9")

## Who a booking is credited to

Overview (and Review and offer) shows the Sales credit: the staff member the booking counts for in their sales.

1. A quote or a rental is credited to whoever created or added it. A request from the website is credited to whoever sent its first offer.
2. To give it to someone else, press **Reassign**, choose who (or Nobody), say whether they sourced the client and write the reason. The booking''s history and the audit log keep it, and the deal stays in the same week and month.
3. Sourced means the staff member chose I sourced this client when they entered it, it came with a field staff referral link, or you credited it. Only a sourced booking earns a staff commission. A website request earns none unless you credit someone.
4. Someone said they sourced a website request? The credit line shows the claim: press **Credit them** or **Not theirs**, with a reason.
5. A price typed by hand shows beside the rate-sheet price, with the reason. A price under the floor or past the discount limit is flagged: press **Mark reviewed** once you have looked at it.

> Good to know: A request keeps the lead-time adjustment of the moment it came in ("Short-notice pricing +10%" or "Booked ahead −5%"), through the offer and the payment. To change it, open the booking''s review screen, **More options**, **Lead-time pricing (%)**: a number (0 for none), or empty for the tier of the request. A price typed by hand replaces it.

> Good to know: The rental never goes below the car''s minimum daily rate or above its maximum (its price limits, set by the owner or on the car''s Rates tab), whatever the discount, promo code or lead-time pricing: a line "Minimum daily rate for this car" or "Maximum daily rate for this car" brings it back. Only an Admin allows a price outside them: **More options**, **Allow a price outside the car''s price limits (Admin only)**, with the reason.

> Tip: The renter has 48 hours to accept (and sign the amendment) or decline, with one reminder. Any extra is charged to their Card on File; a lower price raises a refund for your approval.

## Review requests

Every renter is asked for a review by email and text, as they chose, only from 9 am to 9 pm Toronto time. Nothing needs setting up.

| Message | When |
| --- | --- |
| Mid-trip check | Rentals of 2 days or more, 24 hours after the pickup: "How is the car? Reply or call if anything is off." No review ask. |
| Review request | 1 hour after the check-out. It links the review page: the renter taps what they liked, adds a sentence, and gets a short draft to copy and post on Google. |
| Reminder | 24 hours after the request. |
| Final follow-up | 7 days after the request. Nothing more after it. |

1. The booking page has the card Review requests: each message with when it went or when it will go, and why it stopped.
2. **Ask for a review** sends the request now (or at 9 am if it is later than 9 pm), on any booking on a trip, returned or closed. Not twice in 24 hours.
3. On hold: a return or later charge (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls and tickets) is not settled or waived, or an incident or dispute is open. The request goes by itself once they are. Press **Send anyway** to send it now.
4. **Mark reviewed** stops the messages when the renter tells you they already reviewed.

The messages also stop by themselves when the renter presses "I already left a review", leaves a review on the site, unsubscribes, or a Google review is matched to them. **Bookings** > **Reviews** has the numbers (requests sent, on hold, reviews detected, the average rating), the hold list and the Google reviews to match.

> Tip: The draft is made only from what the renter picked and wrote, and from the booking (the car, how long, delivery or pickup). Everyone gets the Google link, whatever their stars; a renter who gives 3 stars or fewer also sees "Something wasn''t right? Tell us directly".

## What the owner sees, and owner deductions

Each booking on an owner''s or partner''s car shows the card What the owner sees at the top of its page.

1. **Hide from the owner** keeps the booking''s revenue from the owner until the car is returned, or until the owner statement covering it is approved. The owner sees the booking as Booked with its dates, and the calendar still shows the car busy. Add a reason if you like: it is kept in the history.
2. **Show to the owner** shows it now. Approving the statement shows every hidden booking on it by itself.
3. Not shown to the owner is for a booking with no owner revenue (an insurance placeholder, a shareholder''s or the owner''s own use at no charge): the owner sees only that the car is unavailable for those dates. A booking with revenue cannot be set this way.
4. Add a rental and Send an offer have What the owner sees. It starts from Settings > Program, Owners and fleet: Owners see a booking''s revenue (right away by default).
5. On the Money tab, Owner deductions on this booking: **Add a booking expense** (cleaning, repair, fuel, platform fee or other, the amount, the reason the owner reads, a receipt number) comes off before Owner Revenue.
6. **Set the Revenue Share for this booking** applies within the car''s signed terms. Above the terms only an Admin can, with Above the signed terms ticked and the reason. **Back to the car''s terms** undoes it.
7. Add a rental has the same under The car''s owner.

> Good to know: The owner''s statement carries each booking that counts toward the owner''s revenue, at its true amounts, and lists each deduction with its reason, so the payout is always right. A booking billed to the renter always counts. Left out: a booking billed to an insurer and hidden from the owner (while Program settings keep only insurance replacements hidden), an insurer-billed rental that does not block the calendar, and a rental with "Counts toward the owner''s revenue" off. The booking page says when a booking is not part of the owner''s revenue and why. When a booking that was left out starts counting (Blocks the calendar turned on, shown to the owner, or billed to the renter), the owner gets the new booking email once, at that moment. Customer service and sales add deductions only while Program settings let them change fees.

## Email the renter or the adjuster

Press **Email the renter** at the top of a booking, or open its **Messages & history** section.

1. Write a **Subject** and a **Message**, or pick a **Quick reply** to start from (Settings > Quick replies keeps them).
2. Press **Email the renter**. It goes from CarmaCars (bookings@carmacars.ca) and replies come back to the bookings inbox. The renter also sees it in their account and can answer there.
3. On a booking an insurer pays, choose **From**: CarmaCars, or Blind Spot Car Rental (insurance). **Email the adjuster** writes to the adjuster''s email on the booking (Insurance claim), always from Blind Spot Car Rental.

The **Messages & history** section is the booking''s Activity log (release 35): what you and the renter wrote, every email of the booking, the texts, chat, calls, notes, events, payments, documents and visits, newest first, with a chip for each type and a search. The email form is under the log; each email you send shows in the log with your name.

> Good to know: Emails go out through the same daily limit as every email (the line under the form shows today''s use). A message to a renter goes before digests and marketing; past the limit it waits until midnight. To write to a renter from **People** > **Renters**, open the renter: Email the renter is at the bottom, about their latest booking or the one you pick.

### Record the pickup or the return now (details later)
When the car went out or came back but the checklist could not be done (no photos, no time, the renter dropped the keys), the booking''s **Check-in, check-out and signing** card has **Record the pickup now (details later)** on a confirmed booking and **Record the return now (details later)** while the car is on rent. Give the actual time (now, or earlier), the odometer and fuel if you know them, and why. The booking moves on (on rent, or returned), late return charges follow the actual time, and Fleet gets the task **Add the photos and readings for CC-...**. A car overdue or due back today also has **Returned**: on the To do list (Check-ins and check-outs today), on Bookings > Now and at the top of the booking page, which the late return alert opens. It asks only the return time (now, or earlier) and the km and fuel if you know them, and records the return the same way. Once returned, the statement can be issued and the deposit settled; releasing the deposit before the photos are in needs an Admin and a reason. A pickup without the deposit taken needs an Admin to waive it with a reason, and without the renter''s signature on the check-in report an Admin''s reason too. Later, **Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings** opens the usual checklist (photos, readings, your signature): the task closes when it is saved.

The Agreement card says **Waiting for the renter''s details** when the renter still has blanks to fill (date of birth, address, mobile, licence, coverage): their account asks for them before signing and paying. No email or text is sent.

### Find a booking
**Bookings** has one search box: type the booking number (CC-1042, cc1042 or just 1042), the renter''s or a driver''s name, an email, a phone number in any format, a plate (spaces do not matter) or a car code, then press Enter. The status filters still apply to what is found.

### Record a card payment taken outside the site
A card taken in the Stripe Dashboard, or on a card reader, is recorded on the booking''s **Money** tab with **Record card payment**.

1. Choose what it paid: **Rental and fees**, **Rental**, **Fees**, **Later charges** or **Deposit hold**, and where it was taken.
2. Type the **Last 4 digits** and the amount. A Stripe payment id (pi_... or ch_..., from the payment in the Stripe Dashboard) is optional for a payment: press **Look up** and the amount and last 4 digits are checked against Stripe.
3. Press **Record it**. A payment confirms a booking waiting for payment, as any payment does.

> Good to know: A deposit hold needs its Stripe payment id, so it can be captured or released from **Settle the deposit**. It is recorded as held, with the usual release reminders. A hold on a reader lapses after 2 days, one made online after about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise.

### Link a payment taken outside the platform
A charge or a card deposit taken in the Stripe Dashboard or through a Stripe payment link is linked to its booking by an Admin, on the booking''s **Money** tab: **Link a payment taken outside the platform**, in the rental panel or the deposit panel.

1. Paste the Stripe payment id (pi_... or ch_..., from the payment in the Stripe Dashboard). **Look up** shows what Stripe says: the amount, paid or a hold, and the card.
2. Press **Link as a rental payment** or **Link as the deposit**.

> Good to know: It must be in Canadian dollars and not already linked. A rental payment may not be more than is open for the rental and fees. A deposit must be the whole deposit: a hold waiting to be captured is kept as held (settle it as any hold), a charged deposit is kept as captured. **Money** > **Unlinked Stripe** lists, every night, the Stripe payments of the last 60 days that no booking knows, with a best guess of the booking.

### Charge or hold the deposit on the card reader
With the S700 paired (Settings > Card reader), the **Money** tab has **Charge on reader** (everything open, the rental, the fees or a later charge) and **Hold deposit on reader**. Press **Send to the reader**: the amount shows on the reader and the renter taps, inserts or swipes the card. The screen updates by itself; **Cancel** stops the reader and nothing is charged. A deposit hold is captured or released from Settle the deposit like any hold.

### Credit card coverage: the same card
When the renter''s coverage is their credit card, the whole rental (rental and fees) is paid on that same card. The Money tab says which card. Another card on the pay page is refused and refunded at once; on the reader it is refused before the money is taken; a payment by e-Transfer, cash or the like is refused; a card typed by hand needs its last 4 digits and the box **This is the same card**. Deposits and later charges can go on any card. If the renter truly has to use another card or method, press **Allow another card** and give the reason (an Admin).

## Booked as soon as the renter accepts (release 28)

A booking is booked the moment the renter approves the offer. It takes the car on every calendar, the fleet board, the car''s availability and the counts, even before the payment or the pickup is recorded. Payment and the handover show as their own badges: **Booked, payment due** and **Pickup not recorded**. The first renter to approve gets the car: any other open offer on the same car and dates goes back to Requests with a Re-offer To do.

- **Booked, payment due** To do: a booked rental still unpaid within 48 hours of its pickup. Send the pay link, charge the saved card or record the payment.
- Record the pickup To do: a pickup time that passed with nothing recorded, as before.

When you send an offer, **The offer as the renter sees it** sits right under **Send the offer**: check it before you press it.

## Changes after signing: an amended agreement, no new signature

The rental terms (section 15.4) let CarmaCars update a booking after signing: an extension, new dates or times, a price adjustment, a fee, a car swap. The signed agreement keeps applying. Each change makes a new version of the agreement marked **Amended** with the date, carrying the renter''s original signature, and the renter is sent it. Nobody is asked to sign again, except an additional driver who never signed (they sign before driving).

## Check-in and check-out on one screen

On the booking page, **Check in (pickup)** and **Check out (return)** are one screen: the time (now unless you change it), the odometer, the fuel, the photos and a note. Pick many photos at once from the camera roll or take them; tag an angle on any photo if you like. The suggested angles (front, each corner and side, rear, odometer, fuel gauge, interior front and rear, trunk, wheels, any damage) tick themselves as photos are tagged. Nothing is required but the time; the renter''s own photos are added to the same report, each marked with who took it (the renter or staff) and its angle. The full checklist is still one tap away.

## Type into the Blind Spot agreement

On the **Rental agreements** card, **Type into the Blind Spot agreement** shows each box as the form prints it. Change a value and **Save the corrections**: it is drawn in that box, and the insured vehicle, the claim number, the adjuster and missing km or fuel go back onto the booking. **Preview the filled form** opens it with your corrections.

## Reopen an expired offer (release 28)

An expired offer reopens in one click: **Reopen offer** on the booking or on the **Expired** filter of Requests. The renter gets the usual offer email and text; the offer stays open 24 hours unless you type other hours. When the pickup time has passed, the dialog asks for the new pickup and return first. A renter can also press **Ask to reopen this offer**: you get the To do "Renter wants expired offer reopened" and an alert, as for a new request.

An offer sent after its pickup time no longer expires by itself: it expires at its own expiry time (the pickup only counts when the offer was sent before it and the pickup is 2 hours past). The offer screens say **Pickup time has passed: update it** and do not send until you move the pickup.

## One booking page, six sections (release 31)

A booking has six sections: **Overview** (the next step; the review and offer while it is being arranged), **Money**, **Drivers & documents** (with the agreement), **Car & handovers** (the check-in and check-out, the photo report, signing on this device, what the owner sees), **Messages & history** (with the review request) and **Claims & extras** (changes, extensions, add-ons). Customer service, Sales, Fleet and Finance see the sections their work needs. An old link to a tab opens the section that holds it now.

Admin and staff open the same booking page, the same car page and the same listing review: you see every section and button, each staff function sees the parts it works with (Fleet has no Money section; only customer service and you have **Claims & extras**; refunds are asked for by you or Finance). A staff link to a booking opens the same page in the staff portal.

Every list has one search box (it finds names, numbers, plates, phones, emails and VINs) and one row of at most five chips. **Clear** removes every filter; the last one you used comes back next time on this device.

## Charge the renter after the return

Once the car is back, the Money tab has one action for everything owed after the trip: **Charge the renter**.

1. Press **Charge the renter**.
2. Choose the **Reason** from the list and add a note if it helps (Other needs its note). Enter the **Amount**.
3. Read the line under it: it says where the money comes from before anything moves. The deposit hold while it is still valid and covers the amount (the rest of the hold is released at the same time); otherwise the card on file; otherwise a pay link to the renter by text or email.
4. Press **Charge $...**. If the hold expired meanwhile, the card on file is charged instead, with the same amount and reason.

**Release** stays its own button. The renter''s receipt shows the reason.

## A deposit charged to a debit or prepaid card

When the deposit is charged instead of held on a debit or prepaid card (Charge the card on file as the deposit), the renter also pays the **Card processing fee for a debit deposit** (Program settings, 2.9% and $0.30 by default): a separate, non-refundable amount on the same charge. The Money tab''s history and the receipt show it; the deposit refund returns the deposit only.

## What the renter sees still to do

While a booking waits to be signed and paid, the Next step quotes the renter''s own Sign and pay card, for example: The renter sees: "Two steps left: sign the rental agreement, then pay $...". Signed for an older version of the offer counts as not signed: the renter signs the updated agreement on their Sign and pay page.

## Override a pickup or a return that must go ahead (release 33)
Sometimes the trip has to start (or end) even though a check still stops it. On the booking page, a confirmed booking (or one waiting for payment) and a car on rent show **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) with each check in plain words: the deposit not taken, the rental agreement not signed, no renter signature on the check-in report, a licence or identity not verified, the coverage not confirmed, an additional driver who has not accepted, the payment still due, the calendar switch off, the car not marked available, maintenance overdue, the Ontario licence, the fleet insurance policy (when that rule is on in Program settings), the agreement''s claim details, the tracker; at a return, an odometer lower than at pickup.

1. Press **Override and record the pickup** (or the return).
2. Give the actual time (now, or earlier), the km and fuel if you know them, and why the trip must go ahead. The reason is required.
3. Press the button. The pickup (or the return) is recorded at that time, only the checks listed are passed, for this booking and this once. The booking''s history and the audit log say who, when, why and which checks; every Admin gets the alert Override used. A payment still due is not waived: the booking is confirmed with the balance open, and the deposit is still to collect (it is not waived). The photos and readings come later, as with Record now.

When staff (Fleet, customer service, Sales, field staff) need it, they press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return) on the same card with the time they recorded. You get the alert Override asked for and a line on the To do: press **Approve** (one tap) and it is recorded with the time they entered, or **Decline** with a note. The request also shows on the booking page, with Approve and Decline.

## Record a past trip (release 33)
A trip that happened but was never recorded (the pickup and the return both passed): on the booking page press **Record a past trip**. Give the actual pickup and return times, the km and fuel at each if you know them, and the reason. Every check that would stop it is overridden as above, in one step: the booking lands in **Returned**, the late return charges follow the actual return time, and the deposit can be settled. The car''s status today is left as it is, and the renter is not sent a "your rental started" email for a trip long over. Fleet gets the task to add the photos and readings. Staff ask for it the same way; you approve in one tap.

## Book it now: an offer that is a booking at once (release 33)
When you send an offer (answering a request, or **Send an offer** without one), tick **Book it now (no renter approval)** above Send. The offer becomes the approved version at once: the booking waits for payment, the car is held for its dates as for any approved offer, and the renter gets one link to the **Sign and pay** page to sign and pay (the "approve your offer" email is not sent). To have them sign and pay with you, open the booking: **Sign now on this device**, then take the card on this device. When customer service or Sales tick it, the offer goes out and you get the alert Override asked for and a To do line: **Approve** in one tap books it the same way. The booking''s history says who booked it and that the renter did not approve it.

Already sent the offer? Tell Claude or the assistant: "Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the renter agreed by phone". Claude''s connector has the tool **Book an offer now**, and **Send an offer** and **Make an offer** take Book it now too; the assistant (Assistant at the top of the menu) takes it in the same sentence as the offer. Each is two steps: you see what will change (nothing is changed yet), then you confirm, and the booking waits for the renter to sign and pay as above. As an Admin it is done at once; when customer service or Sales ask the assistant, it waits for your one-tap Approve.

## A request replaced by a newer one
When a request or offer expired and the renter made a newer one for the same car and dates, the old one is hidden from Requests and keeps its number and history. Both booking pages say so under the title: **Replaced by #CC-10483** on the old one and **Replaces #CC-10482** on the new one, each a link to the other. Customer service, Sales and the other staff pages show the same note.

## Change protection (release 41)

How damage to the car is covered is one control on the booking page: the **Protection** card at the top (Overview and the Money tab). An Admin, customer service and fleet use it on any booking; sales on a request or an offer.

1. Press **Change protection**. A small window lists the three options: **Own insurance (OPCF 27)**, **Credit card coverage** and **Protection Plan**, each with the price difference (the plan shows its price a day times the days, plus HST), the deposit (no coverage rule changes it) and what the renter provides.
2. The rule is the same as on the renter''s page: credit card coverage needs the renter''s card picked from the coverage list, a card that covers this car, and the renter''s confirmation that they pay with it; OPCF 27 needs the renter''s confirmation that they upload their policy; otherwise the Protection Plan. An Admin can tick Admin override: the reason is recorded on the change and in the booking history.
3. Write the reason (required; the renter reads it) and press **Change protection**.

What happens: the booking is repriced at once. More to pay is a balance to collect on the Money tab; less, when the plan was paid, is a refund for an Admin to approve. No money moves by itself. An offer is sent again as a new version; a confirmed booking or a rental in progress gets the amended agreement (the renter signs the new version when the rules ask) and one email. Proof tasks follow the new option. Changes are refused after damage is reported on the booking.

A renter''s request to leave the Protection Plan shows on the same card with their proof (**Open the proof**). Customer service or an Admin presses **Approve** (the change is made and the coverage confirmed) or **Decline** with a note the renter reads. The task "The renter asks to leave the Protection Plan" opens the booking.

## Change the car before pickup

On a request, an offer or a confirmed booking that is not picked up yet, press **Change the car** at the top of the booking.

1. Choose the new car. Only cars free for the whole booking are listed, each with its new total and the difference.
2. Say why the car changes, then press **Change the car**.
3. The price comes from the new car''s rate sheet (its rates, the km included and the rate per km). The coverage, the drivers and the add-ons stay as they are.
4. An offer is sent again with the new car: that offer is the renter''s one email.
5. On a confirmed booking, more to pay is left open: the renter sees **Pay the balance** on their booking, or you send a pay link or charge the saved card from Money. Less to pay becomes a refund that waits for approval, with a To do for Finance. The renter gets one email, **Booking updated**, with the new car and the money.
6. The open handover and return jobs move to the new car. The agreement gets a new version for the renter to sign; its link goes by text.
7. The booking''s history and the audit log keep who changed it, from which car, to which car and why.

Customer service and Admins change any of them; Sales changes a request or an offer; Fleet changes a confirmed booking. Once the car is out, use **Swap vehicle** instead.

## The accident card of a booking

Every booking from confirmation to the return shows its **Accident card**: the steps after an accident and the coverage this booking uses.

- OPCF 27: the renter''s own insurer and policy number, from the proof they uploaded.
- Credit card coverage: the card and its coverage provider, from their proof.
- Protection Plan: the provider, the policy number and the claims phone from Settings > Program (Tolls and damage), with the renter''s plan reference.

Press **Print the card** for the printable card. The renter has the same card on their booking. It never shows the fleet policy.

## Close ended trips

A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.

**Bookings** shows a banner when trips have ended and are not closed; **Close ended trips** lists each one: never picked up in the system, on rent after the return, or returned and never closed. Fleet and Finance have the same page.

1. Tick one or several, then **Mark them**: returned on time, returned late (give the time it came back), or a no-show (an Admin or customer service).
2. Choose the deposit: **Deduct the balance owed**, **Deduct the late fee**, or **Release in full**. A card hold that has expired is marked settled at once (released by expiry: no money moves).
3. If no deposit was taken, an Admin fills **Admin: deposit not taken, waive it because** (the same field is in Record a past trip).
4. Nothing is released by itself: the decision waits under **Deposit decisions waiting for an Admin**, and an Admin presses **Release** (or **Release now (tolls window)**).

## Return charges

A late return is charged per started extra day at the booking''s full daily cost (the rental per day after discounts, plus per-day and per-trip fees such as the Protection Plan, never delivery), and only the started hours after the whole days get the hourly late fee. On the booking''s **Money** tab, each renter line not on a statement yet has **Change amount** (lower) and **Waive**, with the reason; it is in the booking history and the next assessment keeps it. An expired card hold after the return has **Mark settled (released by expiry)**.

## The Protection Plan priced from RentalCover (release 35)

The Protection Plan stays our product: renters never see the RentalCover name. Without the RentalCover partner key it is priced from the Protection Plan table, as before. Once the key is set, its price comes from a real RentalCover quote for the renter (their dates, their age at pickup, their name and email) plus our markup (20% unless **Settings** > **Program** changes it). The request form asks for the quote once the renter''s details are in, and an offer as you choose option 3; a quote is reused for 15 minutes. A price you type for the plan wins. If RentalCover does not answer, the table price applies.

RentalCover covers up to $50,000 an incident, so the plan is offered only for a car worth less. The value used: your override under **Value for the Protection Plan** on the car''s page when set, else the car''s Canadian Black Book value, else an AI estimate from typical listing prices that the site makes by itself (**Refresh the AI estimate** asks again). A car with no value counts as over the limit: the request form, the offer screen and the database then offer only OPCF 27 or credit card coverage.

## Extensions at the all-in price a day (release 35)

An extension costs what the renter already pays, averaged per day: the booking''s total for the booked period (the rental after discounts, every fee, one-time fees like delivery included, and HST) divided by its days, for each added day. A booking of $729.36 for 7 days costs $104.19 for each added day. Added hours under a day cost the hourly late fee with HST, never more than a day. There is no extension discount.

| Where | What happens |
| --- | --- |
| The renter''s **Extend** page | Each option shows the total and the price a day before paying |
| **Edit** on a confirmed or on-trip booking, made longer | The booking''s new total is the all-in price of the longer stay; the per-trip fees stay as booked and the rental charge takes the difference |
| The next period of a long rental | Keeps the rate of the booked period (the rental a day, per-trip fees scaled) |
| An insurer-billed booking | Priced as before |

The extension is one line on the booking, "Extension: 3 days at $104.19/day (all-in)", HST included. Its HST is the booking''s own share of HST, so invoices and the books never add HST on top. Type a rental charge in **Edit** to set another price. Late returns are unchanged: the daily cost of each extra day and the hourly late fee.

## A fixed amount per payment (release 35)

On a weekly, every 2 weeks or monthly plan, an Admin can set **Fixed amount per payment** in **Change the plan**. Each payment is that amount and the last one takes the remainder. The total and the payments already made never change. Leave it empty to split the payments by the days again.

## The request as sent and every offer (release 35)

On a request or a booking, **Original request, as the renter sent it** shows the car, dates, places, coverage, add-ons, note and the price the renter saw, exactly as sent; staff changes never touch it. **Offer history** lists every offer version, newest first: its status, who sent it and when, the car and dates, the message, how the total moved, and the price breakdown.

1. To go back to an old version, press **Revert to this offer** on it. Its car, dates, price, deposit, discount and fees load into the review as a new offer, highlighted.
2. Check the price, then send it in step 3. Nothing changes until you send.

The **Coverage** line at the top says what the renter chose (own insurance OPCF 27, credit card, Protection Plan) and its proof: not sent yet, waiting for review, confirmed, or rejected with the reason.

## Send an offer in three steps (release 35)

1. **Car and dates**: the renter, the dates, the car and where they pick it up and return it.
2. **Price**: filled in from the rate sheet with the checkout''s fees and discounts. Change it only if you agreed another price.
3. **Review and send**: what changed, the message and how the link goes.

Rarely used options (billing an insurer, how it is paid, the calendar) are under **More options**. Send waits while the price is being worked out again after a date change, and one tap sends once.

## The owner''s own trip, instant bookings and Book it now (release 35)

- **Owner''s own trip ($0)**: the owner booked their own car. There is nothing to price or send; get the car ready.
- **Instant (repeat renter)**: a Gold renter or above (Rewards, release 40) with a verified licence and nothing owing booked an available car at once and went straight to sign and pay. An Admin can take a renter''s instant booking away from the booking page.
- **Any car, any time** (release 40): a Platinum renter asked for dates the car shows as taken. Fleet gets an urgent task due within 4 hours: confirm it, offer an equivalent car or an upgrade, or decline with a reason. Never cancel or move another renter''s confirmed booking for it. The task closes when the request is answered.
- **Book it now** pressed by staff waits for an Admin''s one-tap approval.

## Secondary contact and rideshare documents (release 35)

The booking shows the renter''s **Secondary contact** when they gave one: call them when the renter cannot be reached. Rideshare and delivery driving are welcome (rental agreement, section 10.3): never tell a renter it is not allowed. When a renter makes **rideshare documents** (Uber, Lyft, DoorDash and others), you get an alert and the booking shows the letters they made.

## Offers, coverage, delivery and fuel (releases 35 and 36)

- Sending an offer is three steps: car and dates, price, review and send. Every request shows the renter''s original request as sent and every offer version, with who sent it and when; reverting loads an old version as a new offer to send.
- Instant booking: a verified Gold renter or above books an available car at once, signs and pays; the booking is marked Instant (repeat renter), and an Admin can take instant booking away from a renter.
- Card coverage is checked against the car: the card, the car''s value, its type and the rental length. A card that does not cover it cannot be approved. OPCF 27 needs both the pink slip and the endorsement page.
- Delivery is priced by distance from the company''s address (1570 Midland Ave, Scarborough): a base, the kilometres included and a rate per km, all in Program settings; a car''s own fee stays as an override.
- The fuel line at the return is suggested from the car''s tank, the weekly pump price and a multiplier, plus the refuelling fee, and checked on the deposit review before any charge.
- Owner price limits: the daily minimum and maximum of a car or an owner hold every price, discount and offer; only an Admin can allow one request outside them, with a reason.
- Rideshare and delivery work is allowed with the documents the renter makes on their booking page (rental agreement copy, coverage letter, vehicle letter); staff get an alert when they are made. The secondary contact shows on the booking.
- Mid-trip review ask: halfway through a trip of several days, the renter gets one short message asking how it is going; a problem they report becomes a To do for customer service.
- A car that has only test bookings can be deleted by an Admin; the test bookings go with it. A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.', 'Requests, offers and bookings', 'See what is out, coming back and owed now; send an offer with or without a request, change it in place, take payments by part, run a booking.',
  'A booking starts as a request from the website, or as an offer you send yourself to a customer on the phone. You check it, adjust it and send the offer; an offer that is out is changed in place. After that, the booking page holds the money, documents, changes and history.

## Bookings now: what is out, coming back and owed

Open **Bookings**. It opens on **Now**, one screen that refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. Every time is Toronto time.

1. The numbers at the top: cars out now, due back today, overdue, going out in the next 72 hours, payments due in the next 7 days (with the total) and free cars. Tap one to jump to its list.
2. **Out now**: every car on rent, overdue returns first in red. Each shows the car (photo, code, plate), the renter with **Call** and **Text**, when it was picked up, when it is due back with a countdown, the payment plan and the next payment, the deposit held, and the km and fuel at pickup. Filter by Overdue, Due today or Payment due.
3. A confirmed booking whose pickup time has passed with no check-in recorded is listed as out, with **Out (pickup not recorded)**. The car most likely left. Press **Mark picked up**: it records the pickup at the booked time (change it if the car left at another time), the booking goes on rent, and Fleet gets a task to add the photos, km and fuel. The usual checks stay: the deposit taken (or an Admin waives it with the reason), the renter''s signature (or an Admin''s reason), the agreement''s details, every driver verified and the coverage confirmed. If one is missing, the reason is shown.
4. **Coming back**: overdue, today and tomorrow, by the time each is due.
5. **Going out**: confirmed pickups in the next 72 hours, delivery or pickup, with ticks and crosses for the licence, the signed agreement, the payment, the deposit (a clock until the morning of the pickup day, when the hold is placed on the card on file) and the check-in photos (done at the handover).
6. **Money due**: every rental payment due in the next 7 days or overdue, the amount, the plan and which payment it is (for example 3 of 4).
7. **Free now**: cars available and not out, the longest idle first, with the next pickup; then the cars in maintenance or cleaning. Partners'' cars are counted apart.

> Good to know: Placeholder bookings never show on Now.

### Payment plans

A rental is paid in full at pickup, weekly, every 2 weeks, or monthly. A rental longer than one period (30 days) pays each period by itself. To change it, open the booking, then the **Payment plan** card on Overview or Money, and press **Change the plan**. Each payment is its share of the total by its days, due on the day it starts. An insurer-billed rental shows **Insurer billed** and is never in Money due unless the renter owes a part. Admins, customer service and finance change the plan; fleet sees it.

## All bookings

The **All bookings** tab of Bookings has the search (booking number, name, email, phone, plate or car code), the status (All, Out now, Booked, Returned, Cancelled; closed bookings are found with the search, which also finds the insurer). **Out now** shows the bookings on rent and those whose pickup passed without a check-in, together. Each booking is one row: its number and status in plain words, the car with its photo, the renter with **Call** and **Text**, the dates, the money (paid up, to pay, overdue, insurer billed) and Bill to.

## The request queue

Open **Bookings** > **Requests and offers**. The oldest waiting request is at the top.

1. The numbers at the top: waiting for an offer, past the reply target (red), offers out, accepted but not paid, and offers expired. Each one is a filter: press it and the list shows just those, with the matching chip below marked as chosen.
2. One queue, the most urgent first: the longest wait, then offers accepted but not paid, then offers out by when they expire. Each row has the car with its photo, the dates, the price, the renter with **Call** and **Text**, the licence (verified, to review, or not uploaded yet), who is answering it, and one button: **Send offer**, **Follow up** or **Open**. **Decline** sits beside **Send offer**.
3. Waiting shows how long the renter has waited ("12 min", "3 h", "2 days"); red means past the first reply target (5 minutes, set in Program settings). **Promise** counts down the 2 hours the site promises the renter.
4. Filter by Active, New, Changes asked, Offer out, Accepted, not paid or Expired. The list remembers your last choice on that device; **Active** always shows the whole queue and replaces what it remembered. When the same renter asks for the same car for overlapping dates again and the earlier request or offer expired, only the newest is listed: the older ones are linked to it and leave Requests (they keep their history). An expired offer leaves the active queue 48 hours after it expired, or once its pickup time passed; Expired lists the ones from the last 7 days. After 7 days an expired offer leaves Requests and offers and becomes a renter lead, once, in People > Renters > Leads (Expired offers), with the car and the dates the renter wanted and a To do for Sales to win them back. An offer still out when its pickup time passes expires by itself.

![](/guides/img/admin-02-requests-desktop-6521282d.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 820; address: carmacars.ca/admin/requests; pins: 1 38.9 29.9, 2 22.2 43.3")

> Good to know: A request whose pickup time passes without an offer expires by itself, with a note in its history. The renter is not emailed unless "Email the renter when their request expires that way" is on in Program settings.

## Answer a request with an offer

1. The Review and offer tab shows the request as the renter sent it.
2. Adjust the car, the dates, the rate type, the places, the rates (under **Show rate card**) and fees, the deposit and extras. A place changed away from a delivery or a collection takes its fee box and its fee with it.
3. Price on the right updates as you change things.
4. Add a message, choose how long the offer stays open, then press **Send the offer**.

![](/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-353f3707.jpg "desktop; size: 1200 1550; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review; pins: 1 5.0 6.5, 2 7.5 45.8, 3 74.2 42.6, 4 76.7 98.1")

5. Changed fields but not ready to send? Press **Save changes**. The panel "The offer as the renter sees it" shows the result.
6. Can''t do it? Press **Decline** and fill in Reason and any alternative.
7. Need an answer first? Press **Ask the renter** to send a question.

![](/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-4dd4ed06.jpg "desktop; size: 500 80; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review; pins: 6 41.2 52.5, 7 18.0 52.5")

Opening a request takes it for you: everyone else sees "Being answered by" your name and since when, with Send the offer and Decline off, until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work; Program settings). Press **Take over** to answer one someone else holds; it is noted in the history. A second answer is refused with who answered and when. A request from the website opens to Sales after 15 minutes (Program settings); until then Admins, customer service and fleet answer it.

## Send an offer without a request

Press **Send an offer** at the top of Bookings, or **Send an offer without a request** on Requests and offers. For a customer on the phone, by text or at the counter: no request needed.

The screen is seven short steps, each with one line saying what to do, and the price beside it (on a phone the total sits at the bottom of the screen: press **See every line**). What most offers never need is under each step''s **More options**, which stays open while something in it is used.

1. **Who is renting and when**: find the renter by name, phone or email, or press **Not on file? Add a new customer** (full legal name, mobile, email for the offer link, date of birth). A customer already on file with the same email or phone is shown with Use: one person, one record. Then the pickup and the return.
2. **Which car**: search by car code, plate or name; each car says Free or Not free for the dates. More options: the rate card and the type and free-only filters.
3. **Where they pick up and return**: at our location, we deliver or collect (the address and distance), an airport or the owner''s location. The fee each one makes shows under it, Automatic or Set by hand.
4. **How damage is covered**: the renter''s own insurance, a credit card or the Protection Plan. More options: another Protection Plan price.
5. **Extras**: add-ons, when the car has any.
6. **The price**: the rate sheet price is filled in. More options: another price (a total for the trip or a rate a day, with why), Amounts I type (before or after HST), the total the renter pays, kilometres, a promo code, the deposit and a discount (an Admin), and **Fees**: press **Change** to set one by hand, **Reset to automatic** to undo it. Below: how it is paid (card online and a card hold unless you change it under More options).
7. **Send it**: who found this client (sales and customer service), a message, and Text or Email. More options: how long the offer is open, the owner''s view, who found the client (an Admin) and the internal note. Above the button, **Ready to send** or **Missing:** with what is left; press Send and each missing field says what it needs. Press **Send the offer to** the renter, or **Save without sending** to keep it as a request for later. **The offer as the renter sees it** is under the price.

> Good to know: Choices drive the charges. Take off a delivery, a collection, the Protection Plan or an add-on and its fee goes with it, even a fee set by hand: there is nothing to remove in a second place. Choose it again and the fee starts from the automatic amount.

> Good to know: It makes the same request and offer the website makes: the renter approves, signs and pays (or you record the payment), and only then is the car on the calendar. No "request received" email goes to the renter for an offer you send. Staff commissions and statements count it like any other booking.

## Change an offer that is out

The renter has the offer (Offered), or approved it and has not paid (Signing and payment). Open **More actions** on the booking and press **Edit the offer**.

1. Change anything: the car, the dates, the places, the price, fees, the deposit, add-ons, how it is paid. Each changed field is highlighted and the before and after are listed. Amounts I type (Before tax or After tax) and the Total the renter pays (after tax) work as on Send an offer.
2. Write what changed in Message to the renter and choose how long the offer is open.
3. Press **Save and send the update**: the renter gets the new version by email or text (ticked), and the old version no longer counts. Or press **Save without telling the renter** and tell them yourself.
4. A confirmed booking is changed with **Change the booking** (Propose a change, below).

> Tip: No need to withdraw first. **Withdraw the offer** is only for taking it back for good; **Send again, later expiry** gives the renter more time, and **Renter approved by phone** records a yes given on a call.

## Edit a booking that has started

On a confirmed, on-trip or returned booking (an Admin: a closed one too), Overview, **Edit the booking**, **Edit**.

1. Change the pickup or the return (extend or shorten: the rental charge is worked out again at this booking''s rates), the car (on trip: the car it leaves goes to Out of service for Fleet to check), the rental charge for the trip, each fee, the kilometres a day, the deposit (an Admin) and the note.
2. Type why, if you like, and tick **Email the renter what changed**, or leave it off for a silent correction. Press **Save the changes**.
3. What is open now shows at once: **Email a pay link** or **Text a pay link** for exactly that amount, **Charge** the saved card (the renter agreed), or record cash or an e-Transfer on the Money tab.

> Good to know: Each edit is kept with who, when, why, before and after (Edits, under the form) and in the booking''s history. A closed booking''s owner split and the staff commission follow. To have the renter accept and sign first, use Propose a change instead.

## Fees, a forgotten fee and the balance

On the booking''s Money tab, Fees lists each fee. Press **Change or add a fee**.

1. Type a new amount (for the whole trip, before HST) beside any fee, or choose one not on the booking (the young driver fee shows its price for these dates), or add a charge of its own with or without HST.
2. Press **Save the fees**. The balance shows by part (rental, fees) with the pay link, the saved card and Record a payment beside it.
3. The renter sees the balance on their booking with a Pay button, and pays by card on Stripe''s form.

> Good to know: Every change is recorded (Changes to the fees): the amount before and after, who and why. Customer service and sales may change fees while Program settings, Staff may change fees, is on.

## A renter with only a debit or prepaid card

A credit card is required by default: the deposit must be on a credit card so the deductible can be charged. The pay page tells a renter with only a debit or prepaid card to contact us.

1. On the booking''s Money tab, press **Allow debit and prepaid cards for this booking** and type the reason. Who and when are kept, and the change is in the booking''s history.
2. The booking''s pay page, staff pay links and deposit hold then take a debit or prepaid card, and the renter is told the hold lowers the money available on the card until it is released, which can take several business days.
3. **Require a credit card again** turns it off.

The Money tab shows each card used and its type (credit, debit, prepaid). A booking on credit card rental coverage is always paid on the credit card that carries the coverage, and cannot be allowed. Program settings, **Card types accepted**, can open debit and prepaid cards to every booking.

## Correct a renter''s details

On the renter''s page (People, Renters) or on any of their bookings, **Edit renter**.

1. Correct the name, email, phone, date of birth, licence, home address (start typing to find it) or the staff note.
2. A new email also becomes their sign-in at once (no confirmation needed for a typo you correct); tick **Email the renter a link to set a password** to send one there. Unsigned agreements and offers go to the new address.
3. Press **Save the renter**. An email that another renter has is refused with their name; the same phone is a warning.
4. The same person entered twice? Possible duplicates (same email, same phone, or same name and date of birth) shows under the renter. **Merge into this record** moves the other record''s bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages here and fills any detail missing here; the other record stays, blocked, with the merge in both histories.

## The Money tab: Rental charges and Security deposit

The booking''s Money tab opens on a strip with the three numbers that matter: **Rental due**, **Deposit** (one word: Not collected, Held, Charged, Released or Partly kept) and **Total paid**. Below are two panels, side by side on a computer and one above the other on a phone. Collecting one never touches the other, and every receipt says which one it is.

**Rental charges**: each line of the price and the total, Paid, then Balance due.

1. The one main button, Collect (the amount) rental: choose how. **The card on file** charges it now (Finance or an Admin); **A payment link by text** or **A payment link by email** sends the renter Stripe''s secure form; **On this device: hand it to the renter** opens it for the renter to type; **Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)** records money received (an e-Transfer, cheque or transfer needs its reference). For: the rental and fees together by default, or one of them. With the card on file, the rental and fees together are one charge with one receipt that lists both (the rental is paid first, then the fees; an insurer''s part and money already received another way are left out). The renter gets a receipt; **Print** prints one to hand over.
2. **A later charge** (before the return): on the card on file, by a link, on this device, or recorded. Choose the **Reason** from the list (Mileage overage, Fuel, Cleaning, Smoking, Late return, Tolls, Tickets/fines, Damage, Missing items, Other) and add a note; Other needs its note. The renter''s receipt shows the reason.
3. **Save a card** saves the renter''s card without charging it. Card readers, the fees (**Change or add a fee**), failed card payments (**Paid another way**), payments received another way and **Refund** sit in this panel too. The history lists rental payments only.
4. An offer paid another way: once the renter approved and signed and the money is recorded, the booking is confirmed (or press **Confirm the booking**).

**Security deposit**: the amount, how it is taken (a credit card hold, a debit or prepaid card at the standard multiple, a charge, or cash), its status in one word and the next step.

1. Not collected: the one main button, Collect (the amount) deposit. **Hold on the card on file** places the hold now (Finance or an Admin); **A deposit hold link by text** or **A deposit hold link by email**, or **A hold on this device: hand it to the renter**; **Charge the card on file as the deposit** only when no hold can be placed; **Cash or e-Transfer (record it)**. The rental balance is not touched.
2. Before every pickup the deposit hold link is texted to the renter on its own: 24 hours before (at once when the pickup is sooner), for a confirmed booking whose deposit is a card hold with no hold yet. The panel says **Deposit link texted** and when it was opened. No mobile number, or the text not sent: a task **Deposit link not sent**. **Settings**, then Site settings, Deposit link by text: on or off, and the hours.
3. Held, while the car is out: **Release** (an Admin, with the reason), **Keep part (damage/fees)** with the amount and the reason from the list, or **Re-authorize the hold** on the saved card before it lapses (the panel shows when the hold expires). A job re-authorizes it by itself about 24 hours before it expires; if it cannot, Finance and the Admins get the alert **Deposit hold not re-authorized**.
4. **Hold expired**: a card hold lasts about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise. Once it has expired, nothing can be kept from it: the panel says Hold expired, Keep and Release are hidden, and **Charge the card on file instead** opens the later charge with the amount and the reason filled in.
4. After the return: **Settle the deposit** (below).
5. **Waive the deposit** (an Admin, before it is taken), **Change the debit deposit**, and **Allow debit and prepaid cards for this booking** sit in this panel. The history lists deposit payments only.
6. A deposit taken in cash or by e-Transfer is given back the same way after the return: Finance gets a task; press **Returned** with the reference or receipt number.

> Good to know: Statements, reconciliation and the deposit settlement read each payment with its method: a cash deposit is never refunded to a card.

## Settle the deposit

The deposit is never given back by itself. Finance or an Admin settles it after the return: on the booking''s Money tab, under Deposit, press **Settle the deposit**. Issue the Check-out statement first.

1. The form shows the deposit, what is still available, the charges owed from the statement and what is taken from the deposit for them. What the deposit does not cover is charged to the card on file; with no card (or a card declined), the renter gets a pay link by email and text, and Finance has a task until it is paid.
2. Tolls and tickets can take up to 7 days to come in. Inside that window the whole rest of the deposit is filled in as the hold-back, until the window ends. To give it back sooner, tick Release now anyway: a toll that comes in later is charged to the card on file.
3. Something still open keeps the whole deposit: an incident, a claim, new damage at the return not priced, damage found later not billed, a toll or ticket on the car during the rental not matched or not charged, a card dispute, or charges not on a statement yet. The form lists them. Only an Admin can release part of it, with the reason; it is recorded.
4. Damage: **Keep the whole deposit (damage)** turns what is left of the deposit into a damage charge, with what was damaged and the photos; the renter is told. **Bill damage** adds a damage charge up to the $2,500 deductible (more goes through a claim): the deposit pays first, then the card on file.
5. Press **Settle**. The money moves at Stripe at once: the charges are collected and what is not owed is refunded or the hold released. A step Stripe refuses is tried again by itself, and Finance gets a task if it keeps failing.

> Good to know: A card hold lapses after about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise. While the car is out, or returned and not settled, the hold is collected in full a day and a half before it lapses: that keeps the money, and the settlement refunds what is not owed. A hold that lapses anyway is charged to the saved card, and Finance is told at once.

## A booking

Open **Bookings** > **Bookings**, then a booking number. Or type the number in the search box.

1. Tabs: Overview, Money, Changes, History, and Drivers and documents.
2. Overview shows the trip, the renter, what is still missing for the handover, and the price.
3. Open tasks for this booking, with the queue and the due time.
4. Top right: **Email the renter** and **More actions**, the menu with **Edit the offer**, **Stop blocking the calendar**, **Cancel for the renter**, **Cancel by CarmaCars** and the rest.
5. Under the booking number: **Next step**, what happens next and who does it, with one button for that step (for example **Send the offer**, **Sign on this device** or **Check in the car**); then where the booking is on its way, from Request to Closed, with the dates, the days, the total and who pays.

![](/guides/img/admin-04-booking-desktop-b56b668a.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 960; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065; pins: 2 50.0 46.6, 4 85.4 14.5, 5 22.9 26.8")

## Check a car out or in

From the booking, with your phone or a tablet: the same checklist field staff use.

1. A confirmed booking shows **Check in (pickup)** under Check-in, check-out and signing; a booking on rent shows **Check out (return)**. Today lists the check-ins and check-outs due, each with **Check in** or **Check out**.
2. The checklist opens: the ready check, the renter and their licence and card, the odometer (km) and fuel or charge, the keys, the photo set (every side, the wheels, the interior, the odometer and fuel gauge, the plate), damage marks with close-ups, then the renter and you sign.
3. Photos wait on the device without a connection and upload in the background. Each keeps its time, and the place when the device allows location.
4. A field job of the booking is taken over (the history says so); with no job, one is made for you. When done, press **See the photo report**.

> Tip: Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in the same way from their own booking page.

## The photo report, late returns and the return charges

Under Check-in, check-out and signing, press **Photo report**.

1. The report shows the due-back time, the actual check-in and check-out, Late by (or Overdue by while the car is out), the odometer and kilometres over the allowance, the fuel or charge out and in, every photo with its time and place, and the damage.
2. At check-out the mileage overage and the fuel or recharging are written to the return charges at once. A late return (after the grace period of the fee defaults) is not: it waits for a choice on the booking (see "A late return is a choice"). The fuel is a suggested line: the car''s tank x the fuel missing x the pump price of its grade (Program settings, updated weekly) x 1.25, plus the refuelling fee; an electric car the battery kWh x the charge missing x the price a kWh, plus the fee. A pump receipt entered later replaces it. Fleet and Finance confirm it on the deposit review; it is never charged to a card by itself.
3. Not charging one? Press **Waive** beside it and give the reason: it stays waived if the charges are worked out again.
4. The time was wrong? Press **Correct the check-out time** (or the check-in time) with the reason: lateness follows, a return that is no longer late loses its late charge, and the history keeps both times.
5. The renter gets the same report (without these buttons) by email and in their Documents. Late by shows on the booking and in the Bookings list.

### The renter says the car is back

Every overdue email, text and alert (at the return time, at 15 minutes and the final notice) has a one-tap **I''ve returned the car** link, and the renter''s booking page has the button. The renter can add photos, the odometer, the fuel level and the time they returned it. Sending it stops every overdue notice of the booking at once, the booking shows **Returned, waiting for confirmation**, and Fleet gets an urgent To do: "The renter says the car is back".

1. Open the booking. The card **The renter says the car is back** shows what the renter gave, marked renter-provided, with their photos.
2. Check the car: the return place, the tracker, the photos.
3. Press **Confirm** to complete the trip. Correct the odometer, fuel or return time first if they are wrong: the late charges follow the time you confirm. The renter''s photos join the check-out report.
4. Or press **Deny** and say why. The renter gets your reason by email and text, and the overdue notices start again.

Checking the car in the usual way also completes the trip and stops the notices. Admins, Fleet, Sales, Customer service and field staff can Confirm or Deny.

## Signatures on the spot, or by link

The renter or an additional driver signs the rental agreement on your device, or on their own phone.

1. While a signature is missing, the booking shows **Sign now on this device**, **Email the signing link** and **Text the signing link**.
2. No agreement made yet (the renter has not saved their details at home)? **Sign now on this device** still shows: press **Prepare the agreement to sign now** and it is made on the spot.
3. **Sign now on this device**: confirm the name matches their licence and that you saw the original licence (photograph it if none is on file), then press **Hand the device to** and their name.
4. They read both agreements (CarmaCars'' and Blind Spot''s), tick the statements and sign. Then **Back to the staff view** for the next signer.
5. The record is the same as signing online, and says it was signed in person, collected by you, on your device. It is printed on the signed copy''s signature record page.

## Rental agreements: every version, every field

The booking''s Rental agreements card: the current version of CarmaCars'' and Blind Spot''s agreements, every earlier one, and what is still blank.

1. Once the agreement is signed and countersigned, any change to what it prints makes a new version of both documents by itself: the dates, the price lines, the car, a driver added or corrected, the coverage, the deposit or how it was paid, an address.
2. A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage option is signed again: the renter (and each driver it affects) gets their link by email and text, and the card shows "Agreement v3 waiting for signature". A correction (a typo in an address, a plate written differently) is filed without signing; the renter gets the corrected copy by email.
3. Check-in makes the "as picked up" copy (time out, km out, fuel out, the car''s plate and VIN, the check-in report), countersigned by whoever checked the car out; check-out makes the closing copy (time in, km in, driven and charged, fuel in, late hours, damage, the return charges, the final totals). Both go to the renter by email.
4. **Every version** lists each one with what changed and both PDFs. **Resend the signing links**, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your phone or tablet.
5. The card lists what the agreements still print blank (a licence expiry, the insurer''s policy number, the insured vehicle, a VIN). Type the values and press **Save the missing fields**: the agreements follow.
6. Check-in stops while a field a claim needs is blank. An Admin can let it go ahead: type the reason and press **Override**; the reason is in the booking''s history.
7. **Make the agreements again** checks both against the booking at once (they also follow every change by themselves).
8. **Edit the wording** (Admin only) changes CarmaCars'' agreement text for this booking: press **Change** beside a clause, edit its text, say why and press **Save the wording**; **Add** writes Additional terms at the end of Part 2. Only clauses not required by law or the insurer can be removed; the consents are fixed, and Blind Spot''s form (the insurer''s official form) is never changed. Before the renter signs, the agreement is made again; after, the change is a new version they sign, and **Every version** shows each clause before and after.

## Signing that holds up in a dispute

Every signature on the site is made the same way: rental agreements, amendments and new versions (remotely or on your device), and the owner agreements, schedules and forms, a co-owner''s link, the partner, investment and staff agreements.

1. The licence on file is shown. A 6-digit code to their phone or email on file is optional: the signer may press **Verify by code (optional)**, and Program settings, E-signing, **ask for a one-time code** makes it a required first step again (off by default). Without the code, the certificate says the identity was not confirmed by a code.
2. They say they read the documents, initial the key terms (each initials box is saved with **Save initials**; **Clear** takes it back to initial again) (damage and the deductible, the deposit and later charges, fuel, kilometres and late returns, their coverage, cancellation), give three consents (to sign electronically, to receive records electronically, to card charges under the agreement) and draw their signature.
3. Owners, partners, investors and staff do the same for their documents: the code, the reading, the key terms of their documents initialled (for example the Enrollment Agreement''s three confirmations, Form C''s acknowledgments, Schedule C, the staff agreement''s confidentiality), two consents and the drawn signature. Form C''s witness still types their name beside the owner.
4. Each step is recorded with its time, IP address and device, and the place when the device shares it. The signed PDFs end with a certificate of completion; anyone can check a signed file at `carmacars.ca/verify`.
5. Typed names are off. For a signer who cannot draw, an Admin can turn on the accessibility fallback: **Settings** > **Program**, Esign typed fallback.

## Card disputes: the evidence pack

Everything that proves the rental, in one PDF for Stripe.

1. When a card payment is disputed, the evidence pack is built by itself: the signed agreements with their certificates, the check-in and check-out reports with photos, kilometres and fuel, the licence, the payments and charges, every message to the renter, and the card checks from Stripe. It is staged in Stripe as the dispute''s evidence, and To do gets an urgent task.
2. Open the booking: the Rental agreements card shows the pack. Press **Download** to check it, then **Submit to Stripe** before the evidence date.
3. **Build the dispute evidence pack** makes one at any time (an Admin or Finance).

## The licence before an offer is accepted

Front, back and a selfie, from the request on.

1. After sending a request the renter is asked for their licence. A licence already on file from an earlier booking is used again while it is valid after the return.
2. The offer cannot be accepted (by the renter, or by you on their word) and nothing is paid until the licence and its expiry date are on file.
3. Review the images as usual with **Review documents**: the card Renter documents is on Review and offer too.
4. The switch is in **Settings** > **Program**, Booking requests and offers: Booking licence required (on), with the selfie (on).

## The licence reader

Every licence photo is read on upload: the back''s barcode first, else the vision model (within the day''s AI allowance).

1. The renter''s empty licence fields are filled from the read; the renter confirms them. A blurry or cut-off photo is taken again at once.
2. **Review documents** shows what was read and one line per check, Pass or Flag: photos, valid to the return, class accepted, age at pickup, name and date of birth, the Ontario number, front and back, and the main driver''s Ontario licence. Staff still approve.
3. **Settings** > **Program**, Driver''s licence reader: **Approve automatically when every check passes** (off). On: a driver whose front and back both read sharp and every check passes is approved in your name; anything flagged waits for a person.
4. **Primary driver must hold an Ontario licence** (on): a main driver with a licence from elsewhere becomes an additional driver, the booking needs "Primary driver: Ontario licence needed" and pickup is blocked. The renter adds a main driver, who signs on their own link. On the document review, **Admin: undo or let it go**: undo puts the first main driver back; let it go needs a reason.

> Tip: What was read is staff only and is deleted with the licence image. The licence number is never written to the logs.

## Renter documents: licence and proof of coverage

A renter''s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage (OPCF 27 or a credit card''s rental coverage) are checked before the handover. You check them yourself; no task is needed.

1. A booking with documents waiting is a line on To do: "Check ''s documents for booking ", marked Now when the pickup is within two days. Press **Review documents**.
2. The pop-up shows each driver''s images and the coverage: the insurer, policy number and expiry, or the card, its type and whether the name matches.
3. What to check is written once at the top. One wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**: they are asked for a new one.
4. Then press **Approve all**: every image, the proof of coverage and the Protection Plan still waiting are approved in one step. The number in the button is exactly what it approves (an image whose file was removed is not counted), and an image not tied to a driver of the booking is listed under **Other documents**. Anything the system refuses is named with the reason.
5. The same pop-up is on the booking: the card Renter documents (**Review documents**) on Overview and on Drivers and documents.

> Tip: Each opening of a renter''s documents is logged. The links to the images last one minute. Field staff can also check a licence in person at the check-in (photos and four checks): the history says "checked in person". Field staff also review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from My jobs, with the same Approve all or a reason to reject: the history says the reviewer''s role, field. Sales review the licence images (not the coverage) of any booking being arranged or under way from their To do or the booking, with the same Approve all or a reason to reject: the history says the role, sales.

## Payments by day

**Money** > **Payments**, the **By day** tab: every payment and refund of a day or a range, by method, the cash drawer and the refunds waiting. Finance has the same screen.

1. Choose From and To and the methods (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer, bank transfer, pre-authorized debit, other), then press **Show**.
2. Totals by method and for each day; cards read as the card and its last four digits, never a code.
3. The cash drawer: expected (cash in less cash given back) against the count Finance records with **Record the count**; a difference shows over or short.
4. Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere with the policy maths. **Approve** or **Decline** with the reason in the row, then **Issue the refund**.
5. **Export CSV** for the bookkeeper.

## Propose a change to a confirmed booking

The renter gets an email and answers on their booking. The calendar moves only when they accept.

1. Open the booking''s Changes tab. Under Propose a change, set the new pickup, return or car.
2. To price it by hand, type a New rental charge before tax. Leave it empty to use the car''s rates.
3. Write the Reason, for the renter. They read it.
4. Press **Preview the price**, then **Send to the renter**.

![](/guides/img/admin-05-booking-changes-desktop-97008b21.jpg "desktop; size: 1200 520; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065?tab=changes; pins: 1 17.5 33.7, 2 9.2 50.0, 3 38.3 71.2, 4 12.9 91.9")

## Who a booking is credited to

Overview (and Review and offer) shows the Sales credit: the staff member the booking counts for in their sales.

1. A quote or a rental is credited to whoever created or added it. A request from the website is credited to whoever sent its first offer.
2. To give it to someone else, press **Reassign**, choose who (or Nobody), say whether they sourced the client and write the reason. The booking''s history and the audit log keep it, and the deal stays in the same week and month.
3. Sourced means the staff member chose I sourced this client when they entered it, it came with a field staff referral link, or you credited it. Only a sourced booking earns a staff commission. A website request earns none unless you credit someone.
4. Someone said they sourced a website request? The credit line shows the claim: press **Credit them** or **Not theirs**, with a reason.
5. A price typed by hand shows beside the rate-sheet price, with the reason. A price under the floor or past the discount limit is flagged: press **Mark reviewed** once you have looked at it.

> Good to know: A request keeps the lead-time adjustment of the moment it came in ("Short-notice pricing +10%" or "Booked ahead −5%"), through the offer and the payment. To change it, open the booking''s review screen, **More options**, **Lead-time pricing (%)**: a number (0 for none), or empty for the tier of the request. A price typed by hand replaces it.

> Good to know: The rental never goes below the car''s minimum daily rate or above its maximum (its price limits, set by the owner or on the car''s Rates tab), whatever the discount, promo code or lead-time pricing: a line "Minimum daily rate for this car" or "Maximum daily rate for this car" brings it back. Only an Admin allows a price outside them: **More options**, **Allow a price outside the car''s price limits (Admin only)**, with the reason.

> Tip: The renter has 48 hours to accept (and sign the amendment) or decline, with one reminder. Any extra is charged to their Card on File; a lower price raises a refund for your approval.

## Review requests

Every renter is asked for a review by email and text, as they chose, only from 9 am to 9 pm Toronto time. Nothing needs setting up.

| Message | When |
| --- | --- |
| Mid-trip check | Rentals of 2 days or more, 24 hours after the pickup: "How is the car? Reply or call if anything is off." No review ask. |
| Review request | 1 hour after the check-out. It links the review page: the renter taps what they liked, adds a sentence, and gets a short draft to copy and post on Google. |
| Reminder | 24 hours after the request. |
| Final follow-up | 7 days after the request. Nothing more after it. |

1. The booking page has the card Review requests: each message with when it went or when it will go, and why it stopped.
2. **Ask for a review** sends the request now (or at 9 am if it is later than 9 pm), on any booking on a trip, returned or closed. Not twice in 24 hours.
3. On hold: a return or later charge (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls and tickets) is not settled or waived, or an incident or dispute is open. The request goes by itself once they are. Press **Send anyway** to send it now.
4. **Mark reviewed** stops the messages when the renter tells you they already reviewed.

The messages also stop by themselves when the renter presses "I already left a review", leaves a review on the site, unsubscribes, or a Google review is matched to them. **Bookings** > **Reviews** has the numbers (requests sent, on hold, reviews detected, the average rating), the hold list and the Google reviews to match.

> Tip: The draft is made only from what the renter picked and wrote, and from the booking (the car, how long, delivery or pickup). Everyone gets the Google link, whatever their stars; a renter who gives 3 stars or fewer also sees "Something wasn''t right? Tell us directly".

## What the owner sees, and owner deductions

Each booking on an owner''s or partner''s car shows the card What the owner sees at the top of its page.

1. **Hide from the owner** keeps the booking''s revenue from the owner until the car is returned, or until the owner statement covering it is approved. The owner sees the booking as Booked with its dates, and the calendar still shows the car busy. Add a reason if you like: it is kept in the history.
2. **Show to the owner** shows it now. Approving the statement shows every hidden booking on it by itself.
3. Not shown to the owner is for a booking with no owner revenue (an insurance placeholder, a shareholder''s or the owner''s own use at no charge): the owner sees only that the car is unavailable for those dates. A booking with revenue cannot be set this way.
4. Add a rental and Send an offer have What the owner sees. It starts from Settings > Program, Owners and fleet: Owners see a booking''s revenue (right away by default).
5. On the Money tab, Owner deductions on this booking: **Add a booking expense** (cleaning, repair, fuel, platform fee or other, the amount, the reason the owner reads, a receipt number) comes off before Owner Revenue.
6. **Set the Revenue Share for this booking** applies within the car''s signed terms. Above the terms only an Admin can, with Above the signed terms ticked and the reason. **Back to the car''s terms** undoes it.
7. Add a rental has the same under The car''s owner.

> Good to know: The owner''s statement carries each booking that counts toward the owner''s revenue, at its true amounts, and lists each deduction with its reason, so the payout is always right. A booking billed to the renter always counts. Left out: a booking billed to an insurer and hidden from the owner (while Program settings keep only insurance replacements hidden), an insurer-billed rental that does not block the calendar, and a rental with "Counts toward the owner''s revenue" off. The booking page says when a booking is not part of the owner''s revenue and why. When a booking that was left out starts counting (Blocks the calendar turned on, shown to the owner, or billed to the renter), the owner gets the new booking email once, at that moment. Customer service and sales add deductions only while Program settings let them change fees.

## Email the renter or the adjuster

Press **Email the renter** at the top of a booking, or open its **Messages & history** section.

1. Write a **Subject** and a **Message**, or pick a **Quick reply** to start from (Settings > Quick replies keeps them).
2. Press **Email the renter**. It goes from CarmaCars (bookings@carmacars.ca) and replies come back to the bookings inbox. The renter also sees it in their account and can answer there.
3. On a booking an insurer pays, choose **From**: CarmaCars, or Blind Spot Car Rental (insurance). **Email the adjuster** writes to the adjuster''s email on the booking (Insurance claim), always from Blind Spot Car Rental.

The **Messages & history** section is the booking''s Activity log (release 35): what you and the renter wrote, every email of the booking, the texts, chat, calls, notes, events, payments, documents and visits, newest first, with a chip for each type and a search. The email form is under the log; each email you send shows in the log with your name.

> Good to know: Emails go out through the same daily limit as every email (the line under the form shows today''s use). A message to a renter goes before digests and marketing; past the limit it waits until midnight. To write to a renter from **People** > **Renters**, open the renter: Email the renter is at the bottom, about their latest booking or the one you pick.

### Record the pickup or the return now (details later)
When the car went out or came back but the checklist could not be done (no photos, no time, the renter dropped the keys), the booking''s **Check-in, check-out and signing** card has **Record the pickup now (details later)** on a confirmed booking and **Record the return now (details later)** while the car is on rent. Give the actual time (now, or earlier), the odometer and fuel if you know them, and why. The booking moves on (on rent, or returned), late return charges follow the actual time, and Fleet gets the task **Add the photos and readings for CC-...**. A car overdue or due back today also has **Returned**: on the To do list (Check-ins and check-outs today), on Bookings > Now and at the top of the booking page, which the late return alert opens. It asks only the return time (now, or earlier) and the km and fuel if you know them, and records the return the same way. Once returned, the statement can be issued and the deposit settled; releasing the deposit before the photos are in needs an Admin and a reason. A pickup without the deposit taken needs an Admin to waive it with a reason, and without the renter''s signature on the check-in report an Admin''s reason too. Later, **Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings** opens the usual checklist (photos, readings, your signature): the task closes when it is saved.

The Agreement card says **Waiting for the renter''s details** when the renter still has blanks to fill (date of birth, address, mobile, licence, coverage): their account asks for them before signing and paying. No email or text is sent.

### Find a booking
**Bookings** has one search box: type the booking number (CC-1042, cc1042 or just 1042), the renter''s or a driver''s name, an email, a phone number in any format, a plate (spaces do not matter) or a car code, then press Enter. The status filters still apply to what is found.

### Record a card payment taken outside the site
A card taken in the Stripe Dashboard, or on a card reader, is recorded on the booking''s **Money** tab with **Record card payment**.

1. Choose what it paid: **Rental and fees**, **Rental**, **Fees**, **Later charges** or **Deposit hold**, and where it was taken.
2. Type the **Last 4 digits** and the amount. A Stripe payment id (pi_... or ch_..., from the payment in the Stripe Dashboard) is optional for a payment: press **Look up** and the amount and last 4 digits are checked against Stripe.
3. Press **Record it**. A payment confirms a booking waiting for payment, as any payment does.

> Good to know: A deposit hold needs its Stripe payment id, so it can be captured or released from **Settle the deposit**. It is recorded as held, with the usual release reminders. A hold on a reader lapses after 2 days, one made online after about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise.

### Link a payment taken outside the platform
A charge or a card deposit taken in the Stripe Dashboard or through a Stripe payment link is linked to its booking by an Admin, on the booking''s **Money** tab: **Link a payment taken outside the platform**, in the rental panel or the deposit panel.

1. Paste the Stripe payment id (pi_... or ch_..., from the payment in the Stripe Dashboard). **Look up** shows what Stripe says: the amount, paid or a hold, and the card.
2. Press **Link as a rental payment** or **Link as the deposit**.

> Good to know: It must be in Canadian dollars and not already linked. A rental payment may not be more than is open for the rental and fees. A deposit must be the whole deposit: a hold waiting to be captured is kept as held (settle it as any hold), a charged deposit is kept as captured. **Money** > **Unlinked Stripe** lists, every night, the Stripe payments of the last 60 days that no booking knows, with a best guess of the booking.

### Charge or hold the deposit on the card reader
With the S700 paired (Settings > Card reader), the **Money** tab has **Charge on reader** (everything open, the rental, the fees or a later charge) and **Hold deposit on reader**. Press **Send to the reader**: the amount shows on the reader and the renter taps, inserts or swipes the card. The screen updates by itself; **Cancel** stops the reader and nothing is charged. A deposit hold is captured or released from Settle the deposit like any hold.

### Credit card coverage: the same card
When the renter''s coverage is their credit card, the whole rental (rental and fees) is paid on that same card. The Money tab says which card. Another card on the pay page is refused and refunded at once; on the reader it is refused before the money is taken; a payment by e-Transfer, cash or the like is refused; a card typed by hand needs its last 4 digits and the box **This is the same card**. Deposits and later charges can go on any card. If the renter truly has to use another card or method, press **Allow another card** and give the reason (an Admin).

## Booked as soon as the renter accepts (release 28)

A booking is booked the moment the renter approves the offer. It takes the car on every calendar, the fleet board, the car''s availability and the counts, even before the payment or the pickup is recorded. Payment and the handover show as their own badges: **Booked, payment due** and **Pickup not recorded**. The first renter to approve gets the car: any other open offer on the same car and dates goes back to Requests with a Re-offer To do.

- **Booked, payment due** To do: a booked rental still unpaid within 48 hours of its pickup. Send the pay link, charge the saved card or record the payment.
- Record the pickup To do: a pickup time that passed with nothing recorded, as before.

When you send an offer, **The offer as the renter sees it** sits right under **Send the offer**: check it before you press it.

## Changes after signing: an amended agreement, no new signature

The rental terms (section 15.4) let CarmaCars update a booking after signing: an extension, new dates or times, a price adjustment, a fee, a car swap. The signed agreement keeps applying. Each change makes a new version of the agreement marked **Amended** with the date, carrying the renter''s original signature, and the renter is sent it. Nobody is asked to sign again, except an additional driver who never signed (they sign before driving).

## Check-in and check-out on one screen

On the booking page, **Check in (pickup)** and **Check out (return)** are one screen: the time (now unless you change it), the odometer, the fuel, the photos and a note. Pick many photos at once from the camera roll or take them; tag an angle on any photo if you like. The suggested angles (front, each corner and side, rear, odometer, fuel gauge, interior front and rear, trunk, wheels, any damage) tick themselves as photos are tagged. Nothing is required but the time; the renter''s own photos are added to the same report, each marked with who took it (the renter or staff) and its angle. The one-screen checklist is the button above it.

## Type into the Blind Spot agreement

On the **Rental agreements** card, **Type into the Blind Spot agreement** shows each box as the form prints it. Change a value and **Save the corrections**: it is drawn in that box, and the insured vehicle, the claim number, the adjuster and missing km or fuel go back onto the booking. **Preview the filled form** opens it with your corrections.

## Reopen an expired offer (release 28)

An expired offer reopens in one click: **Reopen offer** on the booking or on the **Expired** filter of Requests. The renter gets the usual offer email and text; the offer stays open 24 hours unless you type other hours. When the pickup time has passed, the dialog asks for the new pickup and return first. A renter can also press **Ask to reopen this offer**: you get the To do "Renter wants expired offer reopened" and an alert, as for a new request.

An offer sent after its pickup time no longer expires by itself: it expires at its own expiry time (the pickup only counts when the offer was sent before it and the pickup is 2 hours past). The offer screens say **Pickup time has passed: update it** and do not send until you move the pickup.

## One booking page, six sections (release 31)

A booking has six sections: **Overview** (the next step; the review and offer while it is being arranged), **Money**, **Drivers & documents** (with the agreement), **Car & handovers** (the check-in and check-out, the photo report, signing on this device, what the owner sees), **Messages & history** (with the review request) and **Claims & extras** (changes, extensions, add-ons). Customer service, Sales, Fleet and Finance see the sections their work needs. An old link to a tab opens the section that holds it now.

Admin and staff open the same booking page, the same car page and the same listing review: you see every section and button, each staff function sees the parts it works with (Fleet has no Money section; only customer service and you have **Claims & extras**; refunds are asked for by you or Finance). A staff link to a booking opens the same page in the staff portal.

Every list has one search box (it finds names, numbers, plates, phones, emails and VINs) and one row of at most five chips. **Clear** removes every filter; the last one you used comes back next time on this device.

## Charge the renter after the return

Once the car is back, the Money tab has one action for everything owed after the trip: **Charge the renter**.

1. Press **Charge the renter**.
2. Choose the **Reason** from the list and add a note if it helps (Other needs its note). Enter the **Amount**.
3. Read the line under it: it says where the money comes from before anything moves. The deposit hold while it is still valid and covers the amount (the rest of the hold is released at the same time); otherwise the card on file; otherwise a pay link to the renter by text or email.
4. Press **Charge $...**. If the hold expired meanwhile, the card on file is charged instead, with the same amount and reason.

**Release** stays its own button. The renter''s receipt shows the reason.

## A deposit charged to a debit or prepaid card

When the deposit is charged instead of held on a debit or prepaid card (Charge the card on file as the deposit), the renter also pays the **Card processing fee for a debit deposit** (Program settings, 2.9% and $0.30 by default): a separate, non-refundable amount on the same charge. The Money tab''s history and the receipt show it; the deposit refund returns the deposit only.

## What the renter sees still to do

While a booking waits to be signed and paid, the Next step quotes the renter''s own Sign and pay card, for example: The renter sees: "Two steps left: sign the rental agreement, then pay $...". Signed for an older version of the offer counts as not signed: the renter signs the updated agreement on their Sign and pay page.

## Override a pickup or a return that must go ahead (release 33)
Sometimes the trip has to start (or end) even though a check still stops it. On the booking page, a confirmed booking (or one waiting for payment) and a car on rent show **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) with each check in plain words: the deposit not taken, the rental agreement not signed, no renter signature on the check-in report, a licence or identity not verified, the coverage not confirmed, an additional driver who has not accepted, the payment still due, the calendar switch off, the car not marked available, maintenance overdue, the Ontario licence, the fleet insurance policy (when that rule is on in Program settings), the agreement''s claim details, the tracker; at a return, an odometer lower than at pickup.

1. Press **Override and record the pickup** (or the return).
2. Give the actual time (now, or earlier), the km and fuel if you know them, and why the trip must go ahead. The reason is required.
3. Press the button. The pickup (or the return) is recorded at that time, only the checks listed are passed, for this booking and this once. The booking''s history and the audit log say who, when, why and which checks; every Admin gets the alert Override used. A payment still due is not waived: the booking is confirmed with the balance open, and the deposit is still to collect (it is not waived). The photos and readings come later, as with Record now.

When staff (Fleet, customer service, Sales, field staff) need it, they press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return) on the same card with the time they recorded. You get the alert Override asked for and a line on the To do: press **Approve** (one tap) and it is recorded with the time they entered, or **Decline** with a note. The request also shows on the booking page, with Approve and Decline.

## Record a past trip (release 33)
A trip that happened but was never recorded (the pickup and the return both passed): on the booking page press **Record a past trip**. Give the actual pickup and return times, the km and fuel at each if you know them, and the reason. Every check that would stop it is overridden as above, in one step: the booking lands in **Returned**, the late return charges follow the actual return time, and the deposit can be settled. The car''s status today is left as it is, and the renter is not sent a "your rental started" email for a trip long over. Fleet gets the task to add the photos and readings. Staff ask for it the same way; you approve in one tap.

## Book it now: an offer that is a booking at once (release 33)
When you send an offer (answering a request, or **Send an offer** without one), tick **Book it now (no renter approval)** above Send. The offer becomes the approved version at once: the booking waits for payment, the car is held for its dates as for any approved offer, and the renter gets one link to the **Sign and pay** page to sign and pay (the "approve your offer" email is not sent). To have them sign and pay with you, open the booking: **Sign now on this device**, then take the card on this device. When customer service or Sales tick it, the offer goes out and you get the alert Override asked for and a To do line: **Approve** in one tap books it the same way. The booking''s history says who booked it and that the renter did not approve it.

Already sent the offer? Tell Claude or the assistant: "Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the renter agreed by phone". Claude''s connector has the tool **Book an offer now**, and **Send an offer** and **Make an offer** take Book it now too; the assistant (Assistant at the top of the menu) takes it in the same sentence as the offer. Each is two steps: you see what will change (nothing is changed yet), then you confirm, and the booking waits for the renter to sign and pay as above. As an Admin it is done at once; when customer service or Sales ask the assistant, it waits for your one-tap Approve.

## A request replaced by a newer one
When a request or offer expired and the renter made a newer one for the same car and dates, the old one is hidden from Requests and keeps its number and history. Both booking pages say so under the title: **Replaced by #CC-10483** on the old one and **Replaces #CC-10482** on the new one, each a link to the other. Customer service, Sales and the other staff pages show the same note.

## Change protection (release 41)

How damage to the car is covered is one control on the booking page: the **Protection** card at the top (Overview and the Money tab). An Admin, customer service and fleet use it on any booking; sales on a request or an offer.

1. Press **Change protection**. A small window lists the three options: **Own insurance (OPCF 27)**, **Credit card coverage** and **Protection Plan**, each with the price difference (the plan shows its price a day times the days, plus HST), the deposit (no coverage rule changes it) and what the renter provides.
2. The rule is the same as on the renter''s page: credit card coverage needs the renter''s card picked from the coverage list, a card that covers this car, and the renter''s confirmation that they pay with it; OPCF 27 needs the renter''s confirmation that they upload their policy; otherwise the Protection Plan. An Admin can tick Admin override: the reason is recorded on the change and in the booking history.
3. Write the reason (required; the renter reads it) and press **Change protection**.

What happens: the booking is repriced at once. More to pay is a balance to collect on the Money tab; less, when the plan was paid, is a refund for an Admin to approve. No money moves by itself. An offer is sent again as a new version; a confirmed booking or a rental in progress gets the amended agreement (the renter signs the new version when the rules ask) and one email. Proof tasks follow the new option. Changes are refused after damage is reported on the booking.

A renter''s request to leave the Protection Plan shows on the same card with their proof (**Open the proof**). Customer service or an Admin presses **Approve** (the change is made and the coverage confirmed) or **Decline** with a note the renter reads. The task "The renter asks to leave the Protection Plan" opens the booking.

## Change the car before pickup

On a request, an offer or a confirmed booking that is not picked up yet, press **Change the car** at the top of the booking.

1. Choose the new car. Only cars free for the whole booking are listed, each with its new total and the difference.
2. Say why the car changes, then press **Change the car**.
3. The price comes from the new car''s rate sheet (its rates, the km included and the rate per km). The coverage, the drivers and the add-ons stay as they are.
4. An offer is sent again with the new car: that offer is the renter''s one email.
5. On a confirmed booking, more to pay is left open: the renter sees **Pay the balance** on their booking, or you send a pay link or charge the saved card from Money. Less to pay becomes a refund that waits for approval, with a To do for Finance. The renter gets one email, **Booking updated**, with the new car and the money.
6. The open handover and return jobs move to the new car. The agreement gets a new version for the renter to sign; its link goes by text.
7. The booking''s history and the audit log keep who changed it, from which car, to which car and why.

Customer service and Admins change any of them; Sales changes a request or an offer; Fleet changes a confirmed booking. Once the car is out, use **Swap vehicle** instead.

## The accident card of a booking

Every booking from confirmation to the return shows its **Accident card**: the steps after an accident and the coverage this booking uses.

- OPCF 27: the renter''s own insurer and policy number, from the proof they uploaded.
- Credit card coverage: the card and its coverage provider, from their proof.
- Protection Plan: the provider, the policy number and the claims phone from Settings > Program (Tolls and damage), with the renter''s plan reference.

Press **Print the card** for the printable card. The renter has the same card on their booking. It never shows the fleet policy.

## Close ended trips

A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.

**Bookings** shows a banner when trips have ended and are not closed; **Close ended trips** lists each one: never picked up in the system, on rent after the return, or returned and never closed. Fleet and Finance have the same page.

1. Tick one or several, then **Mark them**: returned on time, returned late (give the time it came back), or a no-show (an Admin or customer service).
2. Choose the deposit: **Deduct the balance owed**, **Deduct the late fee**, or **Release in full**. A card hold that has expired is marked settled at once (released by expiry: no money moves).
3. If no deposit was taken, an Admin fills **Admin: deposit not taken, waive it because** (the same field is in Record a past trip).
4. Nothing is released by itself: the decision waits under **Deposit decisions waiting for an Admin**, and an Admin presses **Release** (or **Release now (tolls window)**).

## Return charges

A late return is charged per started extra day at the booking''s full daily cost (the rental per day after discounts, plus per-day and per-trip fees such as the Protection Plan, never delivery), and only the started hours after the whole days get the hourly late fee. On the booking''s **Money** tab, each renter line not on a statement yet has **Change amount** (lower) and **Waive**, with the reason; it is in the booking history and the next assessment keeps it. An expired card hold after the return has **Mark settled (released by expiry)**.

## The Protection Plan priced from RentalCover (release 35)

The Protection Plan stays our product: renters never see the RentalCover name. Without the RentalCover partner key it is priced from the Protection Plan table, as before. Once the key is set, its price comes from a real RentalCover quote for the renter (their dates, their age at pickup, their name and email) plus our markup (20% unless **Settings** > **Program** changes it). The request form asks for the quote once the renter''s details are in, and an offer as you choose option 3; a quote is reused for 15 minutes. A price you type for the plan wins. If RentalCover does not answer, the table price applies.

RentalCover covers up to $50,000 an incident, so the plan is offered only for a car worth less. The value used: your override under **Value for the Protection Plan** on the car''s page when set, else the car''s Canadian Black Book value, else an AI estimate from typical listing prices that the site makes by itself (**Refresh the AI estimate** asks again). A car with no value counts as over the limit: the request form, the offer screen and the database then offer only OPCF 27 or credit card coverage.

## Extensions at the all-in price a day (release 35)

An extension costs what the renter already pays, averaged per day: the booking''s total for the booked period (the rental after discounts, every fee, one-time fees like delivery included, and HST) divided by its days, for each added day. A booking of $729.36 for 7 days costs $104.19 for each added day. Added hours under a day cost the hourly late fee with HST, never more than a day. There is no extension discount.

| Where | What happens |
| --- | --- |
| The renter''s **Extend** page | Each option shows the total and the price a day before paying |
| **Edit** on a confirmed or on-trip booking, made longer | The booking''s new total is the all-in price of the longer stay; the per-trip fees stay as booked and the rental charge takes the difference |
| The next period of a long rental | Keeps the rate of the booked period (the rental a day, per-trip fees scaled) |
| An insurer-billed booking | Priced as before |

The extension is one line on the booking, "Extension: 3 days at $104.19/day (all-in)", HST included. Its HST is the booking''s own share of HST, so invoices and the books never add HST on top. Type a rental charge in **Edit** to set another price. Late returns are unchanged: the daily cost of each extra day and the hourly late fee.

## A fixed amount per payment (release 35)

On a weekly, every 2 weeks or monthly plan, an Admin can set **Fixed amount per payment** in **Change the plan**. Each payment is that amount and the last one takes the remainder. The total and the payments already made never change. Leave it empty to split the payments by the days again.

## The request as sent and every offer (release 35)

On a request or a booking, **Original request, as the renter sent it** shows the car, dates, places, coverage, add-ons, note and the price the renter saw, exactly as sent; staff changes never touch it. **Offer history** lists every offer version, newest first: its status, who sent it and when, the car and dates, the message, how the total moved, and the price breakdown.

1. To go back to an old version, press **Revert to this offer** on it. Its car, dates, price, deposit, discount and fees load into the review as a new offer, highlighted.
2. Check the price, then send it in step 3. Nothing changes until you send.

The **Coverage** line at the top says what the renter chose (own insurance OPCF 27, credit card, Protection Plan) and its proof: not sent yet, waiting for review, confirmed, or rejected with the reason.

## Send an offer in three steps (release 35)

1. **Car and dates**: the renter, the dates, the car and where they pick it up and return it.
2. **Price**: filled in from the rate sheet with the checkout''s fees and discounts. Change it only if you agreed another price.
3. **Review and send**: what changed, the message and how the link goes.

Rarely used options (billing an insurer, how it is paid, the calendar) are under **More options**. Send waits while the price is being worked out again after a date change, and one tap sends once.

## The owner''s own trip, instant bookings and Book it now (release 35)

- **Owner''s own trip ($0)**: the owner booked their own car. There is nothing to price or send; get the car ready.
- **Instant (repeat renter)**: a Gold renter or above (Rewards, release 40) with a verified licence and nothing owing booked an available car at once and went straight to sign and pay. An Admin can take a renter''s instant booking away from the booking page.
- **Any car, any time** (release 40): a Platinum renter asked for dates the car shows as taken. Fleet gets an urgent task due within 4 hours: confirm it, offer an equivalent car or an upgrade, or decline with a reason. Never cancel or move another renter''s confirmed booking for it. The task closes when the request is answered.
- **Book it now** pressed by staff waits for an Admin''s one-tap approval.

## Secondary contact and rideshare documents (release 35)

The booking shows the renter''s **Secondary contact** when they gave one: call them when the renter cannot be reached. Rideshare and delivery driving are welcome (rental agreement, section 10.3): never tell a renter it is not allowed. When a renter makes **rideshare documents** (Uber, Lyft, DoorDash and others), you get an alert and the booking shows the letters they made.

## Offers, coverage, delivery and fuel (releases 35 and 36)

- Sending an offer is three steps: car and dates, price, review and send. Every request shows the renter''s original request as sent and every offer version, with who sent it and when; reverting loads an old version as a new offer to send.
- Instant booking: a verified Gold renter or above books an available car at once, signs and pays; the booking is marked Instant (repeat renter), and an Admin can take instant booking away from a renter.
- Card coverage is checked against the car: the card, the car''s value, its type and the rental length. A card that does not cover it cannot be approved. OPCF 27 needs both the pink slip and the endorsement page.
- Delivery is priced by distance from the company''s address (1570 Midland Ave, Scarborough): a base, the kilometres included and a rate per km, all in Program settings; a car''s own fee stays as an override.
- The fuel line at the return is suggested from the car''s tank, the weekly pump price and a multiplier, plus the refuelling fee, and checked on the deposit review before any charge.
- Owner price limits: the daily minimum and maximum of a car or an owner hold every price, discount and offer; only an Admin can allow one request outside them, with a reason.
- Rideshare and delivery work is allowed with the documents the renter makes on their booking page (rental agreement copy, coverage letter, vehicle letter); staff get an alert when they are made. The secondary contact shows on the booking.
- Mid-trip review ask: halfway through a trip of several days, the renter gets one short message asking how it is going; a problem they report becomes a To do for customer service.
- A car that has only test bookings can be deleted by an Admin; the test bookings go with it. A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.

## Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)

**Start the check-in (pickup)** and **Start the check-out (return)** on the booking, and **Check in** or **Check out** on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:

1. Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.
2. What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car''s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.
3. Photos are one tap each: **Take this photo** always shows the next angle.
4. What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.
5. The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you to it. When everything is in, press **Hand over the keys** or **Complete the return**.

Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.

**Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)** is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do **Late return: choose the charge**. Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do **Late return: approve the charge** and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

On **Close ended trips**, marking a trip returned late and choosing **Deduct the late fee** is the same choice of the late return fee, made there. The other deposit choices leave the late return to be chosen on the booking.',
  '<p class="gd-p">A booking starts as a request from the website, or as an offer you send yourself to a customer on the phone. You check it, adjust it and send the offer; an offer that is out is changed in place. After that, the booking page holds the money, documents, changes and history.</p><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-bookings-now-what-is-out-coming-back-and-owed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Bookings now: what is out, coming back and owed</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b>. It opens on <b class="gd-ui">Now</b>, one screen that refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. Every time is Toronto time.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The numbers at the top: cars out now, due back today, overdue, going out in the next 72 hours, payments due in the next 7 days (with the total) and free cars. Tap one to jump to its list.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Out now</b>: every car on rent, overdue returns first in red. Each shows the car (photo, code, plate), the renter with <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>, when it was picked up, when it is due back with a countdown, the payment plan and the next payment, the deposit held, and the km and fuel at pickup. Filter by Overdue, Due today or Payment due.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A confirmed booking whose pickup time has passed with no check-in recorded is listed as out, with <b class="gd-ui">Out (pickup not recorded)</b>. The car most likely left. Press <b class="gd-ui">Mark picked up</b>: it records the pickup at the booked time (change it if the car left at another time), the booking goes on rent, and Fleet gets a task to add the photos, km and fuel. The usual checks stay: the deposit taken (or an Admin waives it with the reason), the renter&#39;s signature (or an Admin&#39;s reason), the agreement&#39;s details, every driver verified and the coverage confirmed. If one is missing, the reason is shown.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Coming back</b>: overdue, today and tomorrow, by the time each is due.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Going out</b>: confirmed pickups in the next 72 hours, delivery or pickup, with ticks and crosses for the licence, the signed agreement, the payment, the deposit (a clock until the morning of the pickup day, when the hold is placed on the card on file) and the check-in photos (done at the handover).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Money due</b>: every rental payment due in the next 7 days or overdue, the amount, the plan and which payment it is (for example 3 of 4).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Free now</b>: cars available and not out, the longest idle first, with the next pickup; then the cars in maintenance or cleaning. Partners&#39; cars are counted apart.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Placeholder bookings never show on Now.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Payment plans</h3><p class="gd-p">A rental is paid in full at pickup, weekly, every 2 weeks, or monthly. A rental longer than one period (30 days) pays each period by itself. To change it, open the booking, then the <b class="gd-ui">Payment plan</b> card on Overview or Money, and press <b class="gd-ui">Change the plan</b>. Each payment is its share of the total by its days, due on the day it starts. An insurer-billed rental shows <b class="gd-ui">Insurer billed</b> and is never in Money due unless the renter owes a part. Admins, customer service and finance change the plan; fleet sees it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-all-bookings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">All bookings</h2><p class="gd-p">The <b class="gd-ui">All bookings</b> tab of Bookings has the search (booking number, name, email, phone, plate or car code), the status (All, Out now, Booked, Returned, Cancelled; closed bookings are found with the search, which also finds the insurer). <b class="gd-ui">Out now</b> shows the bookings on rent and those whose pickup passed without a check-in, together. Each booking is one row: its number and status in plain words, the car with its photo, the renter with <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>, the dates, the money (paid up, to pay, overdue, insurer billed) and Bill to.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-request-queue" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The request queue</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Requests and offers</b>. The oldest waiting request is at the top.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The numbers at the top: waiting for an offer, past the reply target (red), offers out, accepted but not paid, and offers expired. Each one is a filter: press it and the list shows just those, with the matching chip below marked as chosen.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">One queue, the most urgent first: the longest wait, then offers accepted but not paid, then offers out by when they expire. Each row has the car with its photo, the dates, the price, the renter with <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>, the licence (verified, to review, or not uploaded yet), who is answering it, and one button: <b class="gd-ui">Send offer</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Follow up</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Open</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> sits beside <b class="gd-ui">Send offer</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Waiting shows how long the renter has waited (&quot;12 min&quot;, &quot;3 h&quot;, &quot;2 days&quot;); red means past the first reply target (5 minutes, set in Program settings). <b class="gd-ui">Promise</b> counts down the 2 hours the site promises the renter.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by Active, New, Changes asked, Offer out, Accepted, not paid or Expired. The list remembers your last choice on that device; <b class="gd-ui">Active</b> always shows the whole queue and replaces what it remembered. When the same renter asks for the same car for overlapping dates again and the earlier request or offer expired, only the newest is listed: the older ones are linked to it and leave Requests (they keep their history). An expired offer leaves the active queue 48 hours after it expired, or once its pickup time passed; Expired lists the ones from the last 7 days. After 7 days an expired offer leaves Requests and offers and becomes a renter lead, once, in People &gt; Renters &gt; Leads (Expired offers), with the car and the dates the renter wanted and a To do for Sales to win them back. An offer still out when its pickup time passes expires by itself.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/requests</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/820"><img src="/guides/img/admin-02-requests-desktop-6521282d.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="820"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:38.9%;top:29.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.2%;top:43.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A request whose pickup time passes without an offer expires by itself, with a note in its history. The renter is not emailed unless &quot;Email the renter when their request expires that way&quot; is on in Program settings.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-answer-a-request-with-an-offer" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Answer a request with an offer</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The Review and offer tab shows the request as the renter sent it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Adjust the car, the dates, the rate type, the places, the rates (under <b class="gd-ui">Show rate card</b>) and fees, the deposit and extras. A place changed away from a delivery or a collection takes its fee box and its fee with it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Price on the right updates as you change things.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add a message, choose how long the offer stays open, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1200/1550"><img src="/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-353f3707.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="1550"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:5%;top:6.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:7.5%;top:45.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.2%;top:42.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.7%;top:98.1%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Changed fields but not ready to send? Press <b class="gd-ui">Save changes</b>. The panel &quot;The offer as the renter sees it&quot; shows the result.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Can&#39;t do it? Press <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> and fill in Reason and any alternative.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Need an answer first? Press <b class="gd-ui">Ask the renter</b> to send a question.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:500/80"><img src="/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-4dd4ed06.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="500" height="80"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:41.2%;top:52.5%" aria-hidden="true">6</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18%;top:52.5%" aria-hidden="true">7</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">Opening a request takes it for you: everyone else sees &quot;Being answered by&quot; your name and since when, with Send the offer and Decline off, until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work; Program settings). Press <b class="gd-ui">Take over</b> to answer one someone else holds; it is noted in the history. A second answer is refused with who answered and when. A request from the website opens to Sales after 15 minutes (Program settings); until then Admins, customer service and fleet answer it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-send-an-offer-without-a-request" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send an offer without a request</h2><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> at the top of Bookings, or <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer without a request</b> on Requests and offers. For a customer on the phone, by text or at the counter: no request needed.</p><p class="gd-p">The screen is seven short steps, each with one line saying what to do, and the price beside it (on a phone the total sits at the bottom of the screen: press <b class="gd-ui">See every line</b>). What most offers never need is under each step&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">More options</b>, which stays open while something in it is used.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Who is renting and when</b>: find the renter by name, phone or email, or press <b class="gd-ui">Not on file? Add a new customer</b> (full legal name, mobile, email for the offer link, date of birth). A customer already on file with the same email or phone is shown with Use: one person, one record. Then the pickup and the return.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Which car</b>: search by car code, plate or name; each car says Free or Not free for the dates. More options: the rate card and the type and free-only filters.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Where they pick up and return</b>: at our location, we deliver or collect (the address and distance), an airport or the owner&#39;s location. The fee each one makes shows under it, Automatic or Set by hand.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">How damage is covered</b>: the renter&#39;s own insurance, a credit card or the Protection Plan. More options: another Protection Plan price.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Extras</b>: add-ons, when the car has any.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The price</b>: the rate sheet price is filled in. More options: another price (a total for the trip or a rate a day, with why), Amounts I type (before or after HST), the total the renter pays, kilometres, a promo code, the deposit and a discount (an Admin), and <b class="gd-ui">Fees</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> to set one by hand, <b class="gd-ui">Reset to automatic</b> to undo it. Below: how it is paid (card online and a card hold unless you change it under More options).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Send it</b>: who found this client (sales and customer service), a message, and Text or Email. More options: how long the offer is open, the owner&#39;s view, who found the client (an Admin) and the internal note. Above the button, <b class="gd-ui">Ready to send</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Missing:</b> with what is left; press Send and each missing field says what it needs. Press <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer to</b> the renter, or <b class="gd-ui">Save without sending</b> to keep it as a request for later. <b class="gd-ui">The offer as the renter sees it</b> is under the price.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Choices drive the charges. Take off a delivery, a collection, the Protection Plan or an add-on and its fee goes with it, even a fee set by hand: there is nothing to remove in a second place. Choose it again and the fee starts from the automatic amount.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>It makes the same request and offer the website makes: the renter approves, signs and pays (or you record the payment), and only then is the car on the calendar. No &quot;request received&quot; email goes to the renter for an offer you send. Staff commissions and statements count it like any other booking.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-change-an-offer-that-is-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change an offer that is out</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter has the offer (Offered), or approved it and has not paid (Signing and payment). Open <b class="gd-ui">More actions</b> on the booking and press <b class="gd-ui">Edit the offer</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Change anything: the car, the dates, the places, the price, fees, the deposit, add-ons, how it is paid. Each changed field is highlighted and the before and after are listed. Amounts I type (Before tax or After tax) and the Total the renter pays (after tax) work as on Send an offer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Write what changed in Message to the renter and choose how long the offer is open.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save and send the update</b>: the renter gets the new version by email or text (ticked), and the old version no longer counts. Or press <b class="gd-ui">Save without telling the renter</b> and tell them yourself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A confirmed booking is changed with <b class="gd-ui">Change the booking</b> (Propose a change, below).</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>No need to withdraw first. <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw the offer</b> is only for taking it back for good; <b class="gd-ui">Send again, later expiry</b> gives the renter more time, and <b class="gd-ui">Renter approved by phone</b> records a yes given on a call.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-edit-a-booking-that-has-started" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Edit a booking that has started</h2><p class="gd-p">On a confirmed, on-trip or returned booking (an Admin: a closed one too), Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Edit the booking</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Change the pickup or the return (extend or shorten: the rental charge is worked out again at this booking&#39;s rates), the car (on trip: the car it leaves goes to Out of service for Fleet to check), the rental charge for the trip, each fee, the kilometres a day, the deposit (an Admin) and the note.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type why, if you like, and tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter what changed</b>, or leave it off for a silent correction. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the changes</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">What is open now shows at once: <b class="gd-ui">Email a pay link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Text a pay link</b> for exactly that amount, <b class="gd-ui">Charge</b> the saved card (the renter agreed), or record cash or an e-Transfer on the Money tab.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Each edit is kept with who, when, why, before and after (Edits, under the form) and in the booking&#39;s history. A closed booking&#39;s owner split and the staff commission follow. To have the renter accept and sign first, use Propose a change instead.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-fees-a-forgotten-fee-and-the-balance" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fees, a forgotten fee and the balance</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking&#39;s Money tab, Fees lists each fee. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change or add a fee</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type a new amount (for the whole trip, before HST) beside any fee, or choose one not on the booking (the young driver fee shows its price for these dates), or add a charge of its own with or without HST.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the fees</b>. The balance shows by part (rental, fees) with the pay link, the saved card and Record a payment beside it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The renter sees the balance on their booking with a Pay button, and pays by card on Stripe&#39;s form.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Every change is recorded (Changes to the fees): the amount before and after, who and why. Customer service and sales may change fees while Program settings, Staff may change fees, is on.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-a-renter-with-only-a-debit-or-prepaid-card" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A renter with only a debit or prepaid card</h2><p class="gd-p">A credit card is required by default: the deposit must be on a credit card so the deductible can be charged. The pay page tells a renter with only a debit or prepaid card to contact us.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the booking&#39;s Money tab, press <b class="gd-ui">Allow debit and prepaid cards for this booking</b> and type the reason. Who and when are kept, and the change is in the booking&#39;s history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The booking&#39;s pay page, staff pay links and deposit hold then take a debit or prepaid card, and the renter is told the hold lowers the money available on the card until it is released, which can take several business days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Require a credit card again</b> turns it off.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The Money tab shows each card used and its type (credit, debit, prepaid). A booking on credit card rental coverage is always paid on the credit card that carries the coverage, and cannot be allowed. Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Card types accepted</b>, can open debit and prepaid cards to every booking.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-correct-a-renter-s-details" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Correct a renter&#39;s details</h2><p class="gd-p">On the renter&#39;s page (People, Renters) or on any of their bookings, <b class="gd-ui">Edit renter</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Correct the name, email, phone, date of birth, licence, home address (start typing to find it) or the staff note.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A new email also becomes their sign-in at once (no confirmation needed for a typo you correct); tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter a link to set a password</b> to send one there. Unsigned agreements and offers go to the new address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the renter</b>. An email that another renter has is refused with their name; the same phone is a warning.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The same person entered twice? Possible duplicates (same email, same phone, or same name and date of birth) shows under the renter. <b class="gd-ui">Merge into this record</b> moves the other record&#39;s bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages here and fills any detail missing here; the other record stays, blocked, with the merge in both histories.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-money-tab-rental-charges-and-security-deposit" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Money tab: Rental charges and Security deposit</h2><p class="gd-p">The booking&#39;s Money tab opens on a strip with the three numbers that matter: <b class="gd-ui">Rental due</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Deposit</b> (one word: Not collected, Held, Charged, Released or Partly kept) and <b class="gd-ui">Total paid</b>. Below are two panels, side by side on a computer and one above the other on a phone. Collecting one never touches the other, and every receipt says which one it is.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Rental charges</b>: each line of the price and the total, Paid, then Balance due.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The one main button, Collect (the amount) rental: choose how. <b class="gd-ui">The card on file</b> charges it now (Finance or an Admin); <b class="gd-ui">A payment link by text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">A payment link by email</b> sends the renter Stripe&#39;s secure form; <b class="gd-ui">On this device: hand it to the renter</b> opens it for the renter to type; <b class="gd-ui">Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)</b> records money received (an e-Transfer, cheque or transfer needs its reference). For: the rental and fees together by default, or one of them. With the card on file, the rental and fees together are one charge with one receipt that lists both (the rental is paid first, then the fees; an insurer&#39;s part and money already received another way are left out). The renter gets a receipt; <b class="gd-ui">Print</b> prints one to hand over.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">A later charge</b> (before the return): on the card on file, by a link, on this device, or recorded. Choose the <b class="gd-ui">Reason</b> from the list (Mileage overage, Fuel, Cleaning, Smoking, Late return, Tolls, Tickets/fines, Damage, Missing items, Other) and add a note; Other needs its note. The renter&#39;s receipt shows the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Save a card</b> saves the renter&#39;s card without charging it. Card readers, the fees (<b class="gd-ui">Change or add a fee</b>), failed card payments (<b class="gd-ui">Paid another way</b>), payments received another way and <b class="gd-ui">Refund</b> sit in this panel too. The history lists rental payments only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An offer paid another way: once the renter approved and signed and the money is recorded, the booking is confirmed (or press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm the booking</b>).</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Security deposit</b>: the amount, how it is taken (a credit card hold, a debit or prepaid card at the standard multiple, a charge, or cash), its status in one word and the next step.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Not collected: the one main button, Collect (the amount) deposit. <b class="gd-ui">Hold on the card on file</b> places the hold now (Finance or an Admin); <b class="gd-ui">A deposit hold link by text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">A deposit hold link by email</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">A hold on this device: hand it to the renter</b>; <b class="gd-ui">Charge the card on file as the deposit</b> only when no hold can be placed; <b class="gd-ui">Cash or e-Transfer (record it)</b>. The rental balance is not touched.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Before every pickup the deposit hold link is texted to the renter on its own: 24 hours before (at once when the pickup is sooner), for a confirmed booking whose deposit is a card hold with no hold yet. The panel says <b class="gd-ui">Deposit link texted</b> and when it was opened. No mobile number, or the text not sent: a task <b class="gd-ui">Deposit link not sent</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then Site settings, Deposit link by text: on or off, and the hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Held, while the car is out: <b class="gd-ui">Release</b> (an Admin, with the reason), <b class="gd-ui">Keep part (damage/fees)</b> with the amount and the reason from the list, or <b class="gd-ui">Re-authorize the hold</b> on the saved card before it lapses (the panel shows when the hold expires). A job re-authorizes it by itself about 24 hours before it expires; if it cannot, Finance and the Admins get the alert <b class="gd-ui">Deposit hold not re-authorized</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hold expired</b>: a card hold lasts about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise. Once it has expired, nothing can be kept from it: the panel says Hold expired, Keep and Release are hidden, and <b class="gd-ui">Charge the card on file instead</b> opens the later charge with the amount and the reason filled in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">After the return: <b class="gd-ui">Settle the deposit</b> (below).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Waive the deposit</b> (an Admin, before it is taken), <b class="gd-ui">Change the debit deposit</b>, and <b class="gd-ui">Allow debit and prepaid cards for this booking</b> sit in this panel. The history lists deposit payments only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">A deposit taken in cash or by e-Transfer is given back the same way after the return: Finance gets a task; press <b class="gd-ui">Returned</b> with the reference or receipt number.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Statements, reconciliation and the deposit settlement read each payment with its method: a cash deposit is never refunded to a card.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-settle-the-deposit" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Settle the deposit</h2><p class="gd-p">The deposit is never given back by itself. Finance or an Admin settles it after the return: on the booking&#39;s Money tab, under Deposit, press <b class="gd-ui">Settle the deposit</b>. Issue the Check-out statement first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The form shows the deposit, what is still available, the charges owed from the statement and what is taken from the deposit for them. What the deposit does not cover is charged to the card on file; with no card (or a card declined), the renter gets a pay link by email and text, and Finance has a task until it is paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Tolls and tickets can take up to 7 days to come in. Inside that window the whole rest of the deposit is filled in as the hold-back, until the window ends. To give it back sooner, tick Release now anyway: a toll that comes in later is charged to the card on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Something still open keeps the whole deposit: an incident, a claim, new damage at the return not priced, damage found later not billed, a toll or ticket on the car during the rental not matched or not charged, a card dispute, or charges not on a statement yet. The form lists them. Only an Admin can release part of it, with the reason; it is recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Damage: <b class="gd-ui">Keep the whole deposit (damage)</b> turns what is left of the deposit into a damage charge, with what was damaged and the photos; the renter is told. <b class="gd-ui">Bill damage</b> adds a damage charge up to the $2,500 deductible (more goes through a claim): the deposit pays first, then the card on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Settle</b>. The money moves at Stripe at once: the charges are collected and what is not owed is refunded or the hold released. A step Stripe refuses is tried again by itself, and Finance gets a task if it keeps failing.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A card hold lapses after about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise. While the car is out, or returned and not settled, the hold is collected in full a day and a half before it lapses: that keeps the money, and the settlement refunds what is not owed. A hold that lapses anyway is charged to the saved card, and Finance is told at once.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-a-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A booking</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b>, then a booking number. Or type the number in the search box.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Tabs: Overview, Money, Changes, History, and Drivers and documents.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Overview shows the trip, the renter, what is still missing for the handover, and the price.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open tasks for this booking, with the queue and the due time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Top right: <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter</b> and <b class="gd-ui">More actions</b>, the menu with <b class="gd-ui">Edit the offer</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Stop blocking the calendar</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Cancel for the renter</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Cancel by CarmaCars</b> and the rest.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Under the booking number: <b class="gd-ui">Next step</b>, what happens next and who does it, with one button for that step (for example <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Sign on this device</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Check in the car</b>); then where the booking is on its way, from Request to Closed, with the dates, the days, the total and who pays.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/960"><img src="/guides/img/admin-04-booking-desktop-b56b668a.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="960"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:46.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:85.4%;top:14.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.9%;top:26.8%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-check-a-car-out-or-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check a car out or in</h2><p class="gd-p">From the booking, with your phone or a tablet: the same checklist field staff use.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A confirmed booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Check in (pickup)</b> under Check-in, check-out and signing; a booking on rent shows <b class="gd-ui">Check out (return)</b>. Today lists the check-ins and check-outs due, each with <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Check out</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The checklist opens: the ready check, the renter and their licence and card, the odometer (km) and fuel or charge, the keys, the photo set (every side, the wheels, the interior, the odometer and fuel gauge, the plate), damage marks with close-ups, then the renter and you sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Photos wait on the device without a connection and upload in the background. Each keeps its time, and the place when the device allows location.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A field job of the booking is taken over (the history says so); with no job, one is made for you. When done, press <b class="gd-ui">See the photo report</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in the same way from their own booking page.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-photo-report-late-returns-and-the-return-charges" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The photo report, late returns and the return charges</h2><p class="gd-p">Under Check-in, check-out and signing, press <b class="gd-ui">Photo report</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The report shows the due-back time, the actual check-in and check-out, Late by (or Overdue by while the car is out), the odometer and kilometres over the allowance, the fuel or charge out and in, every photo with its time and place, and the damage.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">At check-out the mileage overage and the fuel or recharging are written to the return charges at once. A late return (after the grace period of the fee defaults) is not: it waits for a choice on the booking (see &quot;A late return is a choice&quot;). The fuel is a suggested line: the car&#39;s tank x the fuel missing x the pump price of its grade (Program settings, updated weekly) x 1.25, plus the refuelling fee; an electric car the battery kWh x the charge missing x the price a kWh, plus the fee. A pump receipt entered later replaces it. Fleet and Finance confirm it on the deposit review; it is never charged to a card by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Not charging one? Press <b class="gd-ui">Waive</b> beside it and give the reason: it stays waived if the charges are worked out again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The time was wrong? Press <b class="gd-ui">Correct the check-out time</b> (or the check-in time) with the reason: lateness follows, a return that is no longer late loses its late charge, and the history keeps both times.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The renter gets the same report (without these buttons) by email and in their Documents. Late by shows on the booking and in the Bookings list.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">The renter says the car is back</h3><p class="gd-p">Every overdue email, text and alert (at the return time, at 15 minutes and the final notice) has a one-tap <b class="gd-ui">I&#39;ve returned the car</b> link, and the renter&#39;s booking page has the button. The renter can add photos, the odometer, the fuel level and the time they returned it. Sending it stops every overdue notice of the booking at once, the booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Returned, waiting for confirmation</b>, and Fleet gets an urgent To do: &quot;The renter says the car is back&quot;.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the booking. The card <b class="gd-ui">The renter says the car is back</b> shows what the renter gave, marked renter-provided, with their photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the car: the return place, the tracker, the photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b> to complete the trip. Correct the odometer, fuel or return time first if they are wrong: the late charges follow the time you confirm. The renter&#39;s photos join the check-out report.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Deny</b> and say why. The renter gets your reason by email and text, and the overdue notices start again.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Checking the car in the usual way also completes the trip and stops the notices. Admins, Fleet, Sales, Customer service and field staff can Confirm or Deny.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-signatures-on-the-spot-or-by-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Signatures on the spot, or by link</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter or an additional driver signs the rental agreement on your device, or on their own phone.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">While a signature is missing, the booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Email the signing link</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text the signing link</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">No agreement made yet (the renter has not saved their details at home)? <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b> still shows: press <b class="gd-ui">Prepare the agreement to sign now</b> and it is made on the spot.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>: confirm the name matches their licence and that you saw the original licence (photograph it if none is on file), then press <b class="gd-ui">Hand the device to</b> and their name.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">They read both agreements (CarmaCars&#39; and Blind Spot&#39;s), tick the statements and sign. Then <b class="gd-ui">Back to the staff view</b> for the next signer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The record is the same as signing online, and says it was signed in person, collected by you, on your device. It is printed on the signed copy&#39;s signature record page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-rental-agreements-every-version-every-field" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rental agreements: every version, every field</h2><p class="gd-p">The booking&#39;s Rental agreements card: the current version of CarmaCars&#39; and Blind Spot&#39;s agreements, every earlier one, and what is still blank.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Once the agreement is signed and countersigned, any change to what it prints makes a new version of both documents by itself: the dates, the price lines, the car, a driver added or corrected, the coverage, the deposit or how it was paid, an address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage option is signed again: the renter (and each driver it affects) gets their link by email and text, and the card shows &quot;Agreement v3 waiting for signature&quot;. A correction (a typo in an address, a plate written differently) is filed without signing; the renter gets the corrected copy by email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check-in makes the &quot;as picked up&quot; copy (time out, km out, fuel out, the car&#39;s plate and VIN, the check-in report), countersigned by whoever checked the car out; check-out makes the closing copy (time in, km in, driven and charged, fuel in, late hours, damage, the return charges, the final totals). Both go to the renter by email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Every version</b> lists each one with what changed and both PDFs. <b class="gd-ui">Resend the signing links</b>, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your phone or tablet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The card lists what the agreements still print blank (a licence expiry, the insurer&#39;s policy number, the insured vehicle, a VIN). Type the values and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the missing fields</b>: the agreements follow.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Check-in stops while a field a claim needs is blank. An Admin can let it go ahead: type the reason and press <b class="gd-ui">Override</b>; the reason is in the booking&#39;s history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Make the agreements again</b> checks both against the booking at once (they also follow every change by themselves).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Edit the wording</b> (Admin only) changes CarmaCars&#39; agreement text for this booking: press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> beside a clause, edit its text, say why and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the wording</b>; <b class="gd-ui">Add</b> writes Additional terms at the end of Part 2. Only clauses not required by law or the insurer can be removed; the consents are fixed, and Blind Spot&#39;s form (the insurer&#39;s official form) is never changed. Before the renter signs, the agreement is made again; after, the change is a new version they sign, and <b class="gd-ui">Every version</b> shows each clause before and after.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-signing-that-holds-up-in-a-dispute" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Signing that holds up in a dispute</h2><p class="gd-p">Every signature on the site is made the same way: rental agreements, amendments and new versions (remotely or on your device), and the owner agreements, schedules and forms, a co-owner&#39;s link, the partner, investment and staff agreements.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The licence on file is shown. A 6-digit code to their phone or email on file is optional: the signer may press <b class="gd-ui">Verify by code (optional)</b>, and Program settings, E-signing, <b class="gd-ui">ask for a one-time code</b> makes it a required first step again (off by default). Without the code, the certificate says the identity was not confirmed by a code.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">They say they read the documents, initial the key terms (each initials box is saved with <b class="gd-ui">Save initials</b>; <b class="gd-ui">Clear</b> takes it back to initial again) (damage and the deductible, the deposit and later charges, fuel, kilometres and late returns, their coverage, cancellation), give three consents (to sign electronically, to receive records electronically, to card charges under the agreement) and draw their signature.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Owners, partners, investors and staff do the same for their documents: the code, the reading, the key terms of their documents initialled (for example the Enrollment Agreement&#39;s three confirmations, Form C&#39;s acknowledgments, Schedule C, the staff agreement&#39;s confidentiality), two consents and the drawn signature. Form C&#39;s witness still types their name beside the owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Each step is recorded with its time, IP address and device, and the place when the device shares it. The signed PDFs end with a certificate of completion; anyone can check a signed file at <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/verify</span>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Typed names are off. For a signer who cannot draw, an Admin can turn on the accessibility fallback: <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, Esign typed fallback.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-card-disputes-the-evidence-pack" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Card disputes: the evidence pack</h2><p class="gd-p">Everything that proves the rental, in one PDF for Stripe.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">When a card payment is disputed, the evidence pack is built by itself: the signed agreements with their certificates, the check-in and check-out reports with photos, kilometres and fuel, the licence, the payments and charges, every message to the renter, and the card checks from Stripe. It is staged in Stripe as the dispute&#39;s evidence, and To do gets an urgent task.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open the booking: the Rental agreements card shows the pack. Press <b class="gd-ui">Download</b> to check it, then <b class="gd-ui">Submit to Stripe</b> before the evidence date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Build the dispute evidence pack</b> makes one at any time (an Admin or Finance).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-licence-before-an-offer-is-accepted" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The licence before an offer is accepted</h2><p class="gd-p">Front, back and a selfie, from the request on.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">After sending a request the renter is asked for their licence. A licence already on file from an earlier booking is used again while it is valid after the return.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The offer cannot be accepted (by the renter, or by you on their word) and nothing is paid until the licence and its expiry date are on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Review the images as usual with <b class="gd-ui">Review documents</b>: the card Renter documents is on Review and offer too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The switch is in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, Booking requests and offers: Booking licence required (on), with the selfie (on).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-licence-reader" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The licence reader</h2><p class="gd-p">Every licence photo is read on upload: the back&#39;s barcode first, else the vision model (within the day&#39;s AI allowance).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The renter&#39;s empty licence fields are filled from the read; the renter confirms them. A blurry or cut-off photo is taken again at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Review documents</b> shows what was read and one line per check, Pass or Flag: photos, valid to the return, class accepted, age at pickup, name and date of birth, the Ontario number, front and back, and the main driver&#39;s Ontario licence. Staff still approve.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, Driver&#39;s licence reader: <b class="gd-ui">Approve automatically when every check passes</b> (off). On: a driver whose front and back both read sharp and every check passes is approved in your name; anything flagged waits for a person.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Primary driver must hold an Ontario licence</b> (on): a main driver with a licence from elsewhere becomes an additional driver, the booking needs &quot;Primary driver: Ontario licence needed&quot; and pickup is blocked. The renter adds a main driver, who signs on their own link. On the document review, <b class="gd-ui">Admin: undo or let it go</b>: undo puts the first main driver back; let it go needs a reason.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>What was read is staff only and is deleted with the licence image. The licence number is never written to the logs.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-renter-documents-licence-and-proof-of-coverage" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Renter documents: licence and proof of coverage</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter&#39;s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage (OPCF 27 or a credit card&#39;s rental coverage) are checked before the handover. You check them yourself; no task is needed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A booking with documents waiting is a line on To do: &quot;Check &#39;s documents for booking &quot;, marked Now when the pickup is within two days. Press <b class="gd-ui">Review documents</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The pop-up shows each driver&#39;s images and the coverage: the insurer, policy number and expiry, or the card, its type and whether the name matches.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">What to check is written once at the top. One wrong? Open <b class="gd-ui">Reject this one</b> under it, type the reason the renter reads and press <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b>: they are asked for a new one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Then press <b class="gd-ui">Approve all</b>: every image, the proof of coverage and the Protection Plan still waiting are approved in one step. The number in the button is exactly what it approves (an image whose file was removed is not counted), and an image not tied to a driver of the booking is listed under <b class="gd-ui">Other documents</b>. Anything the system refuses is named with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The same pop-up is on the booking: the card Renter documents (<b class="gd-ui">Review documents</b>) on Overview and on Drivers and documents.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Each opening of a renter&#39;s documents is logged. The links to the images last one minute. Field staff can also check a licence in person at the check-in (photos and four checks): the history says &quot;checked in person&quot;. Field staff also review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from My jobs, with the same Approve all or a reason to reject: the history says the reviewer&#39;s role, field. Sales review the licence images (not the coverage) of any booking being arranged or under way from their To do or the booking, with the same Approve all or a reason to reject: the history says the role, sales.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-payments-by-day" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments by day</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Payments</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">By day</b> tab: every payment and refund of a day or a range, by method, the cash drawer and the refunds waiting. Finance has the same screen.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose From and To and the methods (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer, bank transfer, pre-authorized debit, other), then press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Totals by method and for each day; cards read as the card and its last four digits, never a code.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The cash drawer: expected (cash in less cash given back) against the count Finance records with <b class="gd-ui">Record the count</b>; a difference shows over or short.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere with the policy maths. <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with the reason in the row, then <b class="gd-ui">Issue the refund</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Export CSV</b> for the bookkeeper.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-propose-a-change-to-a-confirmed-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Propose a change to a confirmed booking</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter gets an email and answers on their booking. The calendar moves only when they accept.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the booking&#39;s Changes tab. Under Propose a change, set the new pickup, return or car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">To price it by hand, type a New rental charge before tax. Leave it empty to use the car&#39;s rates.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Write the Reason, for the renter. They read it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Preview the price</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Send to the renter</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065?tab=changes</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1200/520"><img src="/guides/img/admin-05-booking-changes-desktop-97008b21.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="520"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:17.5%;top:33.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:9.2%;top:50%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:38.3%;top:71.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:12.9%;top:91.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-who-a-booking-is-credited-to" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Who a booking is credited to</h2><p class="gd-p">Overview (and Review and offer) shows the Sales credit: the staff member the booking counts for in their sales.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A quote or a rental is credited to whoever created or added it. A request from the website is credited to whoever sent its first offer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">To give it to someone else, press <b class="gd-ui">Reassign</b>, choose who (or Nobody), say whether they sourced the client and write the reason. The booking&#39;s history and the audit log keep it, and the deal stays in the same week and month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Sourced means the staff member chose I sourced this client when they entered it, it came with a field staff referral link, or you credited it. Only a sourced booking earns a staff commission. A website request earns none unless you credit someone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Someone said they sourced a website request? The credit line shows the claim: press <b class="gd-ui">Credit them</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Not theirs</b>, with a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A price typed by hand shows beside the rate-sheet price, with the reason. A price under the floor or past the discount limit is flagged: press <b class="gd-ui">Mark reviewed</b> once you have looked at it.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A request keeps the lead-time adjustment of the moment it came in (&quot;Short-notice pricing +10%&quot; or &quot;Booked ahead −5%&quot;), through the offer and the payment. To change it, open the booking&#39;s review screen, <b class="gd-ui">More options</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Lead-time pricing (%)</b>: a number (0 for none), or empty for the tier of the request. A price typed by hand replaces it.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The rental never goes below the car&#39;s minimum daily rate or above its maximum (its price limits, set by the owner or on the car&#39;s Rates tab), whatever the discount, promo code or lead-time pricing: a line &quot;Minimum daily rate for this car&quot; or &quot;Maximum daily rate for this car&quot; brings it back. Only an Admin allows a price outside them: <b class="gd-ui">More options</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Allow a price outside the car&#39;s price limits (Admin only)</b>, with the reason.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The renter has 48 hours to accept (and sign the amendment) or decline, with one reminder. Any extra is charged to their Card on File; a lower price raises a refund for your approval.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-review-requests" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review requests</h2><p class="gd-p">Every renter is asked for a review by email and text, as they chose, only from 9 am to 9 pm Toronto time. Nothing needs setting up.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Message</th><th scope="col">When</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mid-trip check</td><td>Rentals of 2 days or more, 24 hours after the pickup: &quot;How is the car? Reply or call if anything is off.&quot; No review ask.</td></tr><tr><td>Review request</td><td>1 hour after the check-out. It links the review page: the renter taps what they liked, adds a sentence, and gets a short draft to copy and post on Google.</td></tr><tr><td>Reminder</td><td>24 hours after the request.</td></tr><tr><td>Final follow-up</td><td>7 days after the request. Nothing more after it.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The booking page has the card Review requests: each message with when it went or when it will go, and why it stopped.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Ask for a review</b> sends the request now (or at 9 am if it is later than 9 pm), on any booking on a trip, returned or closed. Not twice in 24 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On hold: a return or later charge (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls and tickets) is not settled or waived, or an incident or dispute is open. The request goes by itself once they are. Press <b class="gd-ui">Send anyway</b> to send it now.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Mark reviewed</b> stops the messages when the renter tells you they already reviewed.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The messages also stop by themselves when the renter presses &quot;I already left a review&quot;, leaves a review on the site, unsubscribes, or a Google review is matched to them. <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Reviews</b> has the numbers (requests sent, on hold, reviews detected, the average rating), the hold list and the Google reviews to match.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The draft is made only from what the renter picked and wrote, and from the booking (the car, how long, delivery or pickup). Everyone gets the Google link, whatever their stars; a renter who gives 3 stars or fewer also sees &quot;Something wasn&#39;t right? Tell us directly&quot;.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-what-the-owner-sees-and-owner-deductions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What the owner sees, and owner deductions</h2><p class="gd-p">Each booking on an owner&#39;s or partner&#39;s car shows the card What the owner sees at the top of its page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hide from the owner</b> keeps the booking&#39;s revenue from the owner until the car is returned, or until the owner statement covering it is approved. The owner sees the booking as Booked with its dates, and the calendar still shows the car busy. Add a reason if you like: it is kept in the history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Show to the owner</b> shows it now. Approving the statement shows every hidden booking on it by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Not shown to the owner is for a booking with no owner revenue (an insurance placeholder, a shareholder&#39;s or the owner&#39;s own use at no charge): the owner sees only that the car is unavailable for those dates. A booking with revenue cannot be set this way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add a rental and Send an offer have What the owner sees. It starts from Settings &gt; Program, Owners and fleet: Owners see a booking&#39;s revenue (right away by default).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">On the Money tab, Owner deductions on this booking: <b class="gd-ui">Add a booking expense</b> (cleaning, repair, fuel, platform fee or other, the amount, the reason the owner reads, a receipt number) comes off before Owner Revenue.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Set the Revenue Share for this booking</b> applies within the car&#39;s signed terms. Above the terms only an Admin can, with Above the signed terms ticked and the reason. <b class="gd-ui">Back to the car&#39;s terms</b> undoes it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Add a rental has the same under The car&#39;s owner.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The owner&#39;s statement carries each booking that counts toward the owner&#39;s revenue, at its true amounts, and lists each deduction with its reason, so the payout is always right. A booking billed to the renter always counts. Left out: a booking billed to an insurer and hidden from the owner (while Program settings keep only insurance replacements hidden), an insurer-billed rental that does not block the calendar, and a rental with &quot;Counts toward the owner&#39;s revenue&quot; off. The booking page says when a booking is not part of the owner&#39;s revenue and why. When a booking that was left out starts counting (Blocks the calendar turned on, shown to the owner, or billed to the renter), the owner gets the new booking email once, at that moment. Customer service and sales add deductions only while Program settings let them change fees.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-email-the-renter-or-the-adjuster" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Email the renter or the adjuster</h2><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter</b> at the top of a booking, or open its <b class="gd-ui">Messages &amp; history</b> section.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Write a <b class="gd-ui">Subject</b> and a <b class="gd-ui">Message</b>, or pick a <b class="gd-ui">Quick reply</b> to start from (Settings &gt; Quick replies keeps them).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter</b>. It goes from CarmaCars (bookings@carmacars.ca) and replies come back to the bookings inbox. The renter also sees it in their account and can answer there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On a booking an insurer pays, choose <b class="gd-ui">From</b>: CarmaCars, or Blind Spot Car Rental (insurance). <b class="gd-ui">Email the adjuster</b> writes to the adjuster&#39;s email on the booking (Insurance claim), always from Blind Spot Car Rental.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The <b class="gd-ui">Messages &amp; history</b> section is the booking&#39;s Activity log (release 35): what you and the renter wrote, every email of the booking, the texts, chat, calls, notes, events, payments, documents and visits, newest first, with a chip for each type and a search. The email form is under the log; each email you send shows in the log with your name.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Emails go out through the same daily limit as every email (the line under the form shows today&#39;s use). A message to a renter goes before digests and marketing; past the limit it waits until midnight. To write to a renter from <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b>, open the renter: Email the renter is at the bottom, about their latest booking or the one you pick.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Record the pickup or the return now (details later)</h3><p class="gd-p">When the car went out or came back but the checklist could not be done (no photos, no time, the renter dropped the keys), the booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Check-in, check-out and signing</b> card has <b class="gd-ui">Record the pickup now (details later)</b> on a confirmed booking and <b class="gd-ui">Record the return now (details later)</b> while the car is on rent. Give the actual time (now, or earlier), the odometer and fuel if you know them, and why. The booking moves on (on rent, or returned), late return charges follow the actual time, and Fleet gets the task <b class="gd-ui">Add the photos and readings for CC-...</b>. A car overdue or due back today also has <b class="gd-ui">Returned</b>: on the To do list (Check-ins and check-outs today), on Bookings &gt; Now and at the top of the booking page, which the late return alert opens. It asks only the return time (now, or earlier) and the km and fuel if you know them, and records the return the same way. Once returned, the statement can be issued and the deposit settled; releasing the deposit before the photos are in needs an Admin and a reason. A pickup without the deposit taken needs an Admin to waive it with a reason, and without the renter&#39;s signature on the check-in report an Admin&#39;s reason too. Later, <b class="gd-ui">Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings</b> opens the usual checklist (photos, readings, your signature): the task closes when it is saved.</p><p class="gd-p">The Agreement card says <b class="gd-ui">Waiting for the renter&#39;s details</b> when the renter still has blanks to fill (date of birth, address, mobile, licence, coverage): their account asks for them before signing and paying. No email or text is sent.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Find a booking</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> has one search box: type the booking number (CC-1042, cc1042 or just 1042), the renter&#39;s or a driver&#39;s name, an email, a phone number in any format, a plate (spaces do not matter) or a car code, then press Enter. The status filters still apply to what is found.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Record a card payment taken outside the site</h3><p class="gd-p">A card taken in the Stripe Dashboard, or on a card reader, is recorded on the booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab with <b class="gd-ui">Record card payment</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose what it paid: <b class="gd-ui">Rental and fees</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Rental</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Fees</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Later charges</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Deposit hold</b>, and where it was taken.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type the <b class="gd-ui">Last 4 digits</b> and the amount. A Stripe payment id (pi_... or ch_..., from the payment in the Stripe Dashboard) is optional for a payment: press <b class="gd-ui">Look up</b> and the amount and last 4 digits are checked against Stripe.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record it</b>. A payment confirms a booking waiting for payment, as any payment does.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A deposit hold needs its Stripe payment id, so it can be captured or released from <b class="gd-ui">Settle the deposit</b>. It is recorded as held, with the usual release reminders. A hold on a reader lapses after 2 days, one made online after about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Link a payment taken outside the platform</h3><p class="gd-p">A charge or a card deposit taken in the Stripe Dashboard or through a Stripe payment link is linked to its booking by an Admin, on the booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab: <b class="gd-ui">Link a payment taken outside the platform</b>, in the rental panel or the deposit panel.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Paste the Stripe payment id (pi_... or ch_..., from the payment in the Stripe Dashboard). <b class="gd-ui">Look up</b> shows what Stripe says: the amount, paid or a hold, and the card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Link as a rental payment</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Link as the deposit</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>It must be in Canadian dollars and not already linked. A rental payment may not be more than is open for the rental and fees. A deposit must be the whole deposit: a hold waiting to be captured is kept as held (settle it as any hold), a charged deposit is kept as captured. <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Unlinked Stripe</b> lists, every night, the Stripe payments of the last 60 days that no booking knows, with a best guess of the booking.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Charge or hold the deposit on the card reader</h3><p class="gd-p">With the S700 paired (Settings &gt; Card reader), the <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab has <b class="gd-ui">Charge on reader</b> (everything open, the rental, the fees or a later charge) and <b class="gd-ui">Hold deposit on reader</b>. Press <b class="gd-ui">Send to the reader</b>: the amount shows on the reader and the renter taps, inserts or swipes the card. The screen updates by itself; <b class="gd-ui">Cancel</b> stops the reader and nothing is charged. A deposit hold is captured or released from Settle the deposit like any hold.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Credit card coverage: the same card</h3><p class="gd-p">When the renter&#39;s coverage is their credit card, the whole rental (rental and fees) is paid on that same card. The Money tab says which card. Another card on the pay page is refused and refunded at once; on the reader it is refused before the money is taken; a payment by e-Transfer, cash or the like is refused; a card typed by hand needs its last 4 digits and the box <b class="gd-ui">This is the same card</b>. Deposits and later charges can go on any card. If the renter truly has to use another card or method, press <b class="gd-ui">Allow another card</b> and give the reason (an Admin).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-booked-as-soon-as-the-renter-accepts-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Booked as soon as the renter accepts (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">A booking is booked the moment the renter approves the offer. It takes the car on every calendar, the fleet board, the car&#39;s availability and the counts, even before the payment or the pickup is recorded. Payment and the handover show as their own badges: <b class="gd-ui">Booked, payment due</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Pickup not recorded</b>. The first renter to approve gets the car: any other open offer on the same car and dates goes back to Requests with a Re-offer To do.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Booked, payment due</b> To do: a booked rental still unpaid within 48 hours of its pickup. Send the pay link, charge the saved card or record the payment.</li><li>Record the pickup To do: a pickup time that passed with nothing recorded, as before.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">When you send an offer, <b class="gd-ui">The offer as the renter sees it</b> sits right under <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>: check it before you press it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-changes-after-signing-an-amended-agreement-no-new-signature" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Changes after signing: an amended agreement, no new signature</h2><p class="gd-p">The rental terms (section 15.4) let CarmaCars update a booking after signing: an extension, new dates or times, a price adjustment, a fee, a car swap. The signed agreement keeps applying. Each change makes a new version of the agreement marked <b class="gd-ui">Amended</b> with the date, carrying the renter&#39;s original signature, and the renter is sent it. Nobody is asked to sign again, except an additional driver who never signed (they sign before driving).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-check-in-and-check-out-on-one-screen" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check-in and check-out on one screen</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking page, <b class="gd-ui">Check in (pickup)</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Check out (return)</b> are one screen: the time (now unless you change it), the odometer, the fuel, the photos and a note. Pick many photos at once from the camera roll or take them; tag an angle on any photo if you like. The suggested angles (front, each corner and side, rear, odometer, fuel gauge, interior front and rear, trunk, wheels, any damage) tick themselves as photos are tagged. Nothing is required but the time; the renter&#39;s own photos are added to the same report, each marked with who took it (the renter or staff) and its angle. The one-screen checklist is the button above it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-type-into-the-blind-spot-agreement" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Type into the Blind Spot agreement</h2><p class="gd-p">On the <b class="gd-ui">Rental agreements</b> card, <b class="gd-ui">Type into the Blind Spot agreement</b> shows each box as the form prints it. Change a value and <b class="gd-ui">Save the corrections</b>: it is drawn in that box, and the insured vehicle, the claim number, the adjuster and missing km or fuel go back onto the booking. <b class="gd-ui">Preview the filled form</b> opens it with your corrections.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-reopen-an-expired-offer-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Reopen an expired offer (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">An expired offer reopens in one click: <b class="gd-ui">Reopen offer</b> on the booking or on the <b class="gd-ui">Expired</b> filter of Requests. The renter gets the usual offer email and text; the offer stays open 24 hours unless you type other hours. When the pickup time has passed, the dialog asks for the new pickup and return first. A renter can also press <b class="gd-ui">Ask to reopen this offer</b>: you get the To do &quot;Renter wants expired offer reopened&quot; and an alert, as for a new request.</p><p class="gd-p">An offer sent after its pickup time no longer expires by itself: it expires at its own expiry time (the pickup only counts when the offer was sent before it and the pickup is 2 hours past). The offer screens say <b class="gd-ui">Pickup time has passed: update it</b> and do not send until you move the pickup.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-one-booking-page-six-sections-release-31" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One booking page, six sections (release 31)</h2><p class="gd-p">A booking has six sections: <b class="gd-ui">Overview</b> (the next step; the review and offer while it is being arranged), <b class="gd-ui">Money</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Drivers &amp; documents</b> (with the agreement), <b class="gd-ui">Car &amp; handovers</b> (the check-in and check-out, the photo report, signing on this device, what the owner sees), <b class="gd-ui">Messages &amp; history</b> (with the review request) and <b class="gd-ui">Claims &amp; extras</b> (changes, extensions, add-ons). Customer service, Sales, Fleet and Finance see the sections their work needs. An old link to a tab opens the section that holds it now.</p><p class="gd-p">Admin and staff open the same booking page, the same car page and the same listing review: you see every section and button, each staff function sees the parts it works with (Fleet has no Money section; only customer service and you have <b class="gd-ui">Claims &amp; extras</b>; refunds are asked for by you or Finance). A staff link to a booking opens the same page in the staff portal.</p><p class="gd-p">Every list has one search box (it finds names, numbers, plates, phones, emails and VINs) and one row of at most five chips. <b class="gd-ui">Clear</b> removes every filter; the last one you used comes back next time on this device.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-charge-the-renter-after-the-return" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Charge the renter after the return</h2><p class="gd-p">Once the car is back, the Money tab has one action for everything owed after the trip: <b class="gd-ui">Charge the renter</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Charge the renter</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the <b class="gd-ui">Reason</b> from the list and add a note if it helps (Other needs its note). Enter the <b class="gd-ui">Amount</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Read the line under it: it says where the money comes from before anything moves. The deposit hold while it is still valid and covers the amount (the rest of the hold is released at the same time); otherwise the card on file; otherwise a pay link to the renter by text or email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Charge $...</b>. If the hold expired meanwhile, the card on file is charged instead, with the same amount and reason.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Release</b> stays its own button. The renter&#39;s receipt shows the reason.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-a-deposit-charged-to-a-debit-or-prepaid-card" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A deposit charged to a debit or prepaid card</h2><p class="gd-p">When the deposit is charged instead of held on a debit or prepaid card (Charge the card on file as the deposit), the renter also pays the <b class="gd-ui">Card processing fee for a debit deposit</b> (Program settings, 2.9% and $0.30 by default): a separate, non-refundable amount on the same charge. The Money tab&#39;s history and the receipt show it; the deposit refund returns the deposit only.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-what-the-renter-sees-still-to-do" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What the renter sees still to do</h2><p class="gd-p">While a booking waits to be signed and paid, the Next step quotes the renter&#39;s own Sign and pay card, for example: The renter sees: &quot;Two steps left: sign the rental agreement, then pay $...&quot;. Signed for an older version of the offer counts as not signed: the renter signs the updated agreement on their Sign and pay page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-override-a-pickup-or-a-return-that-must-go-ahead-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Override a pickup or a return that must go ahead (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">Sometimes the trip has to start (or end) even though a check still stops it. On the booking page, a confirmed booking (or one waiting for payment) and a car on rent show <b class="gd-ui">What stops the pickup now</b> (or the return) with each check in plain words: the deposit not taken, the rental agreement not signed, no renter signature on the check-in report, a licence or identity not verified, the coverage not confirmed, an additional driver who has not accepted, the payment still due, the calendar switch off, the car not marked available, maintenance overdue, the Ontario licence, the fleet insurance policy (when that rule is on in Program settings), the agreement&#39;s claim details, the tracker; at a return, an odometer lower than at pickup.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Override and record the pickup</b> (or the return).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Give the actual time (now, or earlier), the km and fuel if you know them, and why the trip must go ahead. The reason is required.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press the button. The pickup (or the return) is recorded at that time, only the checks listed are passed, for this booking and this once. The booking&#39;s history and the audit log say who, when, why and which checks; every Admin gets the alert Override used. A payment still due is not waived: the booking is confirmed with the balance open, and the deposit is still to collect (it is not waived). The photos and readings come later, as with Record now.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">When staff (Fleet, customer service, Sales, field staff) need it, they press <b class="gd-ui">Ask an Admin to override the pickup</b> (or the return) on the same card with the time they recorded. You get the alert Override asked for and a line on the To do: press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> (one tap) and it is recorded with the time they entered, or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with a note. The request also shows on the booking page, with Approve and Decline.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-record-a-past-trip-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Record a past trip (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">A trip that happened but was never recorded (the pickup and the return both passed): on the booking page press <b class="gd-ui">Record a past trip</b>. Give the actual pickup and return times, the km and fuel at each if you know them, and the reason. Every check that would stop it is overridden as above, in one step: the booking lands in <b class="gd-ui">Returned</b>, the late return charges follow the actual return time, and the deposit can be settled. The car&#39;s status today is left as it is, and the renter is not sent a &quot;your rental started&quot; email for a trip long over. Fleet gets the task to add the photos and readings. Staff ask for it the same way; you approve in one tap.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-book-it-now-an-offer-that-is-a-booking-at-once-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Book it now: an offer that is a booking at once (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">When you send an offer (answering a request, or <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> without one), tick <b class="gd-ui">Book it now (no renter approval)</b> above Send. The offer becomes the approved version at once: the booking waits for payment, the car is held for its dates as for any approved offer, and the renter gets one link to the <b class="gd-ui">Sign and pay</b> page to sign and pay (the &quot;approve your offer&quot; email is not sent). To have them sign and pay with you, open the booking: <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>, then take the card on this device. When customer service or Sales tick it, the offer goes out and you get the alert Override asked for and a To do line: <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> in one tap books it the same way. The booking&#39;s history says who booked it and that the renter did not approve it.</p><p class="gd-p">Already sent the offer? Tell Claude or the assistant: &quot;Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the renter agreed by phone&quot;. Claude&#39;s connector has the tool <b class="gd-ui">Book an offer now</b>, and <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Make an offer</b> take Book it now too; the assistant (Assistant at the top of the menu) takes it in the same sentence as the offer. Each is two steps: you see what will change (nothing is changed yet), then you confirm, and the booking waits for the renter to sign and pay as above. As an Admin it is done at once; when customer service or Sales ask the assistant, it waits for your one-tap Approve.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-a-request-replaced-by-a-newer-one" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A request replaced by a newer one</h2><p class="gd-p">When a request or offer expired and the renter made a newer one for the same car and dates, the old one is hidden from Requests and keeps its number and history. Both booking pages say so under the title: <b class="gd-ui">Replaced by #CC-10483</b> on the old one and <b class="gd-ui">Replaces #CC-10482</b> on the new one, each a link to the other. Customer service, Sales and the other staff pages show the same note.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-change-protection-release-41" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change protection (release 41)</h2><p class="gd-p">How damage to the car is covered is one control on the booking page: the <b class="gd-ui">Protection</b> card at the top (Overview and the Money tab). An Admin, customer service and fleet use it on any booking; sales on a request or an offer.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Change protection</b>. A small window lists the three options: <b class="gd-ui">Own insurance (OPCF 27)</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Credit card coverage</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Protection Plan</b>, each with the price difference (the plan shows its price a day times the days, plus HST), the deposit (no coverage rule changes it) and what the renter provides.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The rule is the same as on the renter&#39;s page: credit card coverage needs the renter&#39;s card picked from the coverage list, a card that covers this car, and the renter&#39;s confirmation that they pay with it; OPCF 27 needs the renter&#39;s confirmation that they upload their policy; otherwise the Protection Plan. An Admin can tick Admin override: the reason is recorded on the change and in the booking history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Write the reason (required; the renter reads it) and press <b class="gd-ui">Change protection</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">What happens: the booking is repriced at once. More to pay is a balance to collect on the Money tab; less, when the plan was paid, is a refund for an Admin to approve. No money moves by itself. An offer is sent again as a new version; a confirmed booking or a rental in progress gets the amended agreement (the renter signs the new version when the rules ask) and one email. Proof tasks follow the new option. Changes are refused after damage is reported on the booking.</p><p class="gd-p">A renter&#39;s request to leave the Protection Plan shows on the same card with their proof (<b class="gd-ui">Open the proof</b>). Customer service or an Admin presses <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> (the change is made and the coverage confirmed) or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with a note the renter reads. The task &quot;The renter asks to leave the Protection Plan&quot; opens the booking.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-change-the-car-before-pickup" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change the car before pickup</h2><p class="gd-p">On a request, an offer or a confirmed booking that is not picked up yet, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the car</b> at the top of the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the new car. Only cars free for the whole booking are listed, each with its new total and the difference.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Say why the car changes, then press <b class="gd-ui">Change the car</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The price comes from the new car&#39;s rate sheet (its rates, the km included and the rate per km). The coverage, the drivers and the add-ons stay as they are.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An offer is sent again with the new car: that offer is the renter&#39;s one email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">On a confirmed booking, more to pay is left open: the renter sees <b class="gd-ui">Pay the balance</b> on their booking, or you send a pay link or charge the saved card from Money. Less to pay becomes a refund that waits for approval, with a To do for Finance. The renter gets one email, <b class="gd-ui">Booking updated</b>, with the new car and the money.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">The open handover and return jobs move to the new car. The agreement gets a new version for the renter to sign; its link goes by text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">The booking&#39;s history and the audit log keep who changed it, from which car, to which car and why.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Customer service and Admins change any of them; Sales changes a request or an offer; Fleet changes a confirmed booking. Once the car is out, use <b class="gd-ui">Swap vehicle</b> instead.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-accident-card-of-a-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The accident card of a booking</h2><p class="gd-p">Every booking from confirmation to the return shows its <b class="gd-ui">Accident card</b>: the steps after an accident and the coverage this booking uses.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>OPCF 27: the renter&#39;s own insurer and policy number, from the proof they uploaded.</li><li>Credit card coverage: the card and its coverage provider, from their proof.</li><li>Protection Plan: the provider, the policy number and the claims phone from Settings &gt; Program (Tolls and damage), with the renter&#39;s plan reference.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Print the card</b> for the printable card. The renter has the same card on their booking. It never shows the fleet policy.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-close-ended-trips" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Close ended trips</h2><p class="gd-p">A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> shows a banner when trips have ended and are not closed; <b class="gd-ui">Close ended trips</b> lists each one: never picked up in the system, on rent after the return, or returned and never closed. Fleet and Finance have the same page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Tick one or several, then <b class="gd-ui">Mark them</b>: returned on time, returned late (give the time it came back), or a no-show (an Admin or customer service).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the deposit: <b class="gd-ui">Deduct the balance owed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Deduct the late fee</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Release in full</b>. A card hold that has expired is marked settled at once (released by expiry: no money moves).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">If no deposit was taken, an Admin fills <b class="gd-ui">Admin: deposit not taken, waive it because</b> (the same field is in Record a past trip).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing is released by itself: the decision waits under <b class="gd-ui">Deposit decisions waiting for an Admin</b>, and an Admin presses <b class="gd-ui">Release</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Release now (tolls window)</b>).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-return-charges" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Return charges</h2><p class="gd-p">A late return is charged per started extra day at the booking&#39;s full daily cost (the rental per day after discounts, plus per-day and per-trip fees such as the Protection Plan, never delivery), and only the started hours after the whole days get the hourly late fee. On the booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab, each renter line not on a statement yet has <b class="gd-ui">Change amount</b> (lower) and <b class="gd-ui">Waive</b>, with the reason; it is in the booking history and the next assessment keeps it. An expired card hold after the return has <b class="gd-ui">Mark settled (released by expiry)</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-protection-plan-priced-from-rentalcover-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Protection Plan priced from RentalCover (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">The Protection Plan stays our product: renters never see the RentalCover name. Without the RentalCover partner key it is priced from the Protection Plan table, as before. Once the key is set, its price comes from a real RentalCover quote for the renter (their dates, their age at pickup, their name and email) plus our markup (20% unless <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b> changes it). The request form asks for the quote once the renter&#39;s details are in, and an offer as you choose option 3; a quote is reused for 15 minutes. A price you type for the plan wins. If RentalCover does not answer, the table price applies.</p><p class="gd-p">RentalCover covers up to $50,000 an incident, so the plan is offered only for a car worth less. The value used: your override under <b class="gd-ui">Value for the Protection Plan</b> on the car&#39;s page when set, else the car&#39;s Canadian Black Book value, else an AI estimate from typical listing prices that the site makes by itself (<b class="gd-ui">Refresh the AI estimate</b> asks again). A car with no value counts as over the limit: the request form, the offer screen and the database then offer only OPCF 27 or credit card coverage.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-extensions-at-the-all-in-price-a-day-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Extensions at the all-in price a day (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">An extension costs what the renter already pays, averaged per day: the booking&#39;s total for the booked period (the rental after discounts, every fee, one-time fees like delivery included, and HST) divided by its days, for each added day. A booking of $729.36 for 7 days costs $104.19 for each added day. Added hours under a day cost the hourly late fee with HST, never more than a day. There is no extension discount.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Where</th><th scope="col">What happens</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The renter&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Extend</b> page</td><td>Each option shows the total and the price a day before paying</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> on a confirmed or on-trip booking, made longer</td><td>The booking&#39;s new total is the all-in price of the longer stay; the per-trip fees stay as booked and the rental charge takes the difference</td></tr><tr><td>The next period of a long rental</td><td>Keeps the rate of the booked period (the rental a day, per-trip fees scaled)</td></tr><tr><td>An insurer-billed booking</td><td>Priced as before</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="gd-p">The extension is one line on the booking, &quot;Extension: 3 days at $104.19/day (all-in)&quot;, HST included. Its HST is the booking&#39;s own share of HST, so invoices and the books never add HST on top. Type a rental charge in <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> to set another price. Late returns are unchanged: the daily cost of each extra day and the hourly late fee.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-a-fixed-amount-per-payment-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A fixed amount per payment (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a weekly, every 2 weeks or monthly plan, an Admin can set <b class="gd-ui">Fixed amount per payment</b> in <b class="gd-ui">Change the plan</b>. Each payment is that amount and the last one takes the remainder. The total and the payments already made never change. Leave it empty to split the payments by the days again.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-request-as-sent-and-every-offer-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The request as sent and every offer (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a request or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Original request, as the renter sent it</b> shows the car, dates, places, coverage, add-ons, note and the price the renter saw, exactly as sent; staff changes never touch it. <b class="gd-ui">Offer history</b> lists every offer version, newest first: its status, who sent it and when, the car and dates, the message, how the total moved, and the price breakdown.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">To go back to an old version, press <b class="gd-ui">Revert to this offer</b> on it. Its car, dates, price, deposit, discount and fees load into the review as a new offer, highlighted.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the price, then send it in step 3. Nothing changes until you send.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The <b class="gd-ui">Coverage</b> line at the top says what the renter chose (own insurance OPCF 27, credit card, Protection Plan) and its proof: not sent yet, waiting for review, confirmed, or rejected with the reason.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-send-an-offer-in-three-steps-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send an offer in three steps (release 35)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Car and dates</b>: the renter, the dates, the car and where they pick it up and return it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Price</b>: filled in from the rate sheet with the checkout&#39;s fees and discounts. Change it only if you agreed another price.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Review and send</b>: what changed, the message and how the link goes.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Rarely used options (billing an insurer, how it is paid, the calendar) are under <b class="gd-ui">More options</b>. Send waits while the price is being worked out again after a date change, and one tap sends once.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-owner-s-own-trip-instant-bookings-and-book-it-now-releas" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The owner&#39;s own trip, instant bookings and Book it now (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Owner&#39;s own trip ($0)</b>: the owner booked their own car. There is nothing to price or send; get the car ready.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Instant (repeat renter)</b>: a Gold renter or above (Rewards, release 40) with a verified licence and nothing owing booked an available car at once and went straight to sign and pay. An Admin can take a renter&#39;s instant booking away from the booking page.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Any car, any time</b> (release 40): a Platinum renter asked for dates the car shows as taken. Fleet gets an urgent task due within 4 hours: confirm it, offer an equivalent car or an upgrade, or decline with a reason. Never cancel or move another renter&#39;s confirmed booking for it. The task closes when the request is answered.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Book it now</b> pressed by staff waits for an Admin&#39;s one-tap approval.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-secondary-contact-and-rideshare-documents-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Secondary contact and rideshare documents (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">The booking shows the renter&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Secondary contact</b> when they gave one: call them when the renter cannot be reached. Rideshare and delivery driving are welcome (rental agreement, section 10.3): never tell a renter it is not allowed. When a renter makes <b class="gd-ui">rideshare documents</b> (Uber, Lyft, DoorDash and others), you get an alert and the booking shows the letters they made.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-offers-coverage-delivery-and-fuel-releases-35-and-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Offers, coverage, delivery and fuel (releases 35 and 36)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Sending an offer is three steps: car and dates, price, review and send. Every request shows the renter&#39;s original request as sent and every offer version, with who sent it and when; reverting loads an old version as a new offer to send.</li><li>Instant booking: a verified Gold renter or above books an available car at once, signs and pays; the booking is marked Instant (repeat renter), and an Admin can take instant booking away from a renter.</li><li>Card coverage is checked against the car: the card, the car&#39;s value, its type and the rental length. A card that does not cover it cannot be approved. OPCF 27 needs both the pink slip and the endorsement page.</li><li>Delivery is priced by distance from the company&#39;s address (1570 Midland Ave, Scarborough): a base, the kilometres included and a rate per km, all in Program settings; a car&#39;s own fee stays as an override.</li><li>The fuel line at the return is suggested from the car&#39;s tank, the weekly pump price and a multiplier, plus the refuelling fee, and checked on the deposit review before any charge.</li><li>Owner price limits: the daily minimum and maximum of a car or an owner hold every price, discount and offer; only an Admin can allow one request outside them, with a reason.</li><li>Rideshare and delivery work is allowed with the documents the renter makes on their booking page (rental agreement copy, coverage letter, vehicle letter); staff get an alert when they are made. The secondary contact shows on the booking.</li><li>Mid-trip review ask: halfway through a trip of several days, the renter gets one short message asking how it is going; a problem they report becomes a To do for customer service.</li><li>A car that has only test bookings can be deleted by an Admin; the test bookings go with it. A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-check-in-and-check-out-on-one-screen-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Start the check-in (pickup)</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Start the check-out (return)</b> on the booking, and <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Check out</b> on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car&#39;s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Photos are one tap each: <b class="gd-ui">Take this photo</b> always shows the next angle.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example &quot;Next: Odometer&quot;) and takes you to it. When everything is in, press <b class="gd-ui">Hand over the keys</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Complete the return</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)</b> is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-a-late-return-is-a-choice-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A late return is a choice (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p">A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Late return</b> with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge as an extension</b>: every started day late at the booking&#39;s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge extra days</b>: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge the late return fee</b>: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge a custom amount</b>: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Waive it</b>: no charge, with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the late return charge</b>. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.</p><p class="gd-p">Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do <b class="gd-ui">Late return: choose the charge</b>. Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do <b class="gd-ui">Late return: approve the charge</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Approve as asked</b>, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">On <b class="gd-ui">Close ended trips</b>, marking a trip returned late and choosing <b class="gd-ui">Deduct the late fee</b> is the same choice of the late return fee, made there. The other deposit choices leave the late return to be chosen on the booking.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'customer-service', 'chapter', 'your-workday', 'You answer requests with offers, quote callers, reply to renters, look renters up, and review owner forms. You are often the renter''s first person. There is no commission for customer service, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Requests, New quote, Renter messages, Find a renter, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Owners and enquiries, Owner forms and Scorecard.

## Answer a request

1. Open **Requests and offers**: one queue (the numbers at the top are filters; **Active** always shows everything), the most urgent first, with how long each renter has waited, the countdown to the 2 hours the site promises, the car''s photo, the renter with **Call** and **Text**, the licence and one button (**Send offer**, **Follow up** or **Open**). Filter by Active, New, Asked the renter, Changes asked, Offer out, Not paid or Expired; an expired offer moves to Expired after 48 hours.
2. Waiting shows how long the renter has waited. Open the booking number.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-03-requests-desktop-b3c66d25.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 640; address: carmacars.ca/va/requests; pins: 1 27.1 17.5, 2 52.8 32.8")

3. On the Review tab, check the request: the car is free, the renter, the places.
4. Press **Adjust the booking** to change the car, dates, places, price or extras, then **Save changes**.
5. Add a message and press **Send the offer**. Within your limit you can also use **Approve (within my limit)** or **Approve and send the pay link**.
6. Can''t do it? **Decline** with Reason and any alternative. Need to know more? **Ask the renter**.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-04-booking-review-desktop-52c68a73.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1000; address: carmacars.ca/va/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review; pins: 3 69.4 24.0, 4 95.8 98.0")

> Tip: Reply within 5 minutes: send the offer, or ask the renter what you need. That is the "First reply in opening hours" measure on your scorecard. Requests waiting longer show in red.

Opening a request takes it for you: the others see "Being answered by" your name and cannot answer it until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work). One someone else holds shows who, with the buttons off; it opens to you when their claim runs out, or ask an Admin to take it over. Sales: a request from the website shows "Opens to you at" a time for its first 15 minutes, and a To do task says when it opens; after that whoever opens it first answers it, customer service included.

## An enquiry on an example car

Some cars on the site are marked "Example car": samples that show the kind of cars we rent. A request on one is an enquiry, never a booking.

1. The task Suggest a similar real car comes to To do with the enquiry number (EQ-1001 and up), the car asked for, the dates and the contact. When a real car was free for those dates, the task names it after **Free:** (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price), and the person was told we have a similar car and will confirm it within 2 hours.
2. Check the named car is still right for them (or find a real car of the same kind and price that is free for those dates), and make a **New quote** for it.
3. Call or email the person with the car and the price, then mark the task done.

> Tip: Reply within the first reply target, as for any request. Never offer the example car itself: it does not exist.

## A request from a vehicle page

Every make, model, year and trim page (carmacars.ca/cars/toyota/rav4/2023/xle, for example) has Request it, for the exact car the person wants.

1. The request arrives as an enquiry with the car named in the message ("About the car: 2023 Toyota RAV4 XLE") and an Enquiry task in To do.
2. If we have that car, or one close to it, free for their dates, make a **New quote** for it. If not, suggest the nearest car of the same kind and price.
3. Reply by email or phone, then mark the task done.

> Tip: The pages say only what the data says: EPA fuel use, the Canadian trims and our own cars. Never promise equipment the page does not list.

## A buyer lead from a /buy page

Every vehicle page has a for-sale twin (carmacars.ca/buy/toyota/rav4/2023/xle) with "Find me this car", and twins for financing, detailing and body shop work with their own request: a name, an email or phone, and when.

1. The lead is in **Buyer leads** (customer service: **Owners and enquiries**), Buyer leads (kind buyer, finance, detailing or body shop), with the car and what they asked, and a To do line for Sales: A buyer asked us to find a car, Someone asked about financing or leasing a car, A detailing request, or A body shop request.
2. If one of our cars of that kind is for sale (an Admin flags it with its price), offer it. If not, offer to rent them the car for a week first, and say what we can find. We do not lend or lease: on a financing question, say so and offer the rental. For detailing or body shop work, give a time and a price, and always offer a rental while their car is in (an insurance replacement rental when it is a claim). For mechanical work (a "Mechanical work to arrange" task: an oil change, brakes, tires, a tow and the like), CarmaCars does not do the work: book it with a trusted shop or recommend one, never promise the shop''s price or time, and offer a rental while their car is in.
3. Press **Take it**, then **Update** as you go: contacted, qualified, converted or closed with the reason.

> Tip: We mostly rent cars. Never say a car is for sale unless an Admin flagged it; the page shows it with its price when one is.

## Send an offer to a caller

Open **Send an offer** (or **Send an offer** beside a car in Find a car). No request needed: one screen, and the renter has the link.

1. Find the customer by name, phone or email, or press **Add a new customer**: full legal name, mobile, email and date of birth. Already on file with that email or phone? Use them: never a second record.
2. Choose the car (by car code, plate or name; each says Free or Not free), the dates and the places.
3. The price: the rate sheet, a total or a rate per day, with the reason for a price you type. The deposit, discounts and fees are set by an Admin; customer service sets the Protection Plan price. Amounts I type, at the top of the price: Before tax, or After tax (HST included) to type what the renter pays, worked back to before tax for you. Or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out from it.
4. How the rental and the deposit are paid (card online, e-Transfer, cash, platform payout, the insurer; deposit by card hold, cash or e-Transfer), who found this client, the message, how long it is open (48 hours at most) and Email, Text or both.
5. Check the offer as the renter will see it on the right, then press **Send the offer**.

> Tip: An offer that is out is changed in place: **More actions** > **Edit the offer**, change it, then **Save and send the update** or **Save without telling the renter**. No need to withdraw it first.

## New quote for a caller

1. Open **New quote**. Choose the Car, the Pickup and Return (at least 2 hours from now).
2. Choose how the lead came in, then the caller''s Full legal name, Email, Mobile and Date of birth.
3. Set the Licence class and Damage cover, and note places, extras and what they asked.
4. Press **Create the request**. It opens like any request; send the offer from there.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-05-new-quote-desktop-4e386b1c.jpg "desktop; size: 1220 1260; address: carmacars.ca/va/quotes/new; pins: 1 72.1 15.6, 2 72.1 41.7, 3 72.1 72.7, 4 63.9 85.5")

## Edit a booking, a fee or the renter

A booking that is confirmed, on trip or returned is edited directly; the renter''s details are corrected from the booking.

1. Overview, **Edit the booking**: the return (extend or shorten), the car, the rental charge, each fee, the kilometres and the note. Tick **Email the renter what changed**, or leave it off for a silent correction.
2. Money tab, Fees, **Change or add a fee**: a fee forgotten (the young driver fee shows its price for the dates) or a charge of its own.
3. What is open shows at once: **Email a pay link** or **Text a pay link** for exactly that amount, or record cash or an e-Transfer (Rental charges, Collect (the amount) rental, **Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)**).
4. **Edit renter**: a wrong email, phone, name, licence or address. A new email is their sign-in at once.
5. The same renter twice? Under the renter, Possible duplicates: **Merge into this record** moves everything of the other record here.

> Good to know: Each edit is recorded with your name, the time, the reason and the before and after.

## Renter messages and Find a renter

1. **Renter messages** lists the latest messages with their booking. Open the booking to reply, then press **Send**.
2. **Find a renter**: search by name, email, phone or booking number.
3. To open a renter''s private details, press **Open with a reason**. The reason is kept in the access log.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-06-messages-desktop-3441fa91.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 260; address: carmacars.ca/va/messages; pins: 1 32.6 48.5")

## Add a car for an owner

Open **Owners** > **Add a car for an owner** (fleet: under Cars). You enter everything for the owner; they never fill in the application.

1. The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.
2. The car: type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line with the year, make, model, trim and details (Edit if something is wrong). No VIN at hand: add it by its plate and choose the year, make and model. Tap the colour and check the class. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender''s information if you have them. Photos are optional.
3. Terms and first invoice: what was agreed with the owner, to the cent. An Admin checks them before anything is sent.
4. Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner. The owner signs in the owner portal after one email (no paper signature).
5. Press **Add the car and send to an Admin**. The application waits in the Admin''s Applications, marked Entered by staff with your name. When the Admin approves, the owner gets one email to review and sign.

> Good to know: A fleet supplier (a corporation leasing its cars to CarmaCars): choose New owner, **A corporation**, then Route **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**. The default lease terms are set at once. For the car, enter the VIN, the plate and the ownership copy, choose its tier, **Regular** or **Troubled** (it is set once), and who it is registered to now (for a car moving in or bought, the name and address on the ownership and the date). Its ServiceOntario forms are filled in at once. No terms, no invoices and no paper signing: the supplier signs in the owner portal. The car goes on the lease when an Admin approves it.

## Owners: the checklist, the photos and the forms (release 34)

Open **Owners** (customer service and fleet), then an owner. Search finds any owner by name, email, plate or VIN.

1. The **Onboarding checklist**: per car, each step done, to do (and who it waits on), blocked (and why) or not needed, with the one button to press.
2. **Onboarding photos**: **Replace** or **Remove** (with a reason) a wrong ownership permit, insurance slip or lender''s letter, or **Approve** or mark it **Not accepted** (the owner reads why). A replaced photo is checked again.
3. **Government forms**: each ServiceOntario form the car needs, made by themselves, with its status, the date it was made and its download.
4. **Add cars from a list of VINs** for the owner: paste or upload, **Preview**, **Add**.

## Owner forms (Forms C and D)

1. Open **Owner forms**. Each row is a scan an owner uploaded before November 2026 (Forms C and D are signed on screen since then), with the witnesses and the status.
2. Press Open to read the scan. Check every page is there and signed, with each witness''s signature and name.
3. Press **Approve**, or **Send back** with What to fix (the owner reads this).

![](/guides/img/va-cs-08-owner-forms-desktop-eceaee0b.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 300; address: carmacars.ca/va/owner-forms; pins: 2 68.6 36.7, 3 76.7 36.7")

## Rental agreements are signed online only

A rental agreement, or a booking change, is signed by the renter in their portal or on the phone at the handover (the e-signature). A copy signed on paper is not accepted or recorded: send the renter the link again from the booking. One recorded before November 2026 stays readable under Signed on paper.

## Signatures on the spot, or by link

A renter or an additional driver who has not signed yet.

1. On the booking, press **Sign now on this device**. Confirm the name and that you saw the original licence, then **Hand the device to** the signer.
2. Or press **Email the signing link** or **Text the signing link**: they sign on their own phone.
3. The licence comes first: the renter uploads it from the request, and the offer cannot be accepted without it.

## The booking''s rental agreements

The Rental agreements card keeps both agreements in step with the booking.

1. Any change after signing makes a new version by itself. A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage waits for the renter''s signature: they get the link by email and text, and the card says "Agreement v3 waiting for signature".
2. **Resend the signing links**, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your device.
3. Fields still blank (a licence expiry, an insurer''s policy number) are listed: type them and press **Save the missing fields**. Check-in stops on a field a claim needs until it is filled or an Admin overrides.
4. Every signature: a code to the signer''s phone or email, the key terms initialled, three consents, a drawn signature.

## Check renter documents

The renter''s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage, before the handover.

1. Open the task "identity documents or coverage proof to review", or open the booking: **Review** shows the documents of any booking being arranged or under way, with no task needed.
2. Every licence image, selfie and proof of coverage of the booking is on one screen, with what to check written once above them: the selfie matches, no alteration, the coverage is active to the return date.
3. Under each driver, the licence reader lists what it read (from the back''s barcode, else the photo) and one line per check, Pass or Flag: photos sharp and whole, valid to the return, class accepted, old enough at pickup, name and date of birth match the driver, the Ontario number, front and back the same licence, and the main driver''s Ontario licence. Look closely at each Flag.
4. One is wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**.
5. Then press **Approve all**: everything still waiting is approved at once (the Protection Plan too). A document the system refuses is named with the reason; the rest are approved.

> Tip: Each opening is logged. An Admin can do the same from Admin > To do. Field staff review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from their My jobs: the booking history says the role, field.

> Good to know: Main driver: Ontario licence needed. When the main driver''s licence is from elsewhere, they are moved to additional driver (their photos and checks stay; you still review them) and pickup is blocked until a driver with an Ontario licence is the main driver. The renter adds one from their booking. Only an Admin can undo the swap or let it go with a reason.

## Which credit cards include rental car coverage?

Renters ask this often. **Renters** > **Card coverage** (every function has it under Rentals or Bookings) is your quick reference: what to say, what to check, and the list.

1. Send the renter `carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage`: each card''s car value limit (MSRP), longest rental, key exclusions, its official guide and the day we last checked it.
2. Ask which car they want. Most Canadian cards stop at a car priced $65,000 or $85,000, and many luxury models are priced higher. Give them the car''s model year and trim so they can check.
3. Never tell a renter they are covered. Their card''s issuer decides that: ask them to call the number on the back of their card about this car and these dates. CarmaCars does not decide claims.
4. Over the limit, an excluded make, a debit card or a longer rental than the card allows: offer OPCF 27 on their own auto policy or the CarmaCars Protection Plan.

> Tip: A card marked Unverified came from a published summary, not the issuer''s guide. Something wrong or out of date in the list? Tell an Admin: they correct it in Settings > Card coverage.

## Review requests

Renters are asked for a review by email and text after each trip. **Renters** > **Review requests** shows the ones on hold and the Google reviews to match.

1. On hold: the booking has a charge that is not settled or waived yet (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls) or an open incident. It leaves the list by itself once the charges are settled or waived.
2. The renter should be asked now anyway? Press **Send anyway**. Should never be asked? Press **Do not ask**.
3. Google reviews: a possible match to a renter shows "possible match". Press **Confirm** if it is them, **Not this renter** if not, or **Match to a booking** with the booking number.
4. A review that came another way (Turo, a text, a call, email): press **Add a customer review** and type the customer''s first name and last initial, the source, the date received, the rating and their words exactly as received, with a screenshot if you have one. It shows on the site with its source. Never write or change a review for a customer.
5. On a booking, the card Review requests has **Ask for a review** (for example after a call that went well) and **Mark reviewed** when the renter says they already left one.

> Tip: Never offer anything for a review and never ask only happy renters: everyone gets the same message and the same Google link.

## A change to a confirmed booking

On a booking''s Changes tab you can propose new dates, times or another car, as an Admin does: set the change, write the reason, press **Preview the price**, then **Send to the renter**. The renter has 48 hours to accept and sign the amendment. You also send a new signing link to an additional driver from the booking screen.

## A late return

A booking past its return time shows the late return panel. The renter can still extend in their booking while they have the car: the extension counts from the original return time, it is approved at once when the car is free, and paying it stops the late notices. Point them to **Extend** first. Otherwise work it in order:

| Button | When |
| --- | --- |
| **Log a call** | Record each call to the renter and what they said. |
| **Send T13** | The first late notice email. |
| **Send T14 (final notice)** | The final notice. |
| **Request disable** | Ask an Admin to approve disabling the car. |
| **Open an incident** | When the car is not coming back as planned. |

## Booked when the renter accepts (release 28)

A renter who approves the offer has booked the car, even before paying: the booking shows **Booked, payment due** and holds the car everywhere. Collect the payment before the pickup (a **Booked, payment due** To do comes 48 hours before). When you send an offer, the renter''s view is right under **Send the offer**.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Book it now (release 33)
When you send an offer, tick **Book it now (no renter approval)** when the renter has already agreed. The offer goes out and an Admin approves it in one tap: the booking then waits for payment, the car is held, and the renter gets one link to sign and pay. You can also have them sign and pay with you: open the booking, **Sign now on this device**, then take the card on this device.
Already sent the offer? Ask the assistant: "Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the customer agreed by phone". It shows a card; **Confirm** sends the same request to an Admin, who approves in one tap.

## Change protection (release 41)

On the booking page, the **Protection** card at the top has one button: **Change protection**.

1. Pick the option. Each shows the price difference, the deposit and what the renter provides. Credit card coverage needs the renter''s card from the coverage list (one that covers this car) and their confirmation that they pay with it; OPCF 27 needs their confirmation that they upload their policy. If the rule says no, ask an Admin: only an Admin can override, with a reason.
2. Write the reason (required; the renter reads it) and press **Change protection**. The price changes at once: more to pay is a balance to collect on the Money tab, nothing is charged by itself. An offer is sent again; a confirmed booking gets one email and the amended agreement.

When a renter asks to leave the Protection Plan, the card shows their proof: **Approve**, or **Decline** with a note. Sales changes requests and offers only.

## Unanswered

**More customer service** > **Unanswered**: every customer text with no reply and every missed call not called back, oldest first. Reply or call back from the row; **Mark answered** when it was answered another way. After 15 minutes the team is alerted. Check WhatsApp by hand each morning.

## The request as sent and every offer (release 35)

On a request or a booking, **Original request, as the renter sent it** shows the car, dates, places, coverage, add-ons, note and the price the renter saw, exactly as sent; staff changes never touch it. **Offer history** lists every offer version, newest first: its status, who sent it and when, the car and dates, the message, how the total moved, and the price breakdown.

1. To go back to an old version, press **Revert to this offer** on it. Its car, dates, price, deposit, discount and fees load into the review as a new offer, highlighted.
2. Check the price, then send it in step 3. Nothing changes until you send.

The **Coverage** line at the top says what the renter chose (own insurance OPCF 27, credit card, Protection Plan) and its proof: not sent yet, waiting for review, confirmed, or rejected with the reason.

## Send an offer in three steps (release 35)

1. **Car and dates**: the renter, the dates, the car and where they pick it up and return it.
2. **Price**: filled in from the rate sheet with the checkout''s fees and discounts. Change it only if you agreed another price.
3. **Review and send**: what changed, the message and how the link goes.

Rarely used options (billing an insurer, how it is paid, the calendar) are under **More options**. Send waits while the price is being worked out again after a date change, and one tap sends once.

## The owner''s own trip, instant bookings and Book it now (release 35)

- **Owner''s own trip ($0)**: the owner booked their own car. There is nothing to price or send; get the car ready.
- **Instant (repeat renter)**: a Gold renter or above (Rewards) with a verified licence and nothing owing booked an available car at once and went straight to sign and pay. An Admin can take a renter''s instant booking away from the booking page.
- **Any car, any time**: a Platinum renter''s request on taken dates is a priority request. Fleet answers within 4 hours: confirm, offer an equivalent car or an upgrade, or decline with a reason. Never cancel or move another renter''s booking for it.
- **Book it now** pressed by staff waits for an Admin''s one-tap approval.

## Secondary contact and rideshare documents (release 35)

The booking shows the renter''s **Secondary contact** when they gave one: call them when the renter cannot be reached. Rideshare and delivery driving are welcome (rental agreement, section 10.3): never tell a renter it is not allowed. When a renter makes **rideshare documents** (Uber, Lyft, DoorDash and others), you get an alert and the booking shows the letters they made.

## Automatic answers (release 36)

Common questions by text, email, WhatsApp, Facebook and Instagram are answered by themselves from the FAQ. **Renter messages** > **Automatic answers** shows what was answered and what was left for a person. A question the FAQ does not answer stays for you: texts in Messages, emails and Meta messages as a To do, **Answer** and the question. Once you text someone, no automatic answer goes to them for 2 hours.

## The card the renter picked, and the two OPCF 27 pages (release 35)

On **Review documents** for a booking:

1. **Option 2**: **Card picked** names the card the renter chose from the list (or typed when it was not listed), and **Card check** says whether it covers this car: *Covers this car*, *Check it* (a card not on the list, a card whose coverage or value limit we do not know, or a car with no value on file) or *Does NOT cover this car* with the reason. **Approve** is refused while the card does not cover the car.
2. **Option 1**: each page says what it is: **pink slip** or **OPCF 27 endorsement**. **Approve** is refused until both are in. **Reject** needs the reason the renter sees.
3. A renter on OPCF 27 cannot pay until both pages are uploaded, so you see them before the booking is confirmed.

> Tip: Uploading a renter''s insurance yourself? In **Upload a document**, choose **Which page**: Pink slip or OPCF 27 endorsement page.

## Calls, auto-replies and coverage (releases 35 and 36)

- Calls from the Call button are recorded; the transcript, summary and Play recording are on the renter''s, lead''s and booking''s history. Quo calls show their transcript and summary there too.
- Automatic answers reply to common questions on every channel from our FAQ. A question they cannot answer becomes your To do: answer it yourself.
- Card coverage: the renter picks their card and the page checks it against the car. Approve OPCF 27 only with both the pink slip and the endorsement page.
- Rideshare and delivery work is allowed with the documents the renter makes on their booking; the secondary contact is on the booking.
- The mid-trip message asks the renter how the trip is going; a problem reported becomes your To do.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A lead you handle on a call (release 37)

When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in **Settings** > **Sales**). Every call you handle adds the time again.

- Sales see **Being handled by** your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and **Next lead** skips it.
- Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.
- When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can **Release hold** earlier.
- A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.
- Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.

## The person behind the lead (release 40)

On **Leads**, press **The person** on a card, or open the lead, to see the whole person: contact, account and licence verified (yes or no), bookings and balances, deposit, requests and offers, earlier leads, messages, calls and texts, notes, reviews, incidents, who has handled them, and the **Signals** timeline of everything they did with us. Outside the renter''s window you see it in full while you hold the lead on a call; otherwise you see the contact and account.', 'Customer service', 'Requests and offers, new quotes, renter messages, find a renter, owner forms, late returns.',
  'You answer requests with offers, quote callers, reply to renters, look renters up, and review owner forms. You are often the renter''s first person. There is no commission for customer service, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Requests, New quote, Renter messages, Find a renter, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Owners and enquiries, Owner forms and Scorecard.

## Answer a request

1. Open **Requests and offers**: one queue (the numbers at the top are filters; **Active** always shows everything), the most urgent first, with how long each renter has waited, the countdown to the 2 hours the site promises, the car''s photo, the renter with **Call** and **Text**, the licence and one button (**Send offer**, **Follow up** or **Open**). Filter by Active, New, Asked the renter, Changes asked, Offer out, Not paid or Expired; an expired offer moves to Expired after 48 hours.
2. Waiting shows how long the renter has waited. Open the booking number.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-03-requests-desktop-b3c66d25.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 640; address: carmacars.ca/va/requests; pins: 1 27.1 17.5, 2 52.8 32.8")

3. On the Review tab, check the request: the car is free, the renter, the places.
4. Press **Adjust the booking** to change the car, dates, places, price or extras, then **Save changes**.
5. Add a message and press **Send the offer**. Within your limit you can also use **Approve (within my limit)** or **Approve and send the pay link**.
6. Can''t do it? **Decline** with Reason and any alternative. Need to know more? **Ask the renter**.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-04-booking-review-desktop-52c68a73.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1000; address: carmacars.ca/va/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review; pins: 3 69.4 24.0, 4 95.8 98.0")

> Tip: Reply within 5 minutes: send the offer, or ask the renter what you need. That is the "First reply in opening hours" measure on your scorecard. Requests waiting longer show in red.

Opening a request takes it for you: the others see "Being answered by" your name and cannot answer it until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work). One someone else holds shows who, with the buttons off; it opens to you when their claim runs out, or ask an Admin to take it over. Sales: a request from the website shows "Opens to you at" a time for its first 15 minutes, and a To do task says when it opens; after that whoever opens it first answers it, customer service included.

## An enquiry on an example car

Some cars on the site are marked "Example car": samples that show the kind of cars we rent. A request on one is an enquiry, never a booking.

1. The task Suggest a similar real car comes to To do with the enquiry number (EQ-1001 and up), the car asked for, the dates and the contact. When a real car was free for those dates, the task names it after **Free:** (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price), and the person was told we have a similar car and will confirm it within 2 hours.
2. Check the named car is still right for them (or find a real car of the same kind and price that is free for those dates), and make a **New quote** for it.
3. Call or email the person with the car and the price, then mark the task done.

> Tip: Reply within the first reply target, as for any request. Never offer the example car itself: it does not exist.

## A request from a vehicle page

Every make, model, year and trim page (carmacars.ca/cars/toyota/rav4/2023/xle, for example) has Request it, for the exact car the person wants.

1. The request arrives as an enquiry with the car named in the message ("About the car: 2023 Toyota RAV4 XLE") and an Enquiry task in To do.
2. If we have that car, or one close to it, free for their dates, make a **New quote** for it. If not, suggest the nearest car of the same kind and price.
3. Reply by email or phone, then mark the task done.

> Tip: The pages say only what the data says: EPA fuel use, the Canadian trims and our own cars. Never promise equipment the page does not list.

## A buyer lead from a /buy page

Every vehicle page has a for-sale twin (carmacars.ca/buy/toyota/rav4/2023/xle) with "Find me this car", and twins for financing, detailing and body shop work with their own request: a name, an email or phone, and when.

1. The lead is in **Buyer leads** (customer service: **Owners and enquiries**), Buyer leads (kind buyer, finance, detailing or body shop), with the car and what they asked, and a To do line for Sales: A buyer asked us to find a car, Someone asked about financing or leasing a car, A detailing request, or A body shop request.
2. If one of our cars of that kind is for sale (an Admin flags it with its price), offer it. If not, offer to rent them the car for a week first, and say what we can find. We do not lend or lease: on a financing question, say so and offer the rental. For detailing or body shop work, give a time and a price, and always offer a rental while their car is in (an insurance replacement rental when it is a claim). For mechanical work (a "Mechanical work to arrange" task: an oil change, brakes, tires, a tow and the like), CarmaCars does not do the work: book it with a trusted shop or recommend one, never promise the shop''s price or time, and offer a rental while their car is in.
3. Press **Take it**, then **Update** as you go: contacted, qualified, converted or closed with the reason.

> Tip: We mostly rent cars. Never say a car is for sale unless an Admin flagged it; the page shows it with its price when one is.

## Send an offer to a caller

Open **Send an offer** (or **Send an offer** beside a car in Find a car). No request needed: one screen, and the renter has the link.

1. Find the customer by name, phone or email, or press **Add a new customer**: full legal name, mobile, email and date of birth. Already on file with that email or phone? Use them: never a second record.
2. Choose the car (by car code, plate or name; each says Free or Not free), the dates and the places.
3. The price: the rate sheet, a total or a rate per day, with the reason for a price you type. The deposit, discounts and fees are set by an Admin; customer service sets the Protection Plan price. Amounts I type, at the top of the price: Before tax, or After tax (HST included) to type what the renter pays, worked back to before tax for you. Or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out from it.
4. How the rental and the deposit are paid (card online, e-Transfer, cash, platform payout, the insurer; deposit by card hold, cash or e-Transfer), who found this client, the message, how long it is open (48 hours at most) and Email, Text or both.
5. Check the offer as the renter will see it on the right, then press **Send the offer**.

> Tip: An offer that is out is changed in place: **More actions** > **Edit the offer**, change it, then **Save and send the update** or **Save without telling the renter**. No need to withdraw it first.

## New quote for a caller

1. Open **New quote**. Choose the Car, the Pickup and Return (at least 2 hours from now).
2. Choose how the lead came in, then the caller''s Full legal name, Email, Mobile and Date of birth.
3. Set the Licence class and Damage cover, and note places, extras and what they asked.
4. Press **Create the request**. It opens like any request; send the offer from there.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-05-new-quote-desktop-4e386b1c.jpg "desktop; size: 1220 1260; address: carmacars.ca/va/quotes/new; pins: 1 72.1 15.6, 2 72.1 41.7, 3 72.1 72.7, 4 63.9 85.5")

## Edit a booking, a fee or the renter

A booking that is confirmed, on trip or returned is edited directly; the renter''s details are corrected from the booking.

1. Overview, **Edit the booking**: the return (extend or shorten), the car, the rental charge, each fee, the kilometres and the note. Tick **Email the renter what changed**, or leave it off for a silent correction.
2. Money tab, Fees, **Change or add a fee**: a fee forgotten (the young driver fee shows its price for the dates) or a charge of its own.
3. What is open shows at once: **Email a pay link** or **Text a pay link** for exactly that amount, or record cash or an e-Transfer (Rental charges, Collect (the amount) rental, **Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)**).
4. **Edit renter**: a wrong email, phone, name, licence or address. A new email is their sign-in at once.
5. The same renter twice? Under the renter, Possible duplicates: **Merge into this record** moves everything of the other record here.

> Good to know: Each edit is recorded with your name, the time, the reason and the before and after.

## Renter messages and Find a renter

1. **Renter messages** lists the latest messages with their booking. Open the booking to reply, then press **Send**.
2. **Find a renter**: search by name, email, phone or booking number.
3. To open a renter''s private details, press **Open with a reason**. The reason is kept in the access log.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-06-messages-desktop-3441fa91.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 260; address: carmacars.ca/va/messages; pins: 1 32.6 48.5")

## Add a car for an owner

Open **Owners** > **Add a car for an owner** (fleet: under Cars). You enter everything for the owner; they never fill in the application.

1. The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.
2. The car: type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line with the year, make, model, trim and details (Edit if something is wrong). No VIN at hand: add it by its plate and choose the year, make and model. Tap the colour and check the class. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender''s information if you have them. Photos are optional.
3. Terms and first invoice: what was agreed with the owner, to the cent. An Admin checks them before anything is sent.
4. Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner. The owner signs in the owner portal after one email (no paper signature).
5. Press **Add the car and send to an Admin**. The application waits in the Admin''s Applications, marked Entered by staff with your name. When the Admin approves, the owner gets one email to review and sign.

> Good to know: A fleet supplier (a corporation leasing its cars to CarmaCars): choose New owner, **A corporation**, then Route **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**. The default lease terms are set at once. For the car, enter the VIN, the plate and the ownership copy, choose its tier, **Regular** or **Troubled** (it is set once), and who it is registered to now (for a car moving in or bought, the name and address on the ownership and the date). Its ServiceOntario forms are filled in at once. No terms, no invoices and no paper signing: the supplier signs in the owner portal. The car goes on the lease when an Admin approves it.

## Owners: the checklist, the photos and the forms (release 34)

Open **Owners** (customer service and fleet), then an owner. Search finds any owner by name, email, plate or VIN.

1. The **Onboarding checklist**: per car, each step done, to do (and who it waits on), blocked (and why) or not needed, with the one button to press.
2. **Onboarding photos**: **Replace** or **Remove** (with a reason) a wrong ownership permit, insurance slip or lender''s letter, or **Approve** or mark it **Not accepted** (the owner reads why). A replaced photo is checked again.
3. **Government forms**: each ServiceOntario form the car needs, made by themselves, with its status, the date it was made and its download.
4. **Add cars from a list of VINs** for the owner: paste or upload, **Preview**, **Add**.

## Owner forms (Forms C and D)

1. Open **Owner forms**. Each row is a scan an owner uploaded before November 2026 (Forms C and D are signed on screen since then), with the witnesses and the status.
2. Press Open to read the scan. Check every page is there and signed, with each witness''s signature and name.
3. Press **Approve**, or **Send back** with What to fix (the owner reads this).

![](/guides/img/va-cs-08-owner-forms-desktop-eceaee0b.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 300; address: carmacars.ca/va/owner-forms; pins: 2 68.6 36.7, 3 76.7 36.7")

## Rental agreements are signed online only

A rental agreement, or a booking change, is signed by the renter in their portal or on the phone at the handover (the e-signature). A copy signed on paper is not accepted or recorded: send the renter the link again from the booking. One recorded before November 2026 stays readable under Signed on paper.

## Signatures on the spot, or by link

A renter or an additional driver who has not signed yet.

1. On the booking, press **Sign now on this device**. Confirm the name and that you saw the original licence, then **Hand the device to** the signer.
2. Or press **Email the signing link** or **Text the signing link**: they sign on their own phone.
3. The licence comes first: the renter uploads it from the request, and the offer cannot be accepted without it.

## The booking''s rental agreements

The Rental agreements card keeps both agreements in step with the booking.

1. Any change after signing makes a new version by itself. A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage waits for the renter''s signature: they get the link by email and text, and the card says "Agreement v3 waiting for signature".
2. **Resend the signing links**, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your device.
3. Fields still blank (a licence expiry, an insurer''s policy number) are listed: type them and press **Save the missing fields**. Check-in stops on a field a claim needs until it is filled or an Admin overrides.
4. Every signature: a code to the signer''s phone or email, the key terms initialled, three consents, a drawn signature.

## Check renter documents

The renter''s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage, before the handover.

1. Open the task "identity documents or coverage proof to review", or open the booking: **Review** shows the documents of any booking being arranged or under way, with no task needed.
2. Every licence image, selfie and proof of coverage of the booking is on one screen, with what to check written once above them: the selfie matches, no alteration, the coverage is active to the return date.
3. Under each driver, the licence reader lists what it read (from the back''s barcode, else the photo) and one line per check, Pass or Flag: photos sharp and whole, valid to the return, class accepted, old enough at pickup, name and date of birth match the driver, the Ontario number, front and back the same licence, and the main driver''s Ontario licence. Look closely at each Flag.
4. One is wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**.
5. Then press **Approve all**: everything still waiting is approved at once (the Protection Plan too). A document the system refuses is named with the reason; the rest are approved.

> Tip: Each opening is logged. An Admin can do the same from Admin > To do. Field staff review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from their My jobs: the booking history says the role, field.

> Good to know: Main driver: Ontario licence needed. When the main driver''s licence is from elsewhere, they are moved to additional driver (their photos and checks stay; you still review them) and pickup is blocked until a driver with an Ontario licence is the main driver. The renter adds one from their booking. Only an Admin can undo the swap or let it go with a reason.

## Which credit cards include rental car coverage?

Renters ask this often. **Renters** > **Card coverage** (every function has it under Rentals or Bookings) is your quick reference: what to say, what to check, and the list.

1. Send the renter `carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage`: each card''s car value limit (MSRP), longest rental, key exclusions, its official guide and the day we last checked it.
2. Ask which car they want. Most Canadian cards stop at a car priced $65,000 or $85,000, and many luxury models are priced higher. Give them the car''s model year and trim so they can check.
3. Never tell a renter they are covered. Their card''s issuer decides that: ask them to call the number on the back of their card about this car and these dates. CarmaCars does not decide claims.
4. Over the limit, an excluded make, a debit card or a longer rental than the card allows: offer OPCF 27 on their own auto policy or the CarmaCars Protection Plan.

> Tip: A card marked Unverified came from a published summary, not the issuer''s guide. Something wrong or out of date in the list? Tell an Admin: they correct it in Settings > Card coverage.

## Review requests

Renters are asked for a review by email and text after each trip. **Renters** > **Review requests** shows the ones on hold and the Google reviews to match.

1. On hold: the booking has a charge that is not settled or waived yet (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls) or an open incident. It leaves the list by itself once the charges are settled or waived.
2. The renter should be asked now anyway? Press **Send anyway**. Should never be asked? Press **Do not ask**.
3. Google reviews: a possible match to a renter shows "possible match". Press **Confirm** if it is them, **Not this renter** if not, or **Match to a booking** with the booking number.
4. A review that came another way (Turo, a text, a call, email): press **Add a customer review** and type the customer''s first name and last initial, the source, the date received, the rating and their words exactly as received, with a screenshot if you have one. It shows on the site with its source. Never write or change a review for a customer.
5. On a booking, the card Review requests has **Ask for a review** (for example after a call that went well) and **Mark reviewed** when the renter says they already left one.

> Tip: Never offer anything for a review and never ask only happy renters: everyone gets the same message and the same Google link.

## A change to a confirmed booking

On a booking''s Changes tab you can propose new dates, times or another car, as an Admin does: set the change, write the reason, press **Preview the price**, then **Send to the renter**. The renter has 48 hours to accept and sign the amendment. You also send a new signing link to an additional driver from the booking screen.

## A late return

A booking past its return time shows the late return panel. The renter can still extend in their booking while they have the car: the extension counts from the original return time, it is approved at once when the car is free, and paying it stops the late notices. Point them to **Extend** first. Otherwise work it in order:

| Button | When |
| --- | --- |
| **Log a call** | Record each call to the renter and what they said. |
| **Send T13** | The first late notice email. |
| **Send T14 (final notice)** | The final notice. |
| **Request disable** | Ask an Admin to approve disabling the car. |
| **Open an incident** | When the car is not coming back as planned. |

## Booked when the renter accepts (release 28)

A renter who approves the offer has booked the car, even before paying: the booking shows **Booked, payment due** and holds the car everywhere. Collect the payment before the pickup (a **Booked, payment due** To do comes 48 hours before). When you send an offer, the renter''s view is right under **Send the offer**.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Book it now (release 33)
When you send an offer, tick **Book it now (no renter approval)** when the renter has already agreed. The offer goes out and an Admin approves it in one tap: the booking then waits for payment, the car is held, and the renter gets one link to sign and pay. You can also have them sign and pay with you: open the booking, **Sign now on this device**, then take the card on this device.
Already sent the offer? Ask the assistant: "Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the customer agreed by phone". It shows a card; **Confirm** sends the same request to an Admin, who approves in one tap.

## Change protection (release 41)

On the booking page, the **Protection** card at the top has one button: **Change protection**.

1. Pick the option. Each shows the price difference, the deposit and what the renter provides. Credit card coverage needs the renter''s card from the coverage list (one that covers this car) and their confirmation that they pay with it; OPCF 27 needs their confirmation that they upload their policy. If the rule says no, ask an Admin: only an Admin can override, with a reason.
2. Write the reason (required; the renter reads it) and press **Change protection**. The price changes at once: more to pay is a balance to collect on the Money tab, nothing is charged by itself. An offer is sent again; a confirmed booking gets one email and the amended agreement.

When a renter asks to leave the Protection Plan, the card shows their proof: **Approve**, or **Decline** with a note. Sales changes requests and offers only.

## Unanswered

**More customer service** > **Unanswered**: every customer text with no reply and every missed call not called back, oldest first. Reply or call back from the row; **Mark answered** when it was answered another way. After 15 minutes the team is alerted. Check WhatsApp by hand each morning.

## The request as sent and every offer (release 35)

On a request or a booking, **Original request, as the renter sent it** shows the car, dates, places, coverage, add-ons, note and the price the renter saw, exactly as sent; staff changes never touch it. **Offer history** lists every offer version, newest first: its status, who sent it and when, the car and dates, the message, how the total moved, and the price breakdown.

1. To go back to an old version, press **Revert to this offer** on it. Its car, dates, price, deposit, discount and fees load into the review as a new offer, highlighted.
2. Check the price, then send it in step 3. Nothing changes until you send.

The **Coverage** line at the top says what the renter chose (own insurance OPCF 27, credit card, Protection Plan) and its proof: not sent yet, waiting for review, confirmed, or rejected with the reason.

## Send an offer in three steps (release 35)

1. **Car and dates**: the renter, the dates, the car and where they pick it up and return it.
2. **Price**: filled in from the rate sheet with the checkout''s fees and discounts. Change it only if you agreed another price.
3. **Review and send**: what changed, the message and how the link goes.

Rarely used options (billing an insurer, how it is paid, the calendar) are under **More options**. Send waits while the price is being worked out again after a date change, and one tap sends once.

## The owner''s own trip, instant bookings and Book it now (release 35)

- **Owner''s own trip ($0)**: the owner booked their own car. There is nothing to price or send; get the car ready.
- **Instant (repeat renter)**: a Gold renter or above (Rewards) with a verified licence and nothing owing booked an available car at once and went straight to sign and pay. An Admin can take a renter''s instant booking away from the booking page.
- **Any car, any time**: a Platinum renter''s request on taken dates is a priority request. Fleet answers within 4 hours: confirm, offer an equivalent car or an upgrade, or decline with a reason. Never cancel or move another renter''s booking for it.
- **Book it now** pressed by staff waits for an Admin''s one-tap approval.

## Secondary contact and rideshare documents (release 35)

The booking shows the renter''s **Secondary contact** when they gave one: call them when the renter cannot be reached. Rideshare and delivery driving are welcome (rental agreement, section 10.3): never tell a renter it is not allowed. When a renter makes **rideshare documents** (Uber, Lyft, DoorDash and others), you get an alert and the booking shows the letters they made.

## Automatic answers (release 36)

Common questions by text, email, WhatsApp, Facebook and Instagram are answered by themselves from the FAQ. **Renter messages** > **Automatic answers** shows what was answered and what was left for a person. A question the FAQ does not answer stays for you: texts in Messages, emails and Meta messages as a To do, **Answer** and the question. Once you text someone, no automatic answer goes to them for 2 hours.

## The card the renter picked, and the two OPCF 27 pages (release 35)

On **Review documents** for a booking:

1. **Option 2**: **Card picked** names the card the renter chose from the list (or typed when it was not listed), and **Card check** says whether it covers this car: *Covers this car*, *Check it* (a card not on the list, a card whose coverage or value limit we do not know, or a car with no value on file) or *Does NOT cover this car* with the reason. **Approve** is refused while the card does not cover the car.
2. **Option 1**: each page says what it is: **pink slip** or **OPCF 27 endorsement**. **Approve** is refused until both are in. **Reject** needs the reason the renter sees.
3. A renter on OPCF 27 cannot pay until both pages are uploaded, so you see them before the booking is confirmed.

> Tip: Uploading a renter''s insurance yourself? In **Upload a document**, choose **Which page**: Pink slip or OPCF 27 endorsement page.

## Calls, auto-replies and coverage (releases 35 and 36)

- Calls from the Call button are recorded; the transcript, summary and Play recording are on the renter''s, lead''s and booking''s history. Quo calls show their transcript and summary there too.
- Automatic answers reply to common questions on every channel from our FAQ. A question they cannot answer becomes your To do: answer it yourself.
- Card coverage: the renter picks their card and the page checks it against the car. Approve OPCF 27 only with both the pink slip and the endorsement page.
- Rideshare and delivery work is allowed with the documents the renter makes on their booking; the secondary contact is on the booking.
- The mid-trip message asks the renter how the trip is going; a problem reported becomes your To do.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A lead you handle on a call (release 37)

When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in **Settings** > **Sales**). Every call you handle adds the time again.

- Sales see **Being handled by** your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and **Next lead** skips it.
- Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.
- When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can **Release hold** earlier.
- A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.
- Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.

## The person behind the lead (release 40)

On **Leads**, press **The person** on a card, or open the lead, to see the whole person: contact, account and licence verified (yes or no), bookings and balances, deposit, requests and offers, earlier leads, messages, calls and texts, notes, reviews, incidents, who has handled them, and the **Signals** timeline of everything they did with us. Outside the renter''s window you see it in full while you hold the lead on a call; otherwise you see the contact and account.

## Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)

**Start the check-in (pickup)** and **Start the check-out (return)** on the booking, and **Check in** or **Check out** on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:

1. Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.
2. What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car''s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.
3. Photos are one tap each: **Take this photo** always shows the next angle.
4. What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.
5. The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you to it. When everything is in, press **Hand over the keys** or **Complete the return**.

Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.

**Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)** is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do **Late return: choose the charge**. Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do **Late return: approve the charge** and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.',
  '<p class="gd-p">You answer requests with offers, quote callers, reply to renters, look renters up, and review owner forms. You are often the renter&#39;s first person. There is no commission for customer service, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.</p><p class="gd-p">Your rail: Queue, Today, Requests, New quote, Renter messages, Find a renter, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Owners and enquiries, Owner forms and Scorecard.</p><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-answer-a-request" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Answer a request</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Requests and offers</b>: one queue (the numbers at the top are filters; <b class="gd-ui">Active</b> always shows everything), the most urgent first, with how long each renter has waited, the countdown to the 2 hours the site promises, the car&#39;s photo, the renter with <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>, the licence and one button (<b class="gd-ui">Send offer</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Follow up</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Open</b>). Filter by Active, New, Asked the renter, Changes asked, Offer out, Not paid or Expired; an expired offer moves to Expired after 48 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Waiting shows how long the renter has waited. Open the booking number.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/requests</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/640"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-03-requests-desktop-b3c66d25.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="640"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:27.1%;top:17.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:52.8%;top:32.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="3"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On the Review tab, check the request: the car is free, the renter, the places.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Adjust the booking</b> to change the car, dates, places, price or extras, then <b class="gd-ui">Save changes</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Add a message and press <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>. Within your limit you can also use <b class="gd-ui">Approve (within my limit)</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Approve and send the pay link</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Can&#39;t do it? <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with Reason and any alternative. Need to know more? <b class="gd-ui">Ask the renter</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1000"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-04-booking-review-desktop-52c68a73.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1000"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:69.4%;top:24%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:95.8%;top:98%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Reply within 5 minutes: send the offer, or ask the renter what you need. That is the &quot;First reply in opening hours&quot; measure on your scorecard. Requests waiting longer show in red.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">Opening a request takes it for you: the others see &quot;Being answered by&quot; your name and cannot answer it until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work). One someone else holds shows who, with the buttons off; it opens to you when their claim runs out, or ask an Admin to take it over. Sales: a request from the website shows &quot;Opens to you at&quot; a time for its first 15 minutes, and a To do task says when it opens; after that whoever opens it first answers it, customer service included.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-an-enquiry-on-an-example-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An enquiry on an example car</h2><p class="gd-p">Some cars on the site are marked &quot;Example car&quot;: samples that show the kind of cars we rent. A request on one is an enquiry, never a booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The task Suggest a similar real car comes to To do with the enquiry number (EQ-1001 and up), the car asked for, the dates and the contact. When a real car was free for those dates, the task names it after <b class="gd-ui">Free:</b> (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price), and the person was told we have a similar car and will confirm it within 2 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the named car is still right for them (or find a real car of the same kind and price that is free for those dates), and make a <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b> for it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Call or email the person with the car and the price, then mark the task done.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Reply within the first reply target, as for any request. Never offer the example car itself: it does not exist.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-request-from-a-vehicle-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A request from a vehicle page</h2><p class="gd-p">Every make, model, year and trim page (carmacars.ca/cars/toyota/rav4/2023/xle, for example) has Request it, for the exact car the person wants.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The request arrives as an enquiry with the car named in the message (&quot;About the car: 2023 Toyota RAV4 XLE&quot;) and an Enquiry task in To do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">If we have that car, or one close to it, free for their dates, make a <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b> for it. If not, suggest the nearest car of the same kind and price.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Reply by email or phone, then mark the task done.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The pages say only what the data says: EPA fuel use, the Canadian trims and our own cars. Never promise equipment the page does not list.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-buyer-lead-from-a-buy-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A buyer lead from a /buy page</h2><p class="gd-p">Every vehicle page has a for-sale twin (carmacars.ca/buy/toyota/rav4/2023/xle) with &quot;Find me this car&quot;, and twins for financing, detailing and body shop work with their own request: a name, an email or phone, and when.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The lead is in <b class="gd-ui">Buyer leads</b> (customer service: <b class="gd-ui">Owners and enquiries</b>), Buyer leads (kind buyer, finance, detailing or body shop), with the car and what they asked, and a To do line for Sales: A buyer asked us to find a car, Someone asked about financing or leasing a car, A detailing request, or A body shop request.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">If one of our cars of that kind is for sale (an Admin flags it with its price), offer it. If not, offer to rent them the car for a week first, and say what we can find. We do not lend or lease: on a financing question, say so and offer the rental. For detailing or body shop work, give a time and a price, and always offer a rental while their car is in (an insurance replacement rental when it is a claim). For mechanical work (a &quot;Mechanical work to arrange&quot; task: an oil change, brakes, tires, a tow and the like), CarmaCars does not do the work: book it with a trusted shop or recommend one, never promise the shop&#39;s price or time, and offer a rental while their car is in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take it</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Update</b> as you go: contacted, qualified, converted or closed with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>We mostly rent cars. Never say a car is for sale unless an Admin flagged it; the page shows it with its price when one is.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-send-an-offer-to-a-caller" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send an offer to a caller</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> beside a car in Find a car). No request needed: one screen, and the renter has the link.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Find the customer by name, phone or email, or press <b class="gd-ui">Add a new customer</b>: full legal name, mobile, email and date of birth. Already on file with that email or phone? Use them: never a second record.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car (by car code, plate or name; each says Free or Not free), the dates and the places.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The price: the rate sheet, a total or a rate per day, with the reason for a price you type. The deposit, discounts and fees are set by an Admin; customer service sets the Protection Plan price. Amounts I type, at the top of the price: Before tax, or After tax (HST included) to type what the renter pays, worked back to before tax for you. Or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out from it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">How the rental and the deposit are paid (card online, e-Transfer, cash, platform payout, the insurer; deposit by card hold, cash or e-Transfer), who found this client, the message, how long it is open (48 hours at most) and Email, Text or both.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Check the offer as the renter will see it on the right, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>An offer that is out is changed in place: <b class="gd-ui">More actions</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Edit the offer</b>, change it, then <b class="gd-ui">Save and send the update</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Save without telling the renter</b>. No need to withdraw it first.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-new-quote-for-a-caller" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">New quote for a caller</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b>. Choose the Car, the Pickup and Return (at least 2 hours from now).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose how the lead came in, then the caller&#39;s Full legal name, Email, Mobile and Date of birth.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Set the Licence class and Damage cover, and note places, extras and what they asked.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Create the request</b>. It opens like any request; send the offer from there.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/quotes/new</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1220/1260"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-05-new-quote-desktop-4e386b1c.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1220" height="1260"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.1%;top:15.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.1%;top:41.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.1%;top:72.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:63.9%;top:85.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-edit-a-booking-a-fee-or-the-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Edit a booking, a fee or the renter</h2><p class="gd-p">A booking that is confirmed, on trip or returned is edited directly; the renter&#39;s details are corrected from the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Edit the booking</b>: the return (extend or shorten), the car, the rental charge, each fee, the kilometres and the note. Tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter what changed</b>, or leave it off for a silent correction.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Money tab, Fees, <b class="gd-ui">Change or add a fee</b>: a fee forgotten (the young driver fee shows its price for the dates) or a charge of its own.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">What is open shows at once: <b class="gd-ui">Email a pay link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Text a pay link</b> for exactly that amount, or record cash or an e-Transfer (Rental charges, Collect (the amount) rental, <b class="gd-ui">Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Edit renter</b>: a wrong email, phone, name, licence or address. A new email is their sign-in at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The same renter twice? Under the renter, Possible duplicates: <b class="gd-ui">Merge into this record</b> moves everything of the other record here.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Each edit is recorded with your name, the time, the reason and the before and after.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-renter-messages-and-find-a-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Renter messages and Find a renter</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Renter messages</b> lists the latest messages with their booking. Open the booking to reply, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Find a renter</b>: search by name, email, phone or booking number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">To open a renter&#39;s private details, press <b class="gd-ui">Open with a reason</b>. The reason is kept in the access log.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/messages</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/260"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-06-messages-desktop-3441fa91.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="260"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:48.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-add-a-car-for-an-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a car for an owner</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add a car for an owner</b> (fleet: under Cars). You enter everything for the owner; they never fill in the application.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car: type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line with the year, make, model, trim and details (Edit if something is wrong). No VIN at hand: add it by its plate and choose the year, make and model. Tap the colour and check the class. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender&#39;s information if you have them. Photos are optional.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Terms and first invoice: what was agreed with the owner, to the cent. An Admin checks them before anything is sent.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner. The owner signs in the owner portal after one email (no paper signature).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the car and send to an Admin</b>. The application waits in the Admin&#39;s Applications, marked Entered by staff with your name. When the Admin approves, the owner gets one email to review and sign.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A fleet supplier (a corporation leasing its cars to CarmaCars): choose New owner, <b class="gd-ui">A corporation</b>, then Route <b class="gd-ui">Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars</b>. The default lease terms are set at once. For the car, enter the VIN, the plate and the ownership copy, choose its tier, <b class="gd-ui">Regular</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Troubled</b> (it is set once), and who it is registered to now (for a car moving in or bought, the name and address on the ownership and the date). Its ServiceOntario forms are filled in at once. No terms, no invoices and no paper signing: the supplier signs in the owner portal. The car goes on the lease when an Admin approves it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-owners-the-checklist-the-photos-and-the-forms-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners: the checklist, the photos and the forms (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> (customer service and fleet), then an owner. Search finds any owner by name, email, plate or VIN.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding checklist</b>: per car, each step done, to do (and who it waits on), blocked (and why) or not needed, with the one button to press.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Onboarding photos</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Replace</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> (with a reason) a wrong ownership permit, insurance slip or lender&#39;s letter, or <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or mark it <b class="gd-ui">Not accepted</b> (the owner reads why). A replaced photo is checked again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>: each ServiceOntario form the car needs, made by themselves, with its status, the date it was made and its download.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add cars from a list of VINs</b> for the owner: paste or upload, <b class="gd-ui">Preview</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-owner-forms-forms-c-and-d" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner forms (Forms C and D)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Owner forms</b>. Each row is a scan an owner uploaded before November 2026 (Forms C and D are signed on screen since then), with the witnesses and the status.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press Open to read the scan. Check every page is there and signed, with each witness&#39;s signature and name.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with What to fix (the owner reads this).</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/owner-forms</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/300"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-08-owner-forms-desktop-eceaee0b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="300"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:68.6%;top:36.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.7%;top:36.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-rental-agreements-are-signed-online-only" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rental agreements are signed online only</h2><p class="gd-p">A rental agreement, or a booking change, is signed by the renter in their portal or on the phone at the handover (the e-signature). A copy signed on paper is not accepted or recorded: send the renter the link again from the booking. One recorded before November 2026 stays readable under Signed on paper.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-signatures-on-the-spot-or-by-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Signatures on the spot, or by link</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter or an additional driver who has not signed yet.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>. Confirm the name and that you saw the original licence, then <b class="gd-ui">Hand the device to</b> the signer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Email the signing link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Text the signing link</b>: they sign on their own phone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The licence comes first: the renter uploads it from the request, and the offer cannot be accepted without it.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-the-booking-s-rental-agreements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The booking&#39;s rental agreements</h2><p class="gd-p">The Rental agreements card keeps both agreements in step with the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Any change after signing makes a new version by itself. A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage waits for the renter&#39;s signature: they get the link by email and text, and the card says &quot;Agreement v3 waiting for signature&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Resend the signing links</b>, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your device.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Fields still blank (a licence expiry, an insurer&#39;s policy number) are listed: type them and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the missing fields</b>. Check-in stops on a field a claim needs until it is filled or an Admin overrides.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Every signature: a code to the signer&#39;s phone or email, the key terms initialled, three consents, a drawn signature.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-check-renter-documents" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check renter documents</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter&#39;s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage, before the handover.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the task &quot;identity documents or coverage proof to review&quot;, or open the booking: <b class="gd-ui">Review</b> shows the documents of any booking being arranged or under way, with no task needed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every licence image, selfie and proof of coverage of the booking is on one screen, with what to check written once above them: the selfie matches, no alteration, the coverage is active to the return date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under each driver, the licence reader lists what it read (from the back&#39;s barcode, else the photo) and one line per check, Pass or Flag: photos sharp and whole, valid to the return, class accepted, old enough at pickup, name and date of birth match the driver, the Ontario number, front and back the same licence, and the main driver&#39;s Ontario licence. Look closely at each Flag.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">One is wrong? Open <b class="gd-ui">Reject this one</b> under it, type the reason the renter reads and press <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Then press <b class="gd-ui">Approve all</b>: everything still waiting is approved at once (the Protection Plan too). A document the system refuses is named with the reason; the rest are approved.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Each opening is logged. An Admin can do the same from Admin &gt; To do. Field staff review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from their My jobs: the booking history says the role, field.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Main driver: Ontario licence needed. When the main driver&#39;s licence is from elsewhere, they are moved to additional driver (their photos and checks stay; you still review them) and pickup is blocked until a driver with an Ontario licence is the main driver. The renter adds one from their booking. Only an Admin can undo the swap or let it go with a reason.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-which-credit-cards-include-rental-car-coverage" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Which credit cards include rental car coverage?</h2><p class="gd-p">Renters ask this often. <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Card coverage</b> (every function has it under Rentals or Bookings) is your quick reference: what to say, what to check, and the list.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Send the renter <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage</span>: each card&#39;s car value limit (MSRP), longest rental, key exclusions, its official guide and the day we last checked it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Ask which car they want. Most Canadian cards stop at a car priced $65,000 or $85,000, and many luxury models are priced higher. Give them the car&#39;s model year and trim so they can check.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Never tell a renter they are covered. Their card&#39;s issuer decides that: ask them to call the number on the back of their card about this car and these dates. CarmaCars does not decide claims.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Over the limit, an excluded make, a debit card or a longer rental than the card allows: offer OPCF 27 on their own auto policy or the CarmaCars Protection Plan.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A card marked Unverified came from a published summary, not the issuer&#39;s guide. Something wrong or out of date in the list? Tell an Admin: they correct it in Settings &gt; Card coverage.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-review-requests" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review requests</h2><p class="gd-p">Renters are asked for a review by email and text after each trip. <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Review requests</b> shows the ones on hold and the Google reviews to match.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On hold: the booking has a charge that is not settled or waived yet (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls) or an open incident. It leaves the list by itself once the charges are settled or waived.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The renter should be asked now anyway? Press <b class="gd-ui">Send anyway</b>. Should never be asked? Press <b class="gd-ui">Do not ask</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Google reviews: a possible match to a renter shows &quot;possible match&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b> if it is them, <b class="gd-ui">Not this renter</b> if not, or <b class="gd-ui">Match to a booking</b> with the booking number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A review that came another way (Turo, a text, a call, email): press <b class="gd-ui">Add a customer review</b> and type the customer&#39;s first name and last initial, the source, the date received, the rating and their words exactly as received, with a screenshot if you have one. It shows on the site with its source. Never write or change a review for a customer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">On a booking, the card Review requests has <b class="gd-ui">Ask for a review</b> (for example after a call that went well) and <b class="gd-ui">Mark reviewed</b> when the renter says they already left one.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Never offer anything for a review and never ask only happy renters: everyone gets the same message and the same Google link.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-change-to-a-confirmed-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A change to a confirmed booking</h2><p class="gd-p">On a booking&#39;s Changes tab you can propose new dates, times or another car, as an Admin does: set the change, write the reason, press <b class="gd-ui">Preview the price</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Send to the renter</b>. The renter has 48 hours to accept and sign the amendment. You also send a new signing link to an additional driver from the booking screen.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-late-return" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A late return</h2><p class="gd-p">A booking past its return time shows the late return panel. The renter can still extend in their booking while they have the car: the extension counts from the original return time, it is approved at once when the car is free, and paying it stops the late notices. Point them to <b class="gd-ui">Extend</b> first. Otherwise work it in order:</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Button</th><th scope="col">When</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Log a call</b></td><td>Record each call to the renter and what they said.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Send T13</b></td><td>The first late notice email.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Send T14 (final notice)</b></td><td>The final notice.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Request disable</b></td><td>Ask an Admin to approve disabling the car.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Open an incident</b></td><td>When the car is not coming back as planned.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-booked-when-the-renter-accepts-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Booked when the renter accepts (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter who approves the offer has booked the car, even before paying: the booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Booked, payment due</b> and holds the car everywhere. Collect the payment before the pickup (a <b class="gd-ui">Booked, payment due</b> To do comes 48 hours before). When you send an offer, the renter&#39;s view is right under <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-when-a-check-stops-the-pickup-or-the-return-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking page, <b class="gd-ui">What stops the pickup now</b> (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press <b class="gd-ui">Ask an Admin to override the pickup</b> (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking&#39;s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: <b class="gd-ui">Ask to record a past trip</b> with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-book-it-now-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Book it now (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">When you send an offer, tick <b class="gd-ui">Book it now (no renter approval)</b> when the renter has already agreed. The offer goes out and an Admin approves it in one tap: the booking then waits for payment, the car is held, and the renter gets one link to sign and pay. You can also have them sign and pay with you: open the booking, <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>, then take the card on this device. Already sent the offer? Ask the assistant: &quot;Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the customer agreed by phone&quot;. It shows a card; <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b> sends the same request to an Admin, who approves in one tap.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-change-protection-release-41" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change protection (release 41)</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking page, the <b class="gd-ui">Protection</b> card at the top has one button: <b class="gd-ui">Change protection</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Pick the option. Each shows the price difference, the deposit and what the renter provides. Credit card coverage needs the renter&#39;s card from the coverage list (one that covers this car) and their confirmation that they pay with it; OPCF 27 needs their confirmation that they upload their policy. If the rule says no, ask an Admin: only an Admin can override, with a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Write the reason (required; the renter reads it) and press <b class="gd-ui">Change protection</b>. The price changes at once: more to pay is a balance to collect on the Money tab, nothing is charged by itself. An offer is sent again; a confirmed booking gets one email and the amended agreement.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">When a renter asks to leave the Protection Plan, the card shows their proof: <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with a note. Sales changes requests and offers only.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-unanswered" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Unanswered</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">More customer service</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>: every customer text with no reply and every missed call not called back, oldest first. Reply or call back from the row; <b class="gd-ui">Mark answered</b> when it was answered another way. After 15 minutes the team is alerted. Check WhatsApp by hand each morning.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-the-request-as-sent-and-every-offer-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The request as sent and every offer (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a request or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Original request, as the renter sent it</b> shows the car, dates, places, coverage, add-ons, note and the price the renter saw, exactly as sent; staff changes never touch it. <b class="gd-ui">Offer history</b> lists every offer version, newest first: its status, who sent it and when, the car and dates, the message, how the total moved, and the price breakdown.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">To go back to an old version, press <b class="gd-ui">Revert to this offer</b> on it. Its car, dates, price, deposit, discount and fees load into the review as a new offer, highlighted.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the price, then send it in step 3. Nothing changes until you send.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The <b class="gd-ui">Coverage</b> line at the top says what the renter chose (own insurance OPCF 27, credit card, Protection Plan) and its proof: not sent yet, waiting for review, confirmed, or rejected with the reason.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-send-an-offer-in-three-steps-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send an offer in three steps (release 35)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Car and dates</b>: the renter, the dates, the car and where they pick it up and return it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Price</b>: filled in from the rate sheet with the checkout&#39;s fees and discounts. Change it only if you agreed another price.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Review and send</b>: what changed, the message and how the link goes.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Rarely used options (billing an insurer, how it is paid, the calendar) are under <b class="gd-ui">More options</b>. Send waits while the price is being worked out again after a date change, and one tap sends once.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-the-owner-s-own-trip-instant-bookings-and-book-it-now-releas" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The owner&#39;s own trip, instant bookings and Book it now (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Owner&#39;s own trip ($0)</b>: the owner booked their own car. There is nothing to price or send; get the car ready.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Instant (repeat renter)</b>: a Gold renter or above (Rewards) with a verified licence and nothing owing booked an available car at once and went straight to sign and pay. An Admin can take a renter&#39;s instant booking away from the booking page.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Any car, any time</b>: a Platinum renter&#39;s request on taken dates is a priority request. Fleet answers within 4 hours: confirm, offer an equivalent car or an upgrade, or decline with a reason. Never cancel or move another renter&#39;s booking for it.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Book it now</b> pressed by staff waits for an Admin&#39;s one-tap approval.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-secondary-contact-and-rideshare-documents-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Secondary contact and rideshare documents (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">The booking shows the renter&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Secondary contact</b> when they gave one: call them when the renter cannot be reached. Rideshare and delivery driving are welcome (rental agreement, section 10.3): never tell a renter it is not allowed. When a renter makes <b class="gd-ui">rideshare documents</b> (Uber, Lyft, DoorDash and others), you get an alert and the booking shows the letters they made.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-automatic-answers-release-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Automatic answers (release 36)</h2><p class="gd-p">Common questions by text, email, WhatsApp, Facebook and Instagram are answered by themselves from the FAQ. <b class="gd-ui">Renter messages</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Automatic answers</b> shows what was answered and what was left for a person. A question the FAQ does not answer stays for you: texts in Messages, emails and Meta messages as a To do, <b class="gd-ui">Answer</b> and the question. Once you text someone, no automatic answer goes to them for 2 hours.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-the-card-the-renter-picked-and-the-two-opcf-27-pages-release" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The card the renter picked, and the two OPCF 27 pages (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">On <b class="gd-ui">Review documents</b> for a booking:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Option 2</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Card picked</b> names the card the renter chose from the list (or typed when it was not listed), and <b class="gd-ui">Card check</b> says whether it covers this car: <em>Covers this car</em>, <em>Check it</em> (a card not on the list, a card whose coverage or value limit we do not know, or a car with no value on file) or <em>Does NOT cover this car</em> with the reason. <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> is refused while the card does not cover the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Option 1</b>: each page says what it is: <b class="gd-ui">pink slip</b> or <b class="gd-ui">OPCF 27 endorsement</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> is refused until both are in. <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b> needs the reason the renter sees.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A renter on OPCF 27 cannot pay until both pages are uploaded, so you see them before the booking is confirmed.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Uploading a renter&#39;s insurance yourself? In <b class="gd-ui">Upload a document</b>, choose <b class="gd-ui">Which page</b>: Pink slip or OPCF 27 endorsement page.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-calls-auto-replies-and-coverage-releases-35-and-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls, auto-replies and coverage (releases 35 and 36)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Calls from the Call button are recorded; the transcript, summary and Play recording are on the renter&#39;s, lead&#39;s and booking&#39;s history. Quo calls show their transcript and summary there too.</li><li>Automatic answers reply to common questions on every channel from our FAQ. A question they cannot answer becomes your To do: answer it yourself.</li><li>Card coverage: the renter picks their card and the page checks it against the car. Approve OPCF 27 only with both the pink slip and the endorsement page.</li><li>Rideshare and delivery work is allowed with the documents the renter makes on their booking; the secondary contact is on the booking.</li><li>The mid-trip message asks the renter how the trip is going; a problem reported becomes your To do.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-lead-you-handle-on-a-call-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A lead you handle on a call (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b>). Every call you handle adds the time again.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Sales see <b class="gd-ui">Being handled by</b> your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and <b class="gd-ui">Next lead</b> skips it.</li><li>Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.</li><li>When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can <b class="gd-ui">Release hold</b> earlier.</li><li>A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.</li><li>Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-the-person-behind-the-lead-release-40" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The person behind the lead (release 40)</h2><p class="gd-p">On <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">The person</b> on a card, or open the lead, to see the whole person: contact, account and licence verified (yes or no), bookings and balances, deposit, requests and offers, earlier leads, messages, calls and texts, notes, reviews, incidents, who has handled them, and the <b class="gd-ui">Signals</b> timeline of everything they did with us. Outside the renter&#39;s window you see it in full while you hold the lead on a call; otherwise you see the contact and account.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-check-in-and-check-out-on-one-screen-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Start the check-in (pickup)</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Start the check-out (return)</b> on the booking, and <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Check out</b> on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car&#39;s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Photos are one tap each: <b class="gd-ui">Take this photo</b> always shows the next angle.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example &quot;Next: Odometer&quot;) and takes you to it. When everything is in, press <b class="gd-ui">Hand over the keys</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Complete the return</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)</b> is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-late-return-is-a-choice-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A late return is a choice (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p">A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Late return</b> with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge as an extension</b>: every started day late at the booking&#39;s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge extra days</b>: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge the late return fee</b>: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge a custom amount</b>: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Waive it</b>: no charge, with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the late return charge</b>. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.</p><p class="gd-p">Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do <b class="gd-ui">Late return: choose the charge</b>. Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do <b class="gd-ui">Late return: approve the charge</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Approve as asked</b>, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'finance', 'chapter', 'chauffeur-requests', 'You keep the money right: payments, deposits and refunds, toll notices, processor payouts and Turo trips. There is no commission for Finance, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Money, Tolls and tickets, Turo trips, Find a renter, Calendar and Scorecard. **Money** opens with a row of tabs on top, as in Admin: **To handle** (payments, deposits, refunds), **By day** (with Today, 7 days, 30 days and 90 days), **All payments**, **Refunds**, **Deposits**, **Reconciliation** and **Unlinked Stripe** (the Stripe payments of the last 60 days that no booking knows, checked every night, with a best guess of the booking: an Admin links one from the booking''s Money tab; put one aside with the reason when it is not a booking''s payment). **Owner money** lists every owner invoice and owner statement. The old Payments by day and Reconciliation addresses open their tabs.

## Your queue

Finance tasks include failed owner debits, toll notices with no match, statements to review and refunds to issue.

![The lanes show what Finance handles: payments to fix, refunds waiting, tolls and tickets, deposits to settle and owner statements. Money today counts them below.](/guides/img/va-finance-01-queue-desktop-2f37513d.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 940; address: carmacars.ca/va; pins: 1 20.3 24.3")

## Payments by day

**Money**, the **By day** tab, is your day in one screen: every payment and refund, by method, with the cash drawer and the refunds to decide.

1. Choose From and To (today by default) and tick the methods you want (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer and others; none ticked shows all), then press **Show**.
2. Totals by method: received, refunded and net. Each day: the same by method, the cash expected in the drawer (cash received less cash given back) and the cash counted.
3. At the end of the day count the drawer and press **Record the count**. The difference shows "balanced", or "over" or "short" with the amount.
4. Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere (a cancellation, a booking, Finance), with the policy maths (paid, the tier, the percentage back, what is kept). Press **Approve** or **Decline** with the reason in the same row; above your limit it says an Admin approves. Approved: **Issue the refund**.
5. **Export CSV** gives the same rows for the bank or the bookkeeper: refunds as negative amounts, holds marked as not money in.

## Payments, deposits, refunds

**Money**, the **To handle** tab.

1. Failed payments: each with the purpose, amount and the bank''s reason.
2. Deposits to take before pickup, and deposits due back.
3. Refunds in progress. Press **Request the refund** and choose What it refunds (the rental charge, delivery or pickup, kilometres, add-ons or other charges); above your limit it waits for an Admin. Then **Issue the refund**.
4. Owner invoices that failed, and owner statements to prepare.

![](/guides/img/va-finance-02-money-desktop-486a8fbc.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 865; address: carmacars.ca/va/money; pins: 1 10.6 60.3, 2 72.4 21.6, 3 73.2 33.8, 4 11.0 45.9")

## A payment received another way

An owner or renter paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer.

1. Owner invoice: on **Payments, deposits, refunds**, find it under Owner invoices owing and press **Record payment**.
2. Renter: beside the failed payment, press **Paid another way**. Or open the booking''s Money tab: in Rental charges press Collect (the amount) rental, or in Security deposit Collect (the amount) deposit, choose **Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)** and how it was paid, then record it. Each panel collects its own part only.
3. Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance; type less for a partial payment.
4. Add the proof if you have it (a screenshot or a photo of the cheque), then press **Record payment**.

The invoice is marked paid or partly paid, the automatic debit stops for that amount and the owner gets a receipt. Above your single limit the payment needs an Admin. Recorded something wrong? Ask an Admin to void it; you cannot void a payment.

Each month''s payments recorded by hand are listed under Reconciliation, with the totals by method, to check against the bank.

## Cards, holds and deposits given back

On the booking''s Money tab.

1. After the return, **Charge the renter**: the Reason from the list (Other with its note), the Amount, and the line that says where the money comes from (the deposit hold while it is valid, else the card on file, else a pay link) before you press **Charge $...**. Before the return, Rental charges, **A later charge**, with the same reason list on the renter''s receipt. A deposit that cannot be held: Security deposit, **Charge the card on file as the deposit**.
2. A deposit hold, in the Security deposit panel: **Keep part (damage/fees)** with the amount and the reason from the list (the rest is released), or **Release**. **Hold expired**: nothing can be kept from it; press **Charge the card on file instead** (the amount and the reason are filled in). While the car is out, inside the toll window or while something is open, both wait for the settlement; an Admin may do it with the reason.
3. A deposit taken in cash or by e-Transfer is given back the same way: the task Give the deposit back the way it came; then press **Returned** with the reference or receipt number.

## Settle a deposit

The deposit is never given back by itself. Finance or an Admin settles it after the return: on the booking''s Money tab, under Deposit, press **Settle the deposit**. Issue the Check-out statement first.

1. The form shows the deposit, what is still available, the charges owed from the statement and what is taken from the deposit for them. What the deposit does not cover is charged to the card on file; with no card (or a card declined), the renter gets a pay link by email and text, and Finance has a task until it is paid.
2. Tolls and tickets can take up to 7 days to come in. Inside that window the whole rest of the deposit is filled in as the hold-back, until the window ends. To give it back sooner, tick Release now anyway: a toll that comes in later is charged to the card on file.
3. Something still open keeps the whole deposit: an incident, a claim, new damage at the return not priced, damage found later not billed, a toll or ticket on the car during the rental not matched or not charged, a card dispute, or charges not on a statement yet. The form lists them. Only an Admin can release part of it, with the reason; it is recorded.
4. Damage: an Admin keeps the whole deposit (**Keep the whole deposit (damage)**) or bills a damage charge up to the $2,500 deductible. Ask an Admin, with the photos.
5. Press **Settle**. The money moves at Stripe at once: the charges are collected and what is not owed is refunded or the hold released. A step Stripe refuses is tried again by itself, and Finance gets a task if it keeps failing.

> Good to know: A card hold lapses after about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise. While the car is out, or returned and not settled, the hold is collected in full a day and a half before it lapses: that keeps the money, and the settlement refunds what is not owed. A hold that lapses anyway is charged to the saved card, and Finance is told at once.

## Read a toll notice

1. Open **Tolls and tickets** and press **Read a notice**.
2. Choose the file: a PDF, a photo or a CSV, under 15 MB. Leave the reading profile to find it from the text.
3. Press **Read it**. Then check each line beside the notice and fix what was read wrong.
4. Press **Checked against the notice** on each line (**Leave out** to skip one), then **Save as checked** and **Confirm and import**.

![](/guides/img/va-finance-04-tolls-read-desktop-aa04a6b2.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 580; address: carmacars.ca/va/tolls/read; pins: 2 19.5 44.1, 3 4.1 64.8, 4 4.1 89.7")

> Tip: In the work queue, **Match again** retries the match after a fix, and **Dispute** marks a notice you think is wrong. Renters matched with high confidence are charged at import, with the notice and our fee.

![The work queue: Unmatched, Needs review, Matched not charged and Disputed, with each notice''s plate, date, amount and match.](/guides/img/va-finance-03-tolls-desktop-37b6f99c.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 540; address: carmacars.ca/va/tolls; pins: 1 23.6 12.2")

## Reconciliation and Turo trips

1. **Money**, the **Reconciliation** tab: press **Record a processor payout**, then **Match** it to the payments it contains. Anything still unmatched at the closing check goes to an Admin.
2. **Turo trips**: press **Add a trip** for one trip, or paste CSV rows and press **Import**.

![](/guides/img/va-finance-06-turo-desktop-b59cc7f9.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 540; address: carmacars.ca/va/turo; pins: 2 95.1 14.8")

## Deposits to release

A deposit is never released by itself. Each morning the system puts one task in your queue for every deposit due back: "Release the deposit for" the booking, with the amount and the day it is due (7 business days after the check-out, or after the return when no check-out was recorded). On the day, and every day after, you and the Admins also get a notice in the portal. Nothing is emailed.

1. Open the task: it opens the booking''s **Money** tab.
2. Settle the deposit: apply what is owed, hold back what an open item needs, release the rest.
3. The task closes by itself once nothing is left to give back.

### Card payments outside the site and the card reader
On a booking''s **Money** tab: **Record card payment** records a card taken in the Stripe Dashboard or on a reader (the last 4 digits always; a Stripe payment id, pi_..., checks it, and a deposit hold needs it). **Charge on reader** and **Hold deposit on reader** send the amount to the S700; the renter taps the card and the screen updates by itself. On a credit card coverage rental the whole rental is paid on the same card: another card is refused with the reason, and only an Admin can allow another one.

## Deposit holds and partner invoices (release 28)

Deposits stay as holds with Stripe and are never captured by itself. A job re-authorizes a hold by itself about 24 hours before it expires; when it cannot, you get the alert **Deposit hold not re-authorized**. A **The deposit hold expires soon** To do opens the booking: **Re-authorize the hold** places a new hold on the saved card and releases the old one; or **Keep part (damage/fees)** for only what is owed. A deposit not taken yet: in the Security deposit panel, **Hold on the card on file**. Under **Money** > **Partner invoices** you write invoices to body shops, tow trucks and storage yards for their kickback, send them, record the cheques and e-Transfers that come in, and export the CSV for the bookkeeper.

## Kickbacks and repairs

**Money** > **Kickbacks and repairs**: the kickbacks received on partner invoices (before HST) and the repair costs paid by CarmaCars for a period, by owner and by car, with the CSV. An invoice with no car counts nowhere until you choose it: open the invoice under **Partner invoices** and press **Choose the car**. Add a repair cost with **Add a repair cost**; Fleet adds them on the car''s page too.

### A debit deposit''s card fee
A deposit charged (not held) on a debit or prepaid card carries the non-refundable **Card processing fee for a debit deposit**, shown on its line in the history and on the receipt. The deposit refund returns the deposit only.

## Partners, the timesheet and ended trips

1. **More finance** > **Partners**: the rental partners (their pages, cars, rates, invoices) and the referral partners (kickbacks, payments), with every action an Admin has there.
2. **Hours** > **Timesheet**: the hours customer service, Fleet and Finance clocked. Add forgotten hours or void a wrong entry, with the reason.
3. **Close ended trips**: mark trips that ended and were never closed, and choose the deposit decision. An Admin presses Release; nothing is released by itself.


## Deposit review: double-check, tolls and tickets, then bill or release

Once Fleet signed every item of a returned booking you get a To do to double-check the deposit review. The deposit stays held until you signed every item too; only an Admin can release it earlier, with the reason.

1. Open **Money** > **Deposit reviews** and open the booking.
2. Press **Double-check** on each item: read Fleet''s finding and the photos, then **OK** or **Issue** with the amount to bill. Someone else double-checks an item you signed for Fleet.
3. **Highway tolls**: open the toll operator''s site from the review, search the plate for the rental dates, then double-check the item.
4. **Tickets**: open each place in the list (its official lookup link), search the plate, and press **None found** or **A ticket**. A ticket is logged in **Tolls and tickets** with the place and the plate and matched to the booking there. The Tickets item waits until every place is checked.
5. Then open **Money** on the booking: bill what is owed with the charge after the return, or release the deposit.

### The sweep, Monday, Wednesday and Friday
On each sweep day a To do **Deposit check sweep** lists every plate returned since the last sweep and every booking still inside the toll and ticket window. **Deposit reviews** > **This sweep** shows them by plate with every link, so you check them in one go. The days are in Program settings.

### Countdowns
**Money** > **Countdowns** (and the top of **To handle**, and each booking) shows the time left before each deposit hold expires (with when the automatic re-authorization runs, 24 hours before), before each deposit is due back to the renter, and before the next payment of a weekly, biweekly or monthly plan. Red is within 24 hours or late, amber within 48. Sort by any column. You get an alert at 48 and 24 hours, and the counts are in your morning digest.

### Do sales too
Under **My numbers** > **Do sales too**, press **I want to do sales too**: the Sales path is added to your academy (your Finance work is never held by it), and the Sales pages open once you pass it.


## The fuel line on the deposit review (release 35)

The fuel item shows **Suggested** with its working: the tank x the fuel missing x the pump price x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee. It is a line on the return charges, never charged by itself: sign the item, then bill it with the rest from the booking''s Money. A pump receipt still wins: enter it when the car was filled up.

## Statements and payroll (release 35)

- Statements cover the 8th to the 7th, paid on the 10th; amounts not yet collected from the renter are listed apart and paid on the statement after they come in.
- Payroll every two weeks: prepare the run with any bonus or deduction and its reason, then send it for approval. An Admin approves and records the payments.
- Email: Settings, Usage shows the real daily capacity of our sending services together; nothing to count by hand.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.', 'Finance', 'Payments, deposits and refunds, tolls and tickets, reconciliation and Turo trips.',
