## Start a handover in one tap (release 42)

On a pickup or a return that is not started yet, the job shows **Start the check-in now** (or **Start the check-out now**): one tap acknowledges the job, starts it and opens the one-screen handover. Not with the car yet? Press **Acknowledge** so the office knows you have the job, and start it later.',
  '<p class="gd-p">The portal has four tabs at the bottom of the screen: <b class="gd-ui">Today</b>, <b class="gd-ui">My shifts</b>, <b class="gd-ui">My pay</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Training</b> (and <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b> if you asked to do sales too). Today is where the work is.</p><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-your-shift-and-the-clock" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your shift and the clock</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">At the top of <b class="gd-ui">Today</b>: your shift, and <b class="gd-ui">Clock in</b>. Press it when you start. The phone shares where you are at that moment only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The bar shows how many of the day&#39;s must-dos are done.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When you finish, press <b class="gd-ui">Clock out</b>. Anything still open is listed: give a reason for each, then press <b class="gd-ui">Clock out with these reasons</b>. Fleet is told, so someone can cover them.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-one-list-in-order" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One list, in order</h2><p class="gd-p">The list is built for you from the bookings and the cars:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Your work</b>: every pickup and return of the day (deliveries and collections too) at its time, and onboarding prep Fleet gave you. Each car and time is one card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">When you have time</b>: cars to clean (not checked clean for a week), cars needing service or not roadworthy, and cars that need listing photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Switch to <b class="gd-ui">Tomorrow</b> to see what is planned so far.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-a-card" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A card</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The time, what it is (Pickup, Return, Delivery to the renter), the car and its plate, the renter and the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The steps of the card, ticked as they are done: the clean check, the add-ons in the car, the pickup photos and handover.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">One big button: the next thing to do. <b class="gd-ui">Start the pickup</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Start the return</b> opens the job screen, where the clean check and the add-ons come first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">More</b> has the place with <b class="gd-ui">Open in maps</b>, the call to the renter, and helping the renter.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The card&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Prepare: put each in the car, then tick</b> checklist lists every add-on to put in the car with its quantity. The office sees your ticks as you go.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The pickup cannot be finished until every add-on (a child seat, for example) is ticked as in the car. If the trip must go without it, ask an Admin to override on the job.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-clean-checks" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Clean checks</h2><p class="gd-p">Every car is checked clean before each pickup and after each return: choose <b class="gd-ui">Clean</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Needs cleaning</b>, take the photo and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the clean check</b>. On a cleaning card in spare time, press <b class="gd-ui">Check it clean</b> the same way.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-cars-needing-service-and-listing-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cars needing service, and listing photos</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a service card, press <b class="gd-ui">Give an update</b> (taken in, at the shop, waiting for parts, sorted) and <b class="gd-ui">Send the update to Fleet</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On a photo card, press <b class="gd-ui">Take the listing photos</b>: the photo shoot opens with the angles the listing is missing.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-onboarding-prep" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Onboarding prep</h2><p class="gd-p">Fleet gives you the prep of a car joining the fleet on a day you hold a shift. Press <b class="gd-ui">Open the prep</b>, then each item: upload what it needs (the safety certificate with its date) and press <b class="gd-ui">Mark it done</b>. When every item is done, the owner&#39;s onboarding checklist updates and Fleet is told.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-the-add-button" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Add button</h2><p class="gd-p">The red <b class="gd-ui">Add</b> button at the bottom right of Today:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Money spent</b>: gas, a wash, parts, parking. The amount, the car, the booking and a photo of the receipt, then <b class="gd-ui">Send to Finance</b>. Finance approves it and pays you back if you used your own money. No receipt yet: you get a To do until you add it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Service record</b>: what was done, where, the odometer, the cost and the invoice photo, then <b class="gd-ui">Record the service</b>. The car&#39;s maintenance resets, the expense is made on the car, and Fleet and Finance are told.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Photos of a car</b>: a photo and a note, saved on the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">A problem with a car</b>: damage, a warning light, a ticket or lost property (see Report, rentals, referrals and profile).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-help-a-renter-on-the-spot" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Help a renter on the spot</h2><p class="gd-p">From a card&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">More</b>, or with <b class="gd-ui">Find the booking</b> on Help a renter (by booking number, name or phone):</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Take a payment</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Take the deposit hold</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Show a QR for their phone</b> (they pay on their own phone), <b class="gd-ui">Text the link</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Email the link</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Use the card reader</b> when you have it. Never type a card number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The licence: check it in person on the pickup.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The agreement: <b class="gd-ui">They sign on my phone</b>, with their own finger.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Refunds stay with Finance and Admin.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-check-the-renter-s-licence" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check the renter&#39;s licence</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter&#39;s licence photos and selfie are checked before the handover. You can check them yourself, for a booking on one of your own jobs today or in the next 7 days. Everything you do is recorded with your name and &quot;field staff&quot;.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">My jobs shows <b class="gd-ui">Licences to check</b> when the licence front, back or selfie of a renter on one of your jobs waits for a decision. The same check is on the job itself, under <b class="gd-ui">Check the licence</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review the licence</b>. The images open with the name, date of birth and licence details on the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Look at each image and the licence reader&#39;s lines under each driver (Pass or Flag: valid to the return, class, age, name and date of birth, the Ontario number, front and back): no sign of alteration, and the selfie matches the licence photo. A photo you take that is blurry or cut off says so at once: take it again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">One is wrong? Open <b class="gd-ui">Reject this one</b> under it, type the reason the renter reads and press <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b>. The renter is told why and sends a new one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Then press <b class="gd-ui">Approve all</b>: everything still waiting is approved at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The renter&#39;s proof of coverage stays with the office. Meeting the renter at the handover? You can still check the original licence in person from the ready check (see A handover).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-documents-to-sign" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Documents to sign</h2><p class="gd-p">Your staff agreement, when CarmaCars sends it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">My jobs shows &quot;You have a document to sign&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Read and sign</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the key values at the top (your role, wage and start date), then press <b class="gd-ui">Read the PDF</b> and read it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Sign in a few steps: press <b class="gd-ui">Send the code</b> and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the key terms (confidentiality, the rules on money, keys and cars, ending the agreement), tick the two consents and draw your signature.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Sign</b>. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, stays on the same page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-move-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Move a car</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under Moving a car, press <b class="gd-ui">Start a move</b>. Choose the Car and Why (for example Reposition).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Fill in From and the Odometer (km), then press <b class="gd-ui">Start the move now</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When you arrive, press <b class="gd-ui">End the move</b>, fill in Now at and the odometer, then press <b class="gd-ui">End the move now</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-call-and-text-the-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Call and text the renter</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on a card opens the Quo app with the renter&#39;s number, so the call comes from the CarmaCars number; <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> opens a small window that sends from the CarmaCars number and keeps the text with the booking.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars now</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Map of your cars</b> are links at the bottom of Today.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-start-a-handover-in-one-tap-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Start a handover in one tap (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a pickup or a return that is not started yet, the job shows <b class="gd-ui">Start the check-in now</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Start the check-out now</b>): one tap acknowledges the job, starts it and opens the one-screen handover. Not with the car yet? Press <b class="gd-ui">Acknowledge</b> so the office knows you have the job, and start it later.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'a-handover', 'chapter', 'my-jobs', 'You give the renter the keys only after every check passes. The steps guide you one by one: press Next after each, Back to go back.

> Good to know: The job''s header shows how much of the rental walkthrough the renter has read, for example "Renter''s walkthrough: read 2 of 6 steps". Below 6, walk them through the rest at the car: what to bring, the walk-around, the road rules and the return.

> Watch out: Finish the handover in the app, to the last step. Until the pickup is recorded the renter''s messages and the office''s records are guesses: 30 minutes after the pickup time you get an alert and a text to record it, or to mark a no-show.

## Before you start: the ready check

The first step lists what must be done before the car can go: signed, paid, ID checked, deposit.

1. Each line should show a green tick: agreement signed, identity verified, coverage confirmed, additional drivers accepted, the booking holds the calendar, deposit taken.
2. A red line shows what you can do about it right under it (see the next part). Fix it, then press **Check again**.
3. All green? Press **Next**.
4. Coverage or the calendar not ready? Only the office fixes those: call CarmaCars. Still not ready? Press **Stop: do not release the car**.

![](/guides/img/field-21-handover-01-ready-phone-ecb54c56.jpg "phone; size: 390 410; pins: 1 91.0 63.4")

> Watch out: Never hand over keys if the ready check fails, the renter does not match the photo on file, or they do not have their original licence or the card on file. Stop and call us.

## Fix the ready check on the spot

Most red lines are fixed on your phone, without calling the office. Everything you do is recorded with your name.

1. Agreement not signed: press **Sign now on this device** and hand the phone to the renter. A copy signed on paper is not accepted.
2. Identity not verified: for each driver, press **Take** for the licence front, the back and the selfie. Hold the original licence: tick that the name matches, the photo is the person, it is valid past the return and it is class G2 or G. No expiry on file? Type the licence number and the expiry. Press **The licence checks out**.
3. Deposit not taken: press **Card hold: hand this phone to the renter**. They type their card in Stripe''s secure form; take the phone back and press **Back to the job**.
4. Paid by e-Transfer instead: open **Paid by e-Transfer**, type the reference number from their confirmation and press **Record the e-Transfer**.
5. Paid in cash: open **Paid in cash**, count the amount in front of the renter and press **I received**. Keep the cash apart from your own money and hand it to CarmaCars within 1 business day, as Finance directs: Finance gets a task to collect it from you.
6. Additional driver not accepted: press **Sign now on this device (additional driver)**.

> Tip: An expired licence, a face that does not match or a renter who will not sign: do not fix it. Press Stop and call us.

## The steps, one by one

:::phones
1. Car ready: fuel full or charged 80%, clean, extras in. **Yes** or **No**, with a note for Fleet. ![](/guides/img/field-22-handover-02-car-ready-phone-c118e08b.jpg "phone; size: 390 350")
2. Is this the renter? Compare the person with the name and photo on file. ![](/guides/img/field-23-handover-03-renter-phone-813b8ced.jpg "phone; size: 390 350")
3. Original licence: name, photo and expiry match. A photo of a licence is not enough. ![](/guides/img/field-24-handover-04-licence-phone-80a47254.jpg "phone; size: 390 350")
4. Card on File: you have seen the physical card with the same last four digits, in the renter''s name. ![](/guides/img/field-25-handover-05-card-phone-64652ced.jpg "phone; size: 390 350")
5. Odometer: type the reading in km. ![](/guides/img/field-26-handover-06-odometer-phone-34c4cbd7.jpg "phone; size: 390 350")
6. Fuel or charge: tap the level on the gauge, in eighths from E to F. ![](/guides/img/field-27-handover-07-fuel-phone-2df75f41.jpg "phone; size: 390 350")
:::

:::phones
7. Keys: how many keys and fobs you hand over. Use **+** and **−**. ![](/guides/img/field-28-handover-08-keys-phone-13bec781.jpg "phone; size: 390 350")
8. Photo set: 19 photos in order. Press **Take this photo** for the next one; every photo is also in the list below, with **Retake** if needed. ![](/guides/img/field-29-handover-09-photos-phone-767ecd4f.jpg "phone; size: 390 350")
9. Damage: tap the car diagram where it is, choose Where and Type, then **Add the damage**. ![](/guides/img/field-30-handover-10-damage-phone-a43b142f.jpg "phone; size: 390 350")
10. Tracker: it should say in place and reporting. **Check again** if not. The car has to go anyway? Open **The car has to go anyway?**, say why and press **Release without the tracker**: an Admin is told at once. ![](/guides/img/field-31-handover-11-tracker-phone-817976ce.jpg "phone; size: 390 350")
11. Renter reviews: the renter reads the summary of odometer, fuel, keys, photos and damage. ![](/guides/img/field-32-handover-12-summary-phone-b1787a2d.jpg "phone; size: 390 350")
12. Signatures: the renter signs, then you. **Use this signature** for each. ![](/guides/img/field-33-handover-13-signatures-phone-fac8ea8d.jpg "phone; size: 390 350")
:::

13. Press **Hand over the keys**. You see "Checked in. The rental has started." The renter gets the photo report by email and in their Documents.

> Tip: Photos wait on the phone without a connection and upload by themselves when it returns; the count shows what is still uploading. Each photo keeps its time, and the place when your phone allows location. No signal on a step? It says "Answers kept on this phone" and you can go on: press Try again, or they are sent when the signal returns.

## Sign now on this device

The renter (or an additional driver) has not signed the rental agreement yet? They sign on your phone.

1. On the job, press **Sign now on this device**. It shows who still has to sign and whether their licence is on file.
2. Check the person: the name matches their licence, and you saw the original licence. Tick both. No licence on file? Press **Photograph: Licence, front** (and the back and the selfie).
3. Press **Hand the device to** and their name. They read the agreements (CarmaCars'' and Blind Spot''s), tick the statements and sign with their name or their finger.
4. They hand the phone back: press **Back to the staff view**. The signature record says it was signed in person, collected by you, on your phone.

## The agreements at check-in

Both rental agreements follow the check-in.

1. Signing at pickup? Record the odometer and the fuel on the check-in first, then hand over the device: the agreement then shows the time, kilometres and fuel out, and the signed copy holds them.
2. The signer gets a code on their phone, initials the key terms, ticks the consents and draws their signature.
3. Already signed online? When you complete the check-in, the "as picked up" copy of both agreements is made with your readings and your countersignature, and emailed to the renter.
4. The check-in stops if the agreement is missing something a claim needs (a licence expiry, a VIN). Ask the office to fill it on the booking, or an Admin to override.

## The deposit on your phone

Deposit not taken yet? The ready check shows how to take it under the Deposit line. You never type a card number.

1. Press **Card hold: hand this phone to the renter**. They type their credit card in Stripe''s secure form and press the button with the amount.
2. They see "Hold placed": take the phone back and press **Back to the job**. The ready check shows the deposit taken.
3. A rental longer than the hold limit shows **Save the card on this phone (long rental)** instead: Finance charges the deposit to that card.
4. No credit card? When CarmaCars allows it, the renter pays the deposit by e-Transfer or in cash: record it under the Deposit line.

## Add-ons to put in the car

A booking may come with add-ons: a baby seat, a child or booster seat, flowers, an umbrella, a phone charger or a prepaid full tank.

1. Open the job. Under Put in the car you see each add-on, how many, and what to do (for example "Put the bouquet on the front passenger seat").
2. Put every item in the car before the handover. The Car ready step lists them again.
3. Prepaid fuel: the renter may return the car at any fuel level. Do not charge for fuel at the return.
4. A chauffeur on the booking: Fleet tells you who drives and when.

> Tip: An item missing? Write it in the note for Fleet on the Car ready step and call the office before the handover.

> Tip: The photo count shows "19 of 19 photos taken · all uploaded" when the set is complete. The first photo must show the plate. Open circles on the damage diagram were recorded before; add only what is new.

## On one screen (release 28)

On the booking page the check-in is one screen: the time, km, fuel, and many photos picked at once from the camera roll, with the suggested angles as a checklist. If the renter checked in themselves, add your photos to theirs. The full checklist is still there when you want it.

## When a check stops the handover (release 33)
When something stops the pickup or the return (the deposit, a signature, the licence, the car''s status) and the trip must go ahead, the job shows **What stops the pickup now** with each check. Press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin approves in one tap and the handover is recorded with the time you entered; add the photos and readings afterwards on the job, as with any handover recorded now.
