select app.guide_release_section('field', 'a-return', 'chapter', 'a-handover', 'The return mirrors the handover. You record the car as it comes back and compare it with the pickup.

## Take the car back

1. Car and keys received: confirm you have the car and its keys.
2. Odometer, then Fuel or charge, as at pickup.
3. Keys and extras: count what came back.
4. Cleanliness: inside and out.
5. Photo set: the same shots, in the same order, as at pickup.
6. Compare with pickup: for new damage, tap the diagram, fill in Where and What it is, press **Add the damage** and take a close-up photo.
7. Belongings: check the seats, the trunk, the glovebox and the door pockets.
8. Renter reviews and signs. Then you sign.
9. Press **Complete the return**. The check-out time is the moment you press it: a late return, the kilometres over the allowance and the fuel or charge used are charged from it automatically. The deposit is not given back at the return: Finance settles it once tolls and tickets have had time to come in (about 7 days), and new damage you mark keeps it held.
10. The closing copy of both rental agreements follows by itself: time and date in, kilometres in, driven and charged, fuel in, the hours late, the new damage, the return charges and the totals, countersigned with your name, emailed to the renter.

> Watch out: New damage needs a close-up photo and a clear note. Finance uses your photos and notes to bill the renter, so take your time.

> Tip: If the renter already pressed I''ve returned the car, the booking shows **The renter says the car is back** with their photos and readings. Check the car in as usual: that completes the trip and settles their report.

## On one screen (release 28)

The check-out is one screen too: the actual return time (late charges follow it), km, fuel, photos and a note. A renter who returned the car themselves with km, fuel and photos has already completed the trip; add photos if anything is missing.', 'A return', 'Odometer, fuel, keys, cleanliness, photos, new damage, belongings and signatures.',
  'The return mirrors the handover. You record the car as it comes back and compare it with the pickup.

## Take the car back

The return is one screen, like the handover.

1. **Odometer, fuel, keys and cleanliness**: the fuel starts at the level of the pickup (or the Tracker''s reading), the keys at what was handed over, the cleanliness at Standard. Check each against the car and change what differs. Type the odometer if it is not filled in.
2. **Photos**: the same shots, in the same order, as at pickup. One tap each.
3. **Damage, compared with pickup**: for new damage, tap the diagram, fill in Where and What it is, press **Add the damage** and take a close-up photo.
4. Belongings: check the seats, the trunk, the glovebox and the door pockets. Something left? Open **Belongings left in the car, or a note**.
5. **Review and sign**: the renter signs, then you. The renter is not there, or will not sign? Open **The renter is not here, or will not sign** and tick which.
6. Press **Complete the return**. The check-out time is the moment you press it: the kilometres over the allowance and the fuel or charge used are charged from it. The deposit is not given back at the return: Finance settles it once tolls and tickets have had time to come in (about 7 days), and new damage you mark keeps it held.
7. The closing copy of both rental agreements follows by itself: time and date in, kilometres in, driven and charged, fuel in, the hours late, the new damage, the return charges and the totals, countersigned with your name, emailed to the renter.

## A late return

A car that comes back late is not charged by itself. The return screen shows **Late return** with how late the car is and what each choice costs:

1. **Decide later** (already chosen): the office chooses on the booking. Nothing is charged until then.
2. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the daily rate.
3. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days.
4. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms.
5. **Charge a custom amount**, with what it is for, or **Waive it**, with the reason.

Your choice is saved when you complete the return, and the renter gets a message that says what was chosen. A custom amount above your limit, or a waiver, waits for an Admin.

> Watch out: New damage needs a close-up photo and a clear note. Finance uses your photos and notes to bill the renter, so take your time.

> Tip: If the renter already pressed I''ve returned the car, the booking shows **The renter says the car is back** with their photos and readings. Check the car in as usual: that completes the trip and settles their report.

## On one screen (release 28)

The form with photos already taken is still on the booking: the actual return time, km, fuel, photos and a note. A late return is then chosen on the booking. A renter who returned the car themselves with km, fuel and photos has already completed the trip; add photos if anything is missing.',
  '<p class="gd-p">The return mirrors the handover. You record the car as it comes back and compare it with the pickup.</p><section class="gd-task" id="a-return-take-the-car-back" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Take the car back</h2><p class="gd-p">The return is one screen, like the handover.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Odometer, fuel, keys and cleanliness</b>: the fuel starts at the level of the pickup (or the Tracker&#39;s reading), the keys at what was handed over, the cleanliness at Standard. Check each against the car and change what differs. Type the odometer if it is not filled in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Photos</b>: the same shots, in the same order, as at pickup. One tap each.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Damage, compared with pickup</b>: for new damage, tap the diagram, fill in Where and What it is, press <b class="gd-ui">Add the damage</b> and take a close-up photo.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Belongings: check the seats, the trunk, the glovebox and the door pockets. Something left? Open <b class="gd-ui">Belongings left in the car, or a note</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Review and sign</b>: the renter signs, then you. The renter is not there, or will not sign? Open <b class="gd-ui">The renter is not here, or will not sign</b> and tick which.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Complete the return</b>. The check-out time is the moment you press it: the kilometres over the allowance and the fuel or charge used are charged from it. The deposit is not given back at the return: Finance settles it once tolls and tickets have had time to come in (about 7 days), and new damage you mark keeps it held.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">The closing copy of both rental agreements follows by itself: time and date in, kilometres in, driven and charged, fuel in, the hours late, the new damage, the return charges and the totals, countersigned with your name, emailed to the renter.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-return-a-late-return" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A late return</h2><p class="gd-p">A car that comes back late is not charged by itself. The return screen shows <b class="gd-ui">Late return</b> with how late the car is and what each choice costs:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Decide later</b> (already chosen): the office chooses on the booking. Nothing is charged until then.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge as an extension</b>: every started day late at the daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge extra days</b>: you choose the days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge the late return fee</b>: the fee of the rental terms.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge a custom amount</b>, with what it is for, or <b class="gd-ui">Waive it</b>, with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Your choice is saved when you complete the return, and the renter gets a message that says what was chosen. A custom amount above your limit, or a waiver, waits for an Admin.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>New damage needs a close-up photo and a clear note. Finance uses your photos and notes to bill the renter, so take your time.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>If the renter already pressed I&#39;ve returned the car, the booking shows <b class="gd-ui">The renter says the car is back</b> with their photos and readings. Check the car in as usual: that completes the trip and settles their report.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-return-on-one-screen-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">On one screen (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">The form with photos already taken is still on the booking: the actual return time, km, fuel, photos and a note. A late return is then chosen on the booking. A renter who returned the car themselves with km, fuel and photos has already completed the trip; add photos if anything is missing.</p></section>');
-- GUIDES 2661 END
